    {
      "data": {
        "text": "*Time: October 28, 2026, 00:30 (~35 minutes)*"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1795702921424067800",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "Conducted an exhaustive architectural breakdown and design mapping of all 12 main menus from the canonical IBM SPSS Statistics Data Editor:\n1. **File:** Unified project container format `.stc` (StatCraft Project), native binary SPSS `.sav` and compressed `.zsav` codecs (L0 `statcraft_io`), keyboard shortcuts, and report exporting.\n2. **Edit:** Bidirectional command Undo/Redo stack on `CommandBus`, specialized clipboard transforms (\"Copy with Variable Names\" `Ctrl+Shift+C`), case and variable navigation (`Ctrl+G`, `Ctrl+J`), modular Preferences dialog (5 tabs: General, Data Grid, Fonts/Scale, Output, AI Bridge).\n3. **View:** Value labels toggle `1/A`, visual themes (Light SPSS Classic, Dark Pro, Auto System), runtime UI language selection, status bar sample flags.\n4. **Data:** Multi-level row/variable sorting, relational file merging (*Add Cases / Add Variables*), group split-file processing (*Split File On*), case filtering (*Select Cases*), sampling weights (*Weight Cases*), matrix restructuring (*Wide <-> Long*).\n5. **Transform:** 100% parity with SPSS: formula calculator `Compute Variable` with `IF` logic, `Recode` (into same / different variables), automatic string-to-code `ValueLabels` recoding, dummy 0/1 variable generation for regressions, time series shifting (`Shift Values / Lag`), Date & Time wizard, missing value imputation (*Replace Missing Values*).\n6. **Analyze:** Full statistical methodology catalog: descriptives, compare means (t-tests, ANOVA), General Linear Model (GLM/ANCOVA/MANOVA), correlations, multiple linear and logistic regressions, non-parametrics, factor analysis (PCA), clustering, scale reliability (Cronbach's $\\alpha$), survival analysis (Kaplan-Meier, Cox).\n7. **Direct Marketing:** Commercial decision-support extension (RFM analysis, profiling, A/B response testing).\n8. **Graphs:** L3 vector plotting engine `statcraft_charts` (`egui_plot`), visual Chart Builder, Gaussian histograms, Boxplots with outlier identification, scatterplot matrices, interactive Brushing & Linking, vector SVG export for scientific journals.\n9. **Utilities:** Quick variable inspector modal, variable sets for large-scale questionnaires (500+ items), embedded dataset research comments, study codebook generation.\n10. **Extensions:** Plugin ecosystem, declarative `Custom Dialog Builder`, Model Context Protocol (MCP) server hub for agentic AI orchestration, Python/R runtime bridge.\n11. **Window:** Emergency layout recovery (*Reset Layout*), split-screen presets, active document switching and protection of permanent workspaces.\n12. **Help:** Interactive *Statistics Coach*, open transparent mathematical specifications for L2 algorithms, sample dataset library (Fisher's Iris, clinical trial, survey)."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1795702921424071100",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "All 12 menus have been documented and synchronized across strategic roadmaps (`docs/ROADMAP.md` and `ROADMAP.en.md`)."
