    {
      "data": {
        "text": "Implemented one of the foundational predictive modeling frameworks in IBM SPSS Statistics — **Multiple Linear Regression** (`Analyze -> Regression -> Linear...`, engine command `stat.regression.linear` / syntax `REGRESSION /DEPENDENT=... /METHOD=ENTER ...`):"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1795702921424274100",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "1. **Mathematical Core L2 (`statcraft_algo::regression` & `regression_types`):**\n   - Ordinary Least Squares (OLS) and Weighted Least Squares (WLS) natively incorporating frequency weights (`row_weight`) and active filters (`active_row_indices`);\n   - Numerically stable normal equations matrix solver $(X^T W X)^{-1}$ utilizing Gauss-Jordan elimination with partial pivoting (`invert_matrix`) in 100% safe Rust without external C dependencies;\n   - Parameter vector estimation $\\mathbf{B} = (X^T W X)^{-1} X^T W \\mathbf{Y}$ and standard errors $SE(B_j) = s_e \\sqrt{c_{jj}}$;\n   - Standardized beta coefficients $\\beta_j = B_j \\frac{s_{X_j}}{s_Y}$;\n   - Student's $t$-statistic $t_j = B_j / SE(B_j)$ and two-tailed significance levels via the regularized incomplete beta function;\n   - Configurable confidence intervals for coefficients $B$ with customizable confidence level (default: 95%);\n   - Complete Analysis of Variance (ANOVA) table: sums of squares $SS_{reg}, SS_{resid}, SS_{total}$, degrees of freedom $df_{reg} = p, df_{resid} = N - p - 1, df_{total} = N - 1$, mean squares $MS$, $F$-test statistic, and asymptotic $p$-value;\n   - Model Summary: $R = \\sqrt{R^2}$, $R^2 = SS_{reg} / SS_{total}$, Adjusted $R^2_{adj} = 1 - \\frac{MS_{resid}}{MS_{total}}$, standard error of the estimate $s_e = \\sqrt{MS_{resid}}$;\n   - Collinearity diagnostics: Tolerance ($Tolerance_j = 1 / r^{jj}$) and Variance Inflation Factor ($VIF_j = 1 / Tolerance_j$) computed from the inverted predictor correlation matrix $R_{xx}^{-1}$;\n   - **Golden Oracle:** Test suite `regression_tests.rs` verifying regression coefficients, $t$-statistics, $R^2$, ANOVA $F$, Tolerance, and VIF against Python `scipy.stats` and `numpy.linalg.lstsq` benchmarks with $\\le 10^{-6}$ precision;\n   - **Never Crash** protection: graceful handling of singular matrices, multicollinearity, small samples ($N \\le p + 1$), zero predictor variance, and missing values in 100% safe Rust with zero panics."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1795702921424275900",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "2. **Command Bus & Syntax L5 (`statcraft_syntax::commands::regression_linear_cmd`):**\n   - Strongly-typed `LinearRegressionCommand` (`stat.regression.linear`) with parameter `specs()` for external AI agents;\n   - Listwise missing value deletion across all specified dependent and independent variables;\n   - Seamless synergy with active sample filtering (`Select Cases`) and frequency weighting (`Weight Cases`);\n   - Canonical IBM SPSS Statistics syntax generator:"
