    {
      "data": {
        "text": "Implemented the fundamental dimension reduction procedure of IBM SPSS Statistics — **Factor Analysis / Principal Component Analysis** (`Analyze -> Dimension Reduction -> Factor...`), complementing Reliability Analysis (Cronbach's Alpha) for comprehensive psychometric and multivariate validation:"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1795702921424377300",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "1. **Mathematical Engine L2 (`statcraft_algo::factor`, `factor_types`, `factor_tests`):**\n   - Listwise missing case deletion and observation weighting (`row_weight`) support;\n   - Computation of pairwise Pearson correlations and weighted correlation matrix $R$ ($p \\times p$);\n   - Factorability and sampling adequacy diagnostics:\n     * **Kaiser-Meyer-Olkin (KMO) Measure of Sampling Adequacy**: anti-image partial correlation calculation $a_{ij} = -s_{ij} / \\sqrt{s_{ii} s_{jj}}$ via numerical inversion of $S = R^{-1}$ and $\\text{KMO} = \\frac{\\sum_{i \\ne j} r_{ij}^2}{\\sum_{i \\ne j} r_{ij}^2 + \\sum_{i \\ne j} a_{ij}^2}$;\n     * **Bartlett's Test of Sphericity**: $\\chi^2 = -(n - 1 - (2p + 5)/6) \\ln |R|$ at $df = p(p - 1)/2$ with exact $p$-value from Chi-square survival function;\n   - Principal Component Analysis (**PCA**) Extraction:\n     * Spectral decomposition of real symmetric matrix $R$ via cyclic Jacobi rotations on 100% safe Rust without external linear algebra dependencies (`jacobi_eigen_symmetric`);\n     * Kaiser criterion ($\\lambda \\ge 1.0$) or fixed factor count extraction;\n     * Deterministic sign convention for positive dominant loadings;\n     * Factor loadings $l_{ik} = \\sqrt{\\lambda_k} \\cdot v_{ik}$;\n     * Communalities (*Communalities*): initial 1.000 for PCA, extraction $h_i^2 = \\sum_{k=1}^m l_{ik}^2$;\n     * Total Variance Explained (*Total Variance Explained*): initial eigenvalues, % of variance, cumulative %, and extraction sums of squared loadings;\n     * Component Matrix (*Component Matrix*);\n   - **Golden Oracle:** `factor_tests.rs` unit tests verified against Python `scipy.linalg.eigh` and `factor_analyzer` with precision $\\le 10^{-6}$;\n   - **Never Crash** protection against singular matrices, $n < 2$, zero-variance variables, and missing cases."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1795702921424379200",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
