      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1795702921424651900",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "Phase 58: Batch Syntax Engine (.sps) & Clean-Room Evidentiary Audit (Microplans S-01 — S-05)"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1795702921424652700",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "*Time: November 6, 2026, 18:55 (~45 minutes)*"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1795702921424653700",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "Implemented and audited according to the *IBM SPSS Statistics 24 Command Syntax Reference* a comprehensive batch command syntax parser and dispatcher (**Batch Syntax Engine & Dispatcher**) in `crates/statcraft_syntax`. The engine delivers raw script `.sps` batch execution capabilities via `CommandBus`, activates the desktop `Syntax Editor` toolbar with real-time log echoing and statistical table insertion in `Output Viewer`, and guarantees a 100% reversible round-trip cycle `GUI -> to_sps -> SyntaxParser -> CommandBus`:"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1795702921424654500",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "1. **Command Block Lexer & Tokenizer (`statcraft_syntax::syntax_parser::lexer`):**\n   * Engineered streaming `SyntaxLexer` splitting script text into `RawCommandBlock` items bounded by command-terminating periods `.`;\n   * Complete isolation of non-terminator periods: decimal fractions in floating-point numbers (`3.14`, `0.95`) and dots inside single (`'path.sav'`) and double (`\"model.v1\"`) quoted strings do not truncate commands;\n   * Full support for quote escaping via doubling (`''` and `\"\"`), with line and column tracking on unclosed string literals;\n   * Recognition of comments beginning with `*` or the keyword `COMMENT` spanning until the terminating period."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1795702921424656700",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "2. **Subcommand & Variable Range Parser (`statcraft_syntax::syntax_parser::parser`):**\n   * Detection of compound command names (`SORT CASES`, `SPLIT FILE`);\n   * Structured parsing of subcommands with leading slash `/` and positional clauses;\n   * Parenthesized parameter tokenization (`GROUPS=gender(1 2)`, `CI(0.95)`, `salary (D)`);\n   * Automatic expansion of variable ranges `VAR1 TO VAR5` matching sequential column order in active dataset `VariableDictionary`;\n   * Expansion of the keyword `ALL` into all active dataset variables."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1795702921424658400",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "3. **Modular Command Dispatcher & `CommandBus` Integration (`statcraft_syntax::syntax_parser::dispatcher`):**\n   * Modular command mappers `mappers/stats.rs` and `mappers/data.rs` strictly below 500 lines;\n   * Translation of parsed commands into strongly-typed `CommandBus::execute` calls with JSON parameters for 15+ procedures:\n     - `DESCRIPTIVES`, `FREQUENCIES`, `CROSSTABS`, `T-TEST` (Independent, Paired, One-Sample);\n     - `ONEWAY`, `CORRELATIONS`, `REGRESSION`, `RELIABILITY`, `FACTOR`, `MEANS`;\n     - `SORT CASES`, `WEIGHT`, `FILTER`, `SPLIT FILE`, `COMPUTE`, `GET`, `SAVE`, `EXECUTE`."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1795702921424660000",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "4. **Batch Runner & Desktop GUI Integration (`statcraft_app::syntax_runner`):**\n   * Added interactive action toolbar in `Syntax Editor`: `[ Run All ]`, `[ Run Selection ]`, `[ Clear ]`;\n   * When selection is empty, `[ Run Selection ]` executes the statement currently under the cursor;\n   * Output Viewer echoing: each executed command block is logged into the report tree prefixed with `> `;\n   * Automated unpacking of statistical calculation results into interactive pivot tables in Output Viewer;\n   * 100% zero-hardcode bilingual localization via Fluent semantic keys (`locales/en.ftl` and `locales/ru.ftl`)."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1795702921424661200",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "5. **Evidentiary Clean-Room Audit, Fixtures & Fuzzing (DoD):**\n   * Created canonical test fixtures in `fixtures/syntax/` (`batch_analysis.sps`, `data_transform.sps`, `malformed.sps`);\n   * Integration test harness `syntax_roundtrip_and_fuzz_tests.rs`:\n     - 100% reversible round-trip: `to_sps -> SyntaxParser -> CommandBus -> Output`;\n     - Fuzzing across 20+ corrupted syntax vectors validating the `Never Crash` invariant (0 panics, 100% safe `Err(SyntaxError)`);\n   * Authored official bilingual audit reports: [`docs/SPSS_SYNTAX_PARSER_AUDIT.md`](SPSS_SYNTAX_PARSER_AUDIT.md) (EN) and [`docs/SPSS_SYNTAX_PARSER_AUDIT_RU.md`](SPSS_SYNTAX_PARSER_AUDIT_RU.md) (RU);\n   * Updated hypotheses in Craft Anything MCP and Section 58 in `docs/CHECKLIST.md`;\n   * 100% pass on all quality gates: `cargo test --workspace -j 1` (112 syntax tests, 37 dialog invariants, 11 output invariants, 12 session lifecycle — 0 failures), `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- file-guard` (279 files OK), `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- layers`, `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- design-guard`."
