    {
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "Phase 62: StatCraft Bridge v2 — Autonomous Code Mode, Output Return & Dynamic Self-Documentation"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1795702921424696700",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "*Time: November 7, 2026, 12:00 (~50 minutes)*"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1795702921424697600",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "Delivered a comprehensive architectural modernization of the StatCraft Socket Bridge (Bridge v2), transforming the bridge interface into an **autonomous Code Mode (SPSS Syntax REPL)**. External AI agents (Claude, Antigravity, local LLMs) are now 100% self-sufficient without access to Rust source code or manual documentation:"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1795702921424698600",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "1. **Closing the Feedback Loop (Code Mode REPL Output Return):**\n   - Extended the batch syntax execution engine `syntax_runner::run_syntax_batch` with `SyntaxBatchOutcome { count: usize, output_text: String }`;\n   - Formatted all newly created procedures (SPSS Pivot Tables: ANOVA, Descriptives, Frequencies, T-Tests, Regression, Reliability) into clean monospace ASCII tables via `export_procedures_to_txt` and returned them directly in the text body of `statcraft_run_syntax`;\n   - External agents immediately receive exact sample sizes, means, standard errors, Student's $t$ and Fisher's $F$ statistics, exact $p$-values, and confidence intervals in their conversation context."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1795702921424699700",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "2. **Dynamic Self-Documentation & MCP Resources (Zero-Manual-Docs):**\n   - Implemented syntax commands `HELP.` (general catalog of analytical procedure categories) and `HELP <COMMAND>.` (canonical syntax template, subcommands, and usage examples, e.g. `HELP ONEWAY.`);\n   - Registered `HelpCommand` (`util.help`) in `CommandBus`, making syntax help accessible through both the parser and direct command execution;\n   - Added native MCP Resources support to the stdio bridge server (`statcraft.exe --mcp`):\n     - `resources/list`: exposes dynamic resource descriptor `statcraft://syntax-reference`;\n     - `resources/read`: dynamically compiles comprehensive syntax and procedure manuals via `statcraft_syntax::generate_full_syntax_reference()` directly from the binary;\n   - Intelligent Self-Correction: when encountering an unknown command or typo, the parser evaluates Levenshtein distance against known commands and suggests the closest valid procedure (`Did you mean 'ONEWAY'? Type 'HELP.' for available commands.`)."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1795702921424701300",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "3. **SPSS Variable Dictionary Syntax Mappers (`variables.rs`):**\n   - Implemented syntax mappers for dataset variable metadata management:\n     - `VARIABLE LEVEL varlist (SCALE | ORDINAL | NOMINAL).` -> `\"var.set_measure\"`;\n     - `VARIABLE LABELS var 'Label'.` -> `\"var.set_label\"`;\n     - `VALUE LABELS var code 'Label'.` -> `\"var.set_value_labels\"`;\n     - `MISSING VALUES var (val1, val2) | (low THRU high).` -> `\"var.set_missing_values\"`;\n   - Upgraded core commands `SetMeasureCommand`, `SetLabelCommand`, `VarSetValueLabelsCommand`, and `VarSetMissingValuesCommand` to accept variable names (`var_name`, `variables`, `assignments`) alongside column indices."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1795702921424703100",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "4. **Statistical Procedure Mapping Fixes:**\n   - `ONEWAY`: aligned parameter keys with canonical `OneWayAnovaCommand` schema (`dependent_vars`, top-level `descriptives`, `homogeneity`, `ci`);\n   - `RELIABILITY`: aligned variable list key with `variables`;\n   - `FACTOR`: aligned variable list key with `variables`;\n   - `MEANS`: lifted summary options (`cell_mean`, `cell_count`, `cell_stddev`, `anova`) to top-level command arguments."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1795702921424704600",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "5. **Quality Control & Definition of Done:**\n   - 100% test pass across the workspace via `cargo test --workspace -j 1` (0 failures, 0 regressions);\n   - New integration test suites: `syntax_bridge_v2_tests.rs` and `syntax_runner_and_output_tests.rs`;\n   - Static linters and architectural guards: `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- layers`, `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- file-guard` (294 files strictly within limits), `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- design-guard`, `cargo fmt --check`;\n   - Zero-warning compiler policy: `cargo clippy --workspace -j 1 -- -D warnings` (0 warnings);\n   - Refactored agent skill `.agents/skills/statcraft-assistant/SKILL.md` to guide agents toward autonomous Code Mode REPL workflows."
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1795702921424706400",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "---"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1795702921424707400",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "Phase 63: Self-Sufficient Introspective Bridge Engine & Universal Code Mode (Zero-Maintenance Introspective Bridge)"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1795702921424708100",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "*Time: November 7, 2026, 15:05 (~35 minutes)*"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1795702921424708900",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "Eliminated the architectural bottleneck of manual command registry maintenance and hardcoded procedure matchers in the socket bridge and output runner. Established the core principle of **\"Write Once — Works for All Future Functions\"**:\n1. **Live Runtime Introspection from Compiled Binary (Zero-Code Base Discovery):**\n   - Extended `CommandBus::list_specs()` with categories and syntax keywords, generating a dynamic live catalog of all engine commands registered in the core;\n   - Added `statcraft_list_commands` tool and `statcraft://commands` dynamic resource to `statcraft_bridge`: external agents receive the exact catalog of all available procedures and JSON parameter schemas on the fly, eliminating the need to read or guess the codebase;\n   - Added `CommandBus::find_by_syntax_keyword` for dynamic command resolution.\n2. **Universal Code Mode (`statcraft_execute_command` & `RUN COMMAND` Directive):**\n   - Added universal execution tool `statcraft_execute_command` to the MCP bridge and IPC protocol: agents can invoke any engine command by `command_id` and JSON arguments with automatic parameter validation;\n   - Added universal syntax directive in `SyntaxParser` and `SyntaxDispatcher`:\n     `RUN COMMAND \"<command_id>\" { <json_params> }.` (with `CALL \"<command_id>\" { ... }.` alias);\n   - Every newly registered `EngineCommand` becomes instantly executable both directly through MCP and inside batch `.sps` syntax scripts without requiring dedicated syntax mappers.\n3. **Universal Output Viewer Renderer (Zero-Match Fallback):**\n   - Replaced hardcoded `match parsed.name.as_str()` in `syntax_runner.rs` with an open two-tier rendering model;\n   - Introduced `OutputItemKind::GenericReport` and isolated rendering module `tables_generic.rs`: arbitrary command results are automatically formatted into SPSS-styled summary tables and key-value cards, recorded into the `OutputViewer` tree, and streamed to `output_text` in bridge responses;\n   - Synchronously updated Fluent localization catalogs `locales/en.ftl` and `locales/ru.ftl` with `output-generic-title` and `output-table`.\n4. **Quality Control & Definition of Done:**\n   - 100% test pass across the workspace via `cargo test --workspace -j 1` (0 failures, 0 regressions);\n   - Full pass of dialog and output viewer invariant suites: `cargo test -p statcraft_app --test dialog_invariants -j 1` and `output_viewer_invariants -j 1`;\n   - Architecture and code guard verifications: `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- layers`, `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- file-guard` (295 files strictly within size limits), `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- design-guard`, and `cargo fmt --check`;\n   - Strict compiler and linting gate: `cargo clippy --workspace -j 1 -- -D warnings` (0 warnings);\n   - Localization linter pass: `cargo test -p statcraft_i18n -j 1` (4/4 passed)."
      },
