<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="generator" content="CapsuleCraft Native"></head><body style="font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,sans-serif;max-width:720px;margin:32px auto;line-height:1.55;color:#23201c;background:#faf8f4;"><h1>📚 StatCraft / StatCraft — Development Chronicle</h1><p><em>[callout block — open in CapsuleCraft web for its canvas]</em></p><h1>StatCraft — Development Chronicle</h1><h3>Project Kickoff: Architectural Canon and Groundwork</h3><p>*Time: October 27, 2026, 16:40 (~45 minutes)*</p><p>Following an in-depth design interview in `/grill-me` mode and full alignment with the ArtCraft (`storytold`) ecosystem standards, the **StatCraft** project is officially launched — an open-source, high-performance statistical suite written in 100% pure Rust.</p><p>The master development regulation `AGENTS.md` is codified:<br>* Strict compilation limit of `jobs = 1` protecting workstation resources;<br>* **Never Crash** principle: complete prohibition of `unwrap()`, `expect()`, `panic!()`, and `unsafe`;<br>* Commands rather than handlers architecture (`CommandBus`, AI-agent schemas);<br>* Strict L0–L6 layering verified via `cargo xtask layers`;<br>* Zero string hardcoding in the UI (`locales/*.ftl`, instant runtime RU/EN switching);<br>* 100% mandatory test coverage per function with precision statistical oracles.</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 1: Workspace Scaffolding, L0/L1/L5 Core, and egui_dock UI</h3><p>*Time: October 27, 2026, 17:05 (~25 minutes)*</p><p>Successfully implemented and verified the initial architectural milestone:<br>1. **L0 Codecs (`statcraft_io`):** Streaming CSV/TSV parser with automatic delimiter detection (comma/semicolon/tab) and type inference (Numeric / Text / Date) with zero panics.<br>2. **L1 Data Engine (`statcraft_core`):** `DataSet` table structure and `VariableDictionary` (scales `Scale`, `Ordinal`, `Nominal`, `ValueLabels` maps, `MissingValues`). Transactional `DeltaBuffer` with cell-level Undo/Redo.<br>3. **Zero-Hardcode Localization (`statcraft_i18n`):** Thread-safe Fluent-based catalog engine (`en.ftl` and `ru.ftl`) supporting runtime language switching. `i18n_lint_test` enforces 0% hardcoded literals in UI code.<br>4. **L5 Command Bus (`statcraft_syntax`):** Strongly-typed `EngineCommand` bus with JSON schemas for AI agents (`data.import_csv`, `var.set_label`, `var.set_measure`, `data.cell_edit`) and Undo/Redo history.<br>5. **L6 Presentation Layer (`statcraft_app`):** Docking workspace on `egui_dock` featuring **Data View** (virtualized grid for 1M+ rows, value labels toggle), **Variable View** (metadata property grid), and **Output Viewer** (outline tree).<br>6. **Branding &amp; Vector Icon:** `assets/icon.svg` cleaned of Illustrator export artifacts and rendered natively via the `paint_app_icon` vector widget.<br>7. **Testing:** 38 out of 38 unit and integration tests passed cleanly (`cargo test --workspace -j 1`). `cargo clippy` and `cargo fmt` passed with zero warnings.</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 1.1: Comprehensive End-to-End Icon Integration</h3><p>*Time: October 27, 2026, 17:30 (~20 minutes)*</p><p>Completed end-to-end integration of the official vector brand icon `assets/icon.svg`:<br>1. **Geometry &amp; Centering:** Removed Adobe Illustrator markup bloat, centered the square glyph viewBox (`26 116 560 560`) with zero letterhead margins.<br>2. **Multi-resolution Asset Generator (`xtask icon`):** Implemented an automated pipeline based on `resvg` and `ico` generating multi-res PNGs (16, 32, 48, 64, 128, 256 px) and `assets/icon.ico`.<br>3. **PE `.exe` Resource Embedding:** Configured `winres` in `build.rs` to embed `icon.ico` directly into the `.rsrc` section of `statcraft_app.exe`. Windows Explorer and the Taskbar now render the official icon.<br>4. **Window &amp; Taskbar Integration:** Supplied the rasterized icon via `eframe::icon_data::from_png_bytes` into `ViewportBuilder::with_icon` for native titlebar and Taskbar presence.<br>5. **In-App Menu Bar Texture:** Replaced distorted line approximations with a pixel-perfect, crisp texture loaded into egui&#39;s context (`egui::TextureHandle`) displayed next to the StatCraft brand name.<br>6. **Verification:** All 37 tests green, Clippy and Fmt passed cleanly, and resource extraction verified via `System.Drawing.Icon.ExtractAssociatedIcon`.</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 1.2: Menu Layout Optimization and Dynamic Localization Fix</h3><p>*Time: October 27, 2026, 17:48 (~15 minutes)*</p><p>Refined top layout ergonomics and solved stale string caching in the localization system:<br>1. **Menu Bar De-duplication:** Removed duplicate icon and app title from `egui::menu::bar`. The menu items (`File`, `Edit`, `View`, `Data`, `Analyze`) now anchor directly to the top-left client area right below the native Windows titlebar, adhering to desktop UX canon (SPSS, Photoshop).<br>2. **Elimination of Stale Localized Strings:** Resolved the apparent &quot;hardcoded strings&quot; issue caused by early string materialization in application state (`String` inside `OutputEntry` and `status_message`). When switching languages, old messages lingered in the prior language. Refactored state into semantic types `StatusMessage` and `OutputPayload`, resolving translations dynamically against the active Fluent catalog on each frame.<br>3. **Refined Russian Catalog:** Cleaned up English parenthetical suffixes in `locales/ru.ftl` (`Представление данных`, `Представление переменных`, `Просмотр вывода`).<br>4. **Verification:** All 38 workspace tests passing with `-j 1`, Clippy and Fmt clean. Release binary built.</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 1.3: Table Grid Alignment Fix and Pinned Column Headers</h3><p>*Time: October 27, 2026, 18:00 (~15 minutes)*</p><p>Resolved table grid column-header misalignment and scrolling defects in both Data View and Variable View:<br>1. **Root Cause Analysis:** Using `ui.allocate_ui_with_layout` caused cells to shrink-wrap to the bounding box of their text contents (a cell displaying `&quot;1&quot;` took 10 px, a large float took 50 px, headers took 80 px, and `text_edit_singleline` expanded to 180+ px). Consequently, column horizontal positions drifted independently on every row. Furthermore, in Data View the headers were placed inside the virtualized `show_rows` callback, causing them to drift down when scrolling vertically.<br>2. **Deterministic Geometric Lock:** Every cell in Data View and Variable View now allocates exact width via `ui.allocate_exact_size` with zero item spacing (`item_spacing = (0, 0)`). Backgrounds, crisp borders, and clipped text rendering (`with_clip_rect`) guarantee mathematical sub-pixel alignment between header columns and all row cells across the entire dataset.<br>3. **Two-Axis Scrolling with Sticky Headers:** Implemented classic spreadsheet ergonomics (SPSS / Excel): an outer `ScrollArea::horizontal()` scrolls both the header row and table body synchronously along the X axis, while an inner `ScrollArea::vertical()` handles vertical virtualization. Column headers stay pinned at the top of the viewport and never scroll out of view.<br>4. **Constrained Interactive Widgets:** In Variable View, the `TextEdit` single-line widget and the `ComboBox` measure selector are strictly bounded within their cell rects via `allocate_new_ui` with `UiBuilder`, preventing adjacent columns from being displaced.<br>5. **Verification:** All 38 workspace tests passing with `-j 1`, `cargo clippy --workspace -j 1 -- -D warnings` 100% clean, `xtask layers` verified, and `cargo fmt` applied.</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 2: L2 Mathematical Engine statcraft_algo, Descriptives Dialog &amp; Pivot Tables</h3><p>*Time: October 27, 2026, 18:20 (~20 minutes)*</p><p>Established the second computational layer of the StatCraft architecture — the statistical procedure engine:<br>1. **L2 Mathematical Algorithms (`statcraft_algo`):**<br>   - Implemented `compute_descriptives`: valid/missing observations $N$, mean $\bar{x}$, standard error of mean $SE_{mean}$, unbiased sample variance $s^2$, sample standard deviation $s$, minimum, maximum, range, sum, unbiased Fisher-Pearson sample skewness $G_1$ (with $SE_{skew}$) and Fisher excess kurtosis $G_2$ (with $SE_{kurt}$).<br>   - Implemented categorical frequency distributions `compute_frequencies` (frequencies, total percent, valid percent, cumulative percent).<br>   - **Golden Oracle Testing:** Rigorous mathematical unit tests verified against Python `scipy.stats` reference values with precision $\le 10^{-6}$.<br>   - **Never Crash Principle:** Comprehensive edge-case handling for empty vectors, single-item samples, NaN sequences, and missing codes without panics.<br>2. **L5 Command Bus (`statcraft_syntax`):**<br>   - Implemented typed `DescriptivesCommand` (`stat.descriptives`) with JSON parameter specifications for AI agents.<br>   - Built SPSS syntax emitter generating `DESCRIPTIVES VARIABLES=... /STATISTICS=MEAN STDDEV MIN MAX.`.<br>3. **L6 Variable Picker Dialog and Pivot Table (`statcraft_app`):**<br>   - Implemented `Analyze &gt; Descriptive Statistics &gt; Descriptives...` modal conforming to SPSS desktop UX: source and target variable lists with vector measure badges, vector chevron transfer buttons `[ &gt; ]` and `[ &lt; ]`, statistics selection checkboxes, action buttons (`OK`, `Paste`, `Reset`, `Cancel`).<br>   - Integrated formatted SPSS-style Pivot Table inside Output Viewer with numerical formatting and authentic grid themes.<br>4. **DoD Compliance:**<br>   - Architecture verified with `cargo xtask layers`.<br>   - All 47 workspace tests passing (`cargo test --workspace -j 1`).<br>   - Localization linter `i18n_lint_test` verifies zero hardcoded strings across all new dialogs and menus.<br>   - `cargo clippy --workspace -j 1 -- -D warnings` and `cargo fmt` 100% clean.</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 2.1: Dialog Layout and Pivot Table Row Alignment Fix</h3><p>*Time: October 27, 2026, 18:35 (~15 minutes)*</p><p>Fixed two critical UI layout defects discovered during visual testing:<br>1. **Compact Centered Variable Picker Dialog:**<br>   - Resolved window width runaway across the screen by constraining `Window` size ($500 \times 420$ px) and anchoring to viewport center (`Align2::CENTER_CENTER`).<br>   - Fixed variable source/target list dimensions ($196 \times 150$ px) so transfer buttons `[ &gt; ]` and `[ &lt; ]` stay centered between panels.<br>   - Resolved egui `ScrollArea ID 4DF5` collisions using distinct `id_salt` tokens.<br>   - Added instant double-click item transfer between variable lists.<br>2. **Vertical Row Flow in Output Viewer:**<br>   - Root cause of the endless horizontal line: `ScrollArea` inside the detail panel inherited `Direction::LeftToRight` from parent `ui.horizontal`. Table headers and all observation rows (`age`, `gender`, `education`) were rendered side-by-side on a single endless row.<br>   - Converted detail panel to strict vertical flow (`ui.vertical`). Each variable is now placed on its own row, stacked vertically under the table header.<br>   - Added standard SPSS `Valid N (listwise)` footer summary row.<br>3. **Verification:** All 47 workspace tests green (`cargo test --workspace -j 1`), Clippy and Fmt clean, release executable built.</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 2.2: Full Dock Height in Output Viewer &amp; Elimination of Slit Scrolling</h3><p>*Time: October 27, 2026, 18:45 (~15 minutes)*</p><p>Resolved layout height collapse causing the output viewer reports area to shrink to ~80 px:<br>1. **Defect Root Cause:** `ui.horizontal` was previously used to divide the left outline tree from the right pivot table viewing panel. In `egui`, horizontal rows shrink-wrap their cross-axis bounding box to the smallest child item (the collapsed single-item outline tree header, $\sim 60-80$ px). The inner `ScrollArea` of the report viewer was clamped to this slit, forcing the user to scroll vertically to see each table row.<br>2. **Explicit Tab Rectangle Splitting:** Replaced `ui.horizontal` with explicit geometric bounding box subdivision of the dock tab (`full_rect = ui.available_rect_before_wrap()`):<br>   - Left outline navigation panel receives `left_rect` with fixed 180 px width and 100% tab height (`full_rect.height()`);<br>   - Clean vertical separator stroke between panels;<br>   - Right detail panel receives `right_rect` claiming all remaining width and 100% tab height via `ui.allocate_new_ui(UiBuilder::new().max_rect(right_rect))`.<br>3. **Outcome:** Pivot tables and logs now render freely down the entire screen height as a continuous readable statistical document.<br>4. **Verification:** All 48 workspace tests green (`cargo test --workspace -j 1`), Clippy and Fmt clean, layers verified with `cargo xtask layers`, release binary compiled.</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 3: Frequency Analysis, Variable Metadata Dictionary (Value Labels / Missing Values), and SPSS Tables</h3><p>*Time: October 27, 2026, 19:30 (~25 minutes)*</p><p>Implemented the third core milestone of the StatCraft roadmap — the Frequencies procedure and the complete interactive variable metadata lifecycle:<br>1. **L2 Mathematical Engine (`statcraft_algo`):**<br>   - Extended the `compute_frequencies_detailed` procedure with comprehensive metadata integration (value labels, discrete missing values, range missing values).<br>   - Implemented percentiles and quartiles ($Q_1 = 25\%$, $Q_2 = 50\%$ Median, $Q_3 = 75\%$) conforming to the standard SPSS HAVERAGE definition (Weibull / Type 6: $r = p(n+1)$).<br>   - Deterministic numeric/lexical category sorting and calculation of frequency counts, total %, valid %, and cumulative %.<br>2. **L5 Command Bus (`statcraft_syntax`):**<br>   - Created typed `FrequenciesCommand` (`stat.frequencies`) with JSON parameter specs for AI agents and SPSS syntax generator `FREQUENCIES VARIABLES=... /STATISTICS=STDDEV MEAN MEDIAN /ORDER=ANALYSIS.`.<br>   - Created metadata mutation commands `VarSetValueLabelsCommand` (`var.set_value_labels`) and `VarSetMissingValuesCommand` (`var.set_missing_values`) with full Undo/Redo.<br>   - Registered all commands in `CommandBus::with_defaults()`.<br>3. **L6 Interactive Dialogs &amp; Presentation (`statcraft_app`):**<br>   - **Frequencies Dialog (`FrequenciesDialog`):** Centered modal ($500 \times 420$ px) with source/target variable lists, vector transfer arrows `[ &gt; ]` and `[ &lt; ]`, instant double-click item transfer, &quot;Display frequency tables&quot; toggle, and action buttons (`OK`, `Paste`, `Reset`, `Cancel`).<br>   - **Value Labels Dialog (`ValueLabelsDialog`):** Modal for adding, updating, and removing `Code -&gt; Label` mappings with scrollable list and selection.<br>   - **Missing Values Dialog (`MissingValuesDialog`):** Modal supporting &quot;No missing values&quot;, &quot;Discrete missing values&quot; (up to 3 values), and &quot;Range plus optional discrete value&quot;.<br>   - **Variable View Integration:** Added authentic SPSS-style `[...]` button inside the &quot;Values&quot; and &quot;Missing&quot; cells, opening the metadata dialogs.<br>   - **Data View Integration:** Connected `1/A` toggle button on the toolbar for instant switching between raw codes and value labels.<br>   - **Output Viewer:** Rendering genuine SPSS frequency tables displaying `Value/Label`, `Frequency`, `Percent`, `Valid Percent`, `Cumulative Percent`, summary rows (`Total Valid`, `System Missing`, `Total`), and percentiles block.<br>4. **Verification &amp; Definition of Done:**<br>   - Strict Resource Guard (`-j 1` across all tasks).<br>   - 100% of workspace tests passing (`cargo test --workspace -j 1`).<br>   - Localization linter `i18n_lint_test` verifies zero hardcoded literals and 100% key parity between `en.ftl` and `ru.ftl`.<br>   - Architectural layer linter `cargo run --package xtask -j 1 -- layers` passed cleanly.<br>   - `cargo clippy --workspace -j 1 -- -D warnings` and `cargo fmt --check` clean.</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 4: Full Two-Way Reactive Data and Metadata Editor (Variable View &amp; Data View)</h3><p>*Time: October 27, 2026, 21:05 (~30 minutes)*</p><p>Implemented the fourth foundational milestone of StatCraft — a complete two-way reactive data and metadata editor, turning the application from a passive viewer into an interactive statistical spreadsheet:</p><p>1. **&quot;Blank State&quot; Out of the Box:**<br>   - Launching StatCraft without opening a file now initializes an interactive blank dataset (`DataSet::blank(40, 0)`).<br>   - The user is immediately greeted by an editable spreadsheet grid (40 cases) and can start entering data or defining variables right away without placeholder blocks.</p><p>2. **Full Canon of 9 SPSS Variable Types &amp; `VariableTypeDialog`:**<br>   - On layer L1 `statcraft_core`, the `DataType` enum was expanded to all 9 classical SPSS types: `Numeric`, `Comma`, `Dot`, `Scientific`, `Date`, `Dollar`, `CustomCurrency`, `String`, `RestrictedNumeric`.<br>   - Core formatting `get_cell_display` now formats numbers according to type parameters (comma/dot thousand groupings, decimal digits, currency symbols, and zero-padded integer widths).<br>   - Core parser `set_cell_parsed` cleanses currency and formatting symbols and normalizes user input into valid numerical or text values.<br>   - On L6 `statcraft_app`, built a centered modal dialog `VariableTypeDialog` ($480 \times 360$ px) featuring 9 radio buttons, dynamic width/decimals inputs, date format selectors (`dd-mmm-yyyy`, `yyyy-mm-dd` etc.), and custom currency selectors (`CCA`..`CCE`).</p><p>3. **Interactive `Variable View`:**<br>   - **Name:** In-place borderless `TextEdit` (`.frame(false)`) with identifier validation and uniqueness checks.<br>   - **Type:** Shows localized type name plus an authentic `[...]` button opening `VariableTypeDialog`.<br>   - **Width &amp; Decimals:** Compact vector spinners with `▲ / ▼` buttons (step 1); decimals are automatically disabled for string variables.<br>   - **Label:** In-place singleline text edit for the full human-readable variable label.<br>   - **Align &amp; Role:** Click to cycle through values (`Left` $\to$ `Right` $\to$ `Center`; `Input` $\to$ `Target` $\to$ `Both` $\to$ `None`).<br>   - **Measure:** Click to cycle through `Scale` $\to$ `Ordinal` $\to$ `Nominal` with crisp vector icons.<br>   - **New Variable Ghost Row (`*`):** An empty row is always available at the bottom; typing a name automatically registers the variable and appends a new column to `Data View`.<br>   - **Row Context Menu:** Right-clicking row numbers brings up &quot;Insert Variable&quot; and &quot;Clear / Delete Variable&quot;.</p><p>4. **Interactive `Data View`:**<br>   - **In-Place Cell Editing:** Double-clicking or pressing Enter focuses an inline singleline editor over the cell.<br>   - **Keyboard Navigation:** Pressing `Enter` commits the value and advances focus to the row below; pressing `Tab` advances to the next column (`Shift+Tab` to previous); pressing `Escape` cancels editing.<br>   - **Automatic Case Expansion:** Typing into any cell on the bottom row automatically expands `row_count` by 1.<br>   - **Case Context Menu:** Right-clicking case numbers brings up &quot;Insert Case&quot; and &quot;Delete Case&quot;.</p><p>5. **L5 Command Bus (`statcraft_syntax`):**<br>   - Implemented and registered commands: `var.rename`, `var.set_type`, `var.set_decimals`, `var.set_width`, `var.set_align`, `var.add`, `var.delete`, `data.add_row`, `data.delete_row`.</p><p>6. **Verification &amp; Definition of Done:**<br>   - Strict Resource Guard: Compilation and testing strictly executed with `-j 1`.<br>   - Test suite expanded to 63 unit and integration tests: 100% passing (`cargo test --workspace -j 1`).<br>   - `cargo clippy --workspace -j 1 -- -D warnings` — 100% clean, 0 warnings.<br>   - `cargo fmt --check` — 100% clean formatting.<br>   - Architectural layering verified with `cargo xtask layers`.<br>   - Localization linter `i18n_lint_test` verifies 0 hardcoded Cyrillic strings and 100% key parity between `ru.ftl` and `en.ftl`.</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 5: Output Viewer Architecture, Outline Tree &amp; TSV Export</h3><p>*Time: October 27, 2026, 22:30 (~20 minutes)*</p><p>Completed the fifth core milestone of the StatCraft roadmap — full modernization of the **Output Viewer** to achieve 100% functional parity with IBM SPSS Statistics Viewer:</p><p>1. **Hierarchical Document Data Model:**<br>   - Implemented a structured typed document model on L6 `statcraft_app`: `OutputProcedure`, `OutputNotes` (dataset &amp; sample metadata), `OutputItem`, and `OutputItemKind` (`DescriptivesTable`, `FrequencyTable`, `DatasetSummary`, `Warning`, `CustomText`), managed via `SelectedTarget`.<br>   - Results now accumulate in an infinite, continuous vertical document scroll — new analyses append below without clearing or replacing previous results.</p><p>2. **Outline Tree Pane &amp; Vector-First UI:**<br>   - The left outline pane includes a quick action toolbar: &quot;Clear All&quot; (`output-btn-clear-all`), &quot;Expand All&quot; (`output-btn-expand-all`), and &quot;Collapse All&quot; (`output-btn-collapse-all`).<br>   - Collapsible hierarchical tree: document root (`paint_output_root_icon`), procedure folders (`paint_output_folder_icon` + `paint_vector_arrow`), syntax log (`paint_output_log_icon`), analysis notes (`paint_output_notes_icon`), pivot tables (`paint_output_table_icon`), and warnings (`paint_output_warning_icon`).<br>   - All icons are 100% vector-rendered using `ui.painter()`, preventing &quot;tofu&quot; glyph rendering artifacts.</p><p>3. **Synchronized Navigation &amp; Focus Indicator:**<br>   - Clicking any item in the outline tree smoothly scrolls the canvas directly to that element (`ui.scroll_to_rect`) and highlights it with an accent focus outline (`Tokens::ACCENT`).<br>   - Clicking an item directly on the canvas synchronizes the selection back to the outline tree.<br>   - Fast item deletion via `Delete` key and context menus.</p><p>4. **TSV Export (Excel / Google Sheets Compatibility):**<br>   - Implemented tab-separated values (TSV) serialization for descriptives, frequencies, notes, and dataset summaries.<br>   - Table context menus allow one-click copying directly to the system clipboard for immediate pasting into spreadsheets with column integrity preserved.</p><p>5. **Syntax Logging &amp; Analysis Metadata:**<br>   - The &quot;Paste&quot; button in `Descriptives` and `Frequencies` dialogs appends genuine SPSS syntax to the syntax log.<br>   - Analyses automatically record an authentic SPSS-style `Notes` block detailing dataset name, case count, variable count, and UTC timestamp.</p><p>6. **Verification &amp; Definition of Done:**<br>   - Strict Resource Guard: compilation and checks run strictly with `-j 1`.<br>   - 100% workspace tests passing (`cargo test --workspace -j 1`).<br>   - `cargo clippy --workspace -j 1 -- -D warnings` and `cargo fmt --check` clean.<br>   - Architectural layering verified with `cargo run --package xtask -j 1 -- layers`.<br>   - Localization linter `i18n_lint_test` verifies zero hardcoded Cyrillic strings and complete key parity.</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 5.1: Elimination of Layout Overflows in i18n (Layout Shield)</h3><p>*Time: October 27, 2026, 23:20 (~25 minutes)*</p><p>Resolved layout overflow and column collision issues when switching to languages with longer word lengths (Russian, German, etc.):<br>1. **Dynamic Column Width Measurement in Pivot Tables (`output_view.rs`):**<br>   - Replaced static column widths with dynamic measurement via `painter.layout_no_wrap` considering font and cell padding (`max(base_min_w, measured_text_w + padding)`). This handles compound multi-tier headers (&quot;Valid Percent&quot;, &quot;Cumulative Percent&quot;) without truncation.<br>   - Tables wrapped in `ScrollArea::horizontal()`, enabling smooth scrolling across multi-column tables.<br>   - Each cell strictly clips its rendering area (`with_clip_rect`), preventing text spillover across column borders.<br>2. **Compact Vector Outline Toolbar:**<br>   - Replaced overflowing text buttons (&quot;Clear All&quot;, &quot;Expand All&quot;, &quot;Collapse All&quot;) with compact vector icon buttons ($24 \times 22$ px) equipped with hover tooltips:<br>     - `paint_icon_trash` — trash can for clearing all entries;<br>     - `paint_icon_expand_all` — expand outline tree;<br>     - `paint_icon_collapse_all` — collapse outline tree.<br>   - Enforced hard clipping (`ui.set_clip_rect`) on both outline and canvas panels, eliminating cross-separator spillover.<br>3. **Auto-Adjusting Header Widths in Variable View (`variable_view.rs`):**<br>   - Table headers (`Decimals`, `Missing`, `Values`, etc.) automatically adapt to localized text length without truncation.<br>4. **Verification &amp; Release:**<br>   - 65 workspace tests passing (`cargo test --workspace -j 1`).<br>   - `cargo clippy --workspace -j 1 -- -D warnings` — 0 errors, 0 warnings.<br>   - `cargo test -p statcraft_i18n --test i18n_lint_test -j 1` — 0 raw Cyrillic strings in app source.<br>   - Built production release binary `target\release\statcraft_app.exe` (6,470,144 bytes).</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 5.2: Complete Main Menu Architectural Canon &amp; 100% IBM SPSS Statistics Parity</h3><p>*Time: October 28, 2026, 00:30 (~35 minutes)*</p><p>Conducted an exhaustive architectural breakdown and design mapping of all 12 main menus from the canonical IBM SPSS Statistics Data Editor:<br>1. **File:** Unified project container format `.stc` (StatCraft Project), native binary SPSS `.sav` and compressed `.zsav` codecs (L0 `statcraft_io`), keyboard shortcuts, and report exporting.<br>2. **Edit:** Bidirectional command Undo/Redo stack on `CommandBus`, specialized clipboard transforms (&quot;Copy with Variable Names&quot; `Ctrl+Shift+C`), case and variable navigation (`Ctrl+G`, `Ctrl+J`), modular Preferences dialog (5 tabs: General, Data Grid, Fonts/Scale, Output, AI Bridge).<br>3. **View:** Value labels toggle `1/A`, visual themes (Light SPSS Classic, Dark Pro, Auto System), runtime UI language selection, status bar sample flags.<br>4. **Data:** Multi-level row/variable sorting, relational file merging (*Add Cases / Add Variables*), group split-file processing (*Split File On*), case filtering (*Select Cases*), sampling weights (*Weight Cases*), matrix restructuring (*Wide &lt;-&gt; Long*).<br>5. **Transform:** 100% parity with SPSS: formula calculator `Compute Variable` with `IF` logic, `Recode` (into same / different variables), automatic string-to-code `ValueLabels` recoding, dummy 0/1 variable generation for regressions, time series shifting (`Shift Values / Lag`), Date &amp; Time wizard, missing value imputation (*Replace Missing Values*).<br>6. **Analyze:** Full statistical methodology catalog: descriptives, compare means (t-tests, ANOVA), General Linear Model (GLM/ANCOVA/MANOVA), correlations, multiple linear and logistic regressions, non-parametrics, factor analysis (PCA), clustering, scale reliability (Cronbach&#39;s $\alpha$), survival analysis (Kaplan-Meier, Cox).<br>7. **Direct Marketing:** Commercial decision-support extension (RFM analysis, profiling, A/B response testing).<br>8. **Graphs:** L3 vector plotting engine `statcraft_charts` (`egui_plot`), visual Chart Builder, Gaussian histograms, Boxplots with outlier identification, scatterplot matrices, interactive Brushing &amp; Linking, vector SVG export for scientific journals.<br>9. **Utilities:** Quick variable inspector modal, variable sets for large-scale questionnaires (500+ items), embedded dataset research comments, study codebook generation.<br>10. **Extensions:** Plugin ecosystem, declarative `Custom Dialog Builder`, Model Context Protocol (MCP) server hub for agentic AI orchestration, Python/R runtime bridge.<br>11. **Window:** Emergency layout recovery (*Reset Layout*), split-screen presets, active document switching and protection of permanent workspaces.<br>12. **Help:** Interactive *Statistics Coach*, open transparent mathematical specifications for L2 algorithms, sample dataset library (Fisher&#39;s Iris, clinical trial, survey).</p><p>All 12 menus have been documented and synchronized across strategic roadmaps (`docs/ROADMAP.md` and `ROADMAP.en.md`).</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 5.3: Canonical 12-Menu Architecture with Readiness Badges (IBM SPSS 12-Menu System)</h3><p>*Time: October 28, 2026, 01:05 (~35 minutes)*</p><p>Integrated the complete canonical ensemble of all 12 menus from desktop IBM SPSS Statistics into the main StatCraft application window (`crates/statcraft_app`):<br>1. **File**<br>2. **Edit**<br>3. **View**<br>4. **Data**<br>5. **Transform**<br>6. **Analyze**<br>7. **Direct Marketing**<br>8. **Graphs**<br>9. **Utilities**<br>10. **Extensions**<br>11. **Window**<br>12. **Help**</p><p>Key engineering achievements of this phase:<br>1. **Reusable Menu Item Widget `menu_item.rs` (`MenuItemStatus`):**<br>   - Implemented strictly typed menu item status handling:<br>     - `Ready { shortcut }` — active interactive item with click response and aligned shortcut labels (`Ctrl+O`, `Ctrl+Z`, `Alt+F4`, `Ctrl+1..3`);<br>     - `ContextDisabled { reason }` — contextual disabling (e.g. analytical procedures when no active dataset is loaded) with informative tooltip *«Requires an open dataset»*;<br>     - `InDev` — disabled against empty clicks, rendering an aligned semantic badge `[dev]` and tooltip *«In development (planned in Roadmap)»*.<br>2. **Localization Catalogs `locales/en.ftl` &amp; `locales/ru.ftl`:**<br>   - Added over 170 new semantic translation keys covering all menu items, flyout submenus (compare means, regression, dimension reduction, file merging, legacy graphs, etc.).<br>   - `crates/statcraft_i18n/tests/i18n_lint_test.rs` verified 100% key parity between English and Russian catalogs with zero raw Cyrillic characters in the application source code.<br>3. **Action Bindings in `app.rs`:**<br>   - **File:** `Open CSV...` (`Ctrl+O`), `Exit` (`Alt+F4`);<br>   - **Edit:** `Undo` (`Ctrl+Z`), `Redo` (`Ctrl+Y`);<br>   - **View:** `Value Labels` (toggle between numeric codes and text labels), `Language` (runtime RU/EN switcher);<br>   - **Analyze:** `Descriptives...` and `Frequencies...` (opening modal analysis dialogs when dataset is present);<br>   - **Window:** `Reset Workspace Layout` (recovering default docking state: Data View on left, Output Viewer on right), `Analytical Split View`, quick tab focusing for `Data View` (`Ctrl+1`), `Variable View` (`Ctrl+2`), `Output Viewer` (`Ctrl+3`).<br>4. **Verification &amp; Artifacts:**<br>   - 100% of workspace tests passing (`cargo test --workspace -j 1`).<br>   - Architecture layer integrity verified (`cargo xtask layers`).<br>   - `cargo clippy --workspace -j 1 -- -D warnings` — clean (0 errors, 0 warnings).<br>   - Produced optimized release binary `target/release/statcraft_app.exe`.</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 5.4: Monolithic Custom Titlebar in PhotoCraft / Photoshop Style</h3><p>*Time: October 28, 2026, 01:30 (~25 minutes)*</p><p>Transformed the application&#39;s top bar into a unified, modern Client-Side Decoration (CSD) titlebar modeled on the PhotoCraft architectural standard:<br>1. **Borderless Window Mode (`main.rs`):**<br>   - Configured `ViewportBuilder::default().with_decorations(false).with_resizable(true)` to eliminate the heavy native OS frame.<br>2. **Unified Monolithic 34 px Bar (`titlebar.rs` &amp; `app.rs`):**<br>   - **Left:** Crisp, enlarged StatCraft icon ($24 \times 24$ px) **with no redundant application name text alongside**, immediately preceding all 12 canonical menus;<br>   - **Center:** Adaptive centering of the active document name (`Untitled-1 •` or the imported dataset name) using `title_x` with collision avoidance and graceful truncation/hiding on narrow viewports;<br>   - **Right:** Native-sized Windows caption button group (width $46 \times 3 = 138$ px):<br>     - 100% vector-rendered glyphs (`line_segment`, `rect_stroke`) for Minimize, Maximize/Restore, and Close;<br>     - Distinctive accent red hover background (`CAPTION_CLOSE_HOVER`) on Close, subtle theme hover on other controls;<br>     - Localized hover tooltips (`caption-minimize`, `caption-maximize`, `caption-restore`, `caption-close`).<br>3. **Frameless Window Interactivity:**<br>   - Entire free gap between menus and caption buttons supports dragging (`ViewportCommand::StartDrag`) and double-click maximize/restore toggle;<br>   - Invisible perimeter resize zones (`render_resize_zones`) with 4 px edges and 8 px corners with responsive mouse cursor icons, auto-suppressed when maximized.<br>4. **Verification &amp; DoD:**<br>   - 100% passing across all 65 workspace tests (`cargo test --workspace -j 1`).<br>   - `cargo clippy --workspace -j 1 -- -D warnings` — 0 warnings.<br>   - Built optimized production binary `target/release/statcraft_app.exe`.</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 5.5: Responsive Menu Overflow, Vertical Centering &amp; Window Drag Restoration</h3><p>*Time: October 28, 2026, 01:55 (~25 minutes)*</p><p>Addressed user feedback on top bar layout alignment and frameless window interactions:<br>1. **Geometric Vertical Centering:**<br>   - Switched from `ui.horizontal` (with implicit top `Align::Min`) to `ui.with_layout(Layout::left_to_right(Align::Center))`.<br>   - The $24 \times 24$ px icon and 13 pt menu buttons are now vertically centered within the 34 px bar with balanced 5 px and 7 px margins.<br>2. **Restored Dragging and Double-Click Maximize/Restore:**<br>   - Identified root cause: `egui::menu::bar` internally called `ui.set_min_width(ui.available_width())`, consuming all remaining horizontal width and collapsing `drag_rect` width to `0.0`.<br>   - Replaced expanding `menu::bar` with direct centered `ui.menu_button` calls, giving an accurate `menus_end_x` measurement.<br>   - The large `drag_rect` gap between menus and window caption buttons now reliably dispatches `ViewportCommand::StartDrag` on drag and `ViewportCommand::Maximized` on double click.<br>3. **Responsive Menu Overflow (`»`):**<br>   - Calculated font-rendered widths for each menu item via `ui.fonts().layout_no_wrap`.<br>   - If a menu item cannot fit before the right caption button group (`controls_start_x`), it and all subsequent menus gracefully collapse into a compact overflow menu button (`»` / `t!(&quot;menu-overflow&quot;)`) displaying them as cascading submenus.<br>   - Menus never overlap the window caption buttons regardless of window width.<br>4. **Quality &amp; Verification (DoD):**<br>   - 100% workspace tests passing (`cargo test --workspace -j 1`).<br>   - Localized via Fluent with zero raw Cyrillic strings in app code (`i18n_lint_test`).<br>   - Clean `clippy --workspace -j 1 -- -D warnings` (0 errors, 0 warnings).<br>   - Produced optimized release binary `target/release/statcraft_app.exe`.</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 5.6: Canonical Toolstrip with Vector SVG Icons (PhotoCraft Standard)</h3><p>*Time: October 28, 2026, 02:30 (~25 minutes)*</p><p>Implemented a full-featured Toolbar / Toolstrip modeled on IBM SPSS Statistics using PhotoCraft&#39;s vector SVG icon architecture:<br>1. **Vector SVG Icon Infrastructure (`egui_extras` + `icons.rs`):**<br>   - Integrated official `egui_extras` with `&quot;svg&quot;` feature enabled;<br>   - Compile-time embedded monochromatic Lucide SVG icon catalog via `include_bytes!` in `icon_data.rs` (zero external asset paths, zero network dependency);<br>   - Built `SvgIconSet` preprocessor replacing `currentColor` with `#ffffff` and normalizing stroke widths for crisp DPI-scaled hardware rasterization;<br>   - `crate::icons::icon_image` enables instant runtime tinting to any design system token (`Tokens::TEXT_PRIMARY`, `Tokens::TEXT_MUTED`, `Tokens::ACCENT`, `Color32::WHITE`).<br>2. **Toolbar Component (`toolbar.rs`):**<br>   - Flexible placement: **Top Toolbar** (default beneath menu), **Left Toolbar**, and **Hide Toolbar** toggleable in `View -&gt; Toolbars`;<br>   - Full 16-button canonical SPSS set organized into 6 logical groups with vector separators:<br>     1. *File Operations:* `Open Data`, `Save Data`, `Print`;<br>     2. *History &amp; Recall:* `Recall Dialogs`, `Undo` (reactive to command history), `Redo`;<br>     3. *Navigation &amp; Search:* `Go to Case`, `Go to Variable`, `Variables Info`, `Find`;<br>     4. *Data Structure:* `Insert Case` (`data.add_row`), `Insert Variable` (`var.add`);<br>     5. *Data Preparation:* `Split File`, `Select Cases`, `Weight Cases`;<br>     6. *Display &amp; Analysis:* `Value Labels (1/A)` (interactive toggle state), quick-launch for `Descriptives` and `Frequencies`.<br>3. **Localization &amp; Interactivity:**<br>   - 100% of tooltips with keyboard shortcuts localized in `locales/en.ftl` and `locales/ru.ftl`;<br>   - Real action dispatch to `CommandBus` and analysis modal dialogs.<br>4. **Quality &amp; DoD:**<br>   - Localization linter `i18n_lint_test` — 2/2 passed (0% raw Cyrillic);<br>   - Workspace tests `cargo test --workspace -j 1` — 65/65 passed;<br>   - Architecture layer integrity `cargo xtask layers` — verified;<br>   - Linter `cargo clippy --workspace -j 1 -- -D warnings` — 0 warnings;<br>   - Produced clean release binary `target/release/statcraft_app.exe`.</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 6.1: One-Sample Student&#39;s T Test (Compare Means)</h3><p>*Time: October 28, 2026, 09:40 (~35 minutes)*</p><p>Implemented the foundational procedure of the **Compare Means** family — Student&#39;s One-Sample T-Test (`Analyze -&gt; Compare Means -&gt; One-Sample T Test...`):<br>1. **Mathematical Engine L2 (`statcraft_algo::ttest_onesample`):**<br>   - Built Student&#39;s t cumulative distribution function, 2-tailed $p$-value, and inverse quantile function (calculating critical $t_{\alpha/2, df}$ for confidence intervals) in 100% pure safe Rust without third-party dependencies;<br>   - Implemented regularized incomplete beta function $I_x(a, b)$ using modified Lentz continued fractions and Lanczos approximation for $\ln\Gamma(z)$;<br>   - Golden Oracle verification against Python SciPy (`scipy.stats.ttest_1samp`): t-statistic, $p$-value, degrees of freedom, and 95% difference CI match standard benchmarks to $10^{-8}$;<br>   - Full Never Crash guarantees for degenerate edge cases ($N &lt; 2$, zero sample variance, missing/NA values).<br>2. **Command Bus &amp; Syntax L5 (`statcraft_syntax::commands::ttest_onesample_cmd`):**<br>   - Typed `OneSampleTTestCommand` (`stat.ttest.onesample`) with parameter schema for AI agents;<br>   - Canonical SPSS syntax generator:</p><p><em>[code block — open in CapsuleCraft web for its canvas]</em></p><p>3. **User Interface L6 (`statcraft_app`):**<br>   - Dedicated modal dialog `OneSampleTTestDialog` ($500 \times 380$ px) with variable selection lists, vector scale icons, Test Value numeric input, and custom confidence level percentage;<br>   - Enabled `Analyze -&gt; Compare Means -&gt; One-Sample T Test...` menu action with reactive data availability checks;<br>   - Rendered dual SPSS Pivot Tables in the Output Viewer:<br>     1. **One-Sample Statistics:** Variable, N, Mean, Std. Deviation, Std. Error Mean;<br>     2. **One-Sample Test (Test Value = ...):** Variable, t, df, Sig. (2-tailed), Mean Difference, 95% Confidence Interval of the Difference (Lower, Upper);<br>   - Context menu TSV clipboard exporter and outline tree integration.<br>4. **Quality &amp; DoD:**<br>   - 100% workspace tests passing (`cargo test --workspace -j 1`);<br>   - Architecture layer rules verified (`cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- layers`);<br>   - Command parity tracked (`cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- parity`);<br>   - Localization linter `i18n_lint_test` — 2/2 passed (zero unlocalized strings);<br>   - `cargo clippy --workspace -j 1 -- -D warnings` — 0 errors, 0 warnings.<br>---</p><h3>Phase 6.2: Independent-Samples T Test (Compare Means)</h3><p>*Time: October 28, 2026, 10:20 (~40 minutes)*</p><p>Implemented the core statistical procedure for experimental research and A/B testing — **Independent-Samples T-Test** (Analyze -&gt; Compare Means -&gt; Independent-Samples T Test...):<br>1. **Mathematical Engine L2 (statcraft_algo::ttest_indep):**<br>   - Full implementation of Levene&#39;s Test for Equality of Variances (canonical SPSS $-test centered at the group mean center=\&#39;mean\&#39;);<br>   - Dual-row hypothesis testing calculated simultaneously (IBM SPSS Statistics canon):<br>     1. *Equal variances assumed* — classic Student\&#39;s t-test with pooled variance ^2$ and degrees of freedom  = N_1 + N_2 - 2$;<br>     2. *Equal variances not assumed* — Welch\&#39;s t-test with separate variances and Satterthwaite degrees of freedom {welch}$;<br>   - Descriptive group statistics (, \bar{x}, SD, SE$), exact mean difference $\Delta$, standard error of difference {diff}$, and confidence intervals;<br>   - **Golden Oracle:** Validated against Python SciPy (scipy.stats.levene and scipy.stats.ttest_ind(equal_var=True/False)) with absolute precision $\le 10^{-6}$;<br>   - Never Crash guarantees for degenerate edge cases ( &lt; 2$, zero sample variance, and numeric/string group codes such as 1/2, 1.0, M/F).<br>2. **Command Bus &amp; Syntax L5 (statcraft_syntax::commands::ttest_indep_cmd):**<br>   - Typed engine command IndependentSamplesTTestCommand (stat.ttest.indep) with parameter schema for AI agents;<br>   - Canonical SPSS syntax generator:<br>     `	ext<br>     T-TEST GROUPS=gender(1 2)<br>       /CRITERIA=CI(0.95)<br>       /VARIABLES=salary score.<br>     `<br>3. **User Interface L6 (statcraft_app):**<br>   - Dedicated dialog IndependentSamplesTTestDialog ( \times 420$ px) with source variable list, test variables target, grouping variable slot, and vector transfer arrows;<br>   - Subdialog Define Groups... for specifying Group 1 and Group 2 labels;<br>   - Activated menu item Analyze -&gt; Compare Means -&gt; Independent-Samples T Test... with dataset availability validation;<br>   - Rendered authentic two-tier SPSS Pivot Tables in Output Viewer:<br>     1. **Group Statistics:** Variable, Group, N, Mean, Std. Deviation, Std. Error Mean;<br>     2. **Independent Samples Test:** Two-tier header with *Levene\&#39;s Test for Equality of Variances* ($, Sig.) and *t-test for Equality of Means* ($, $, Sig., Mean Diff, Std. Error Diff, 95% CI Lower/Upper) across both variance assumption rows;<br>   - Context menu TSV clipboard export (Excel/Sheets) and outline navigation.<br>4. **Quality &amp; DoD:**<br>   - Workspace unit tests cargo test --workspace -j 1 — 100% passed;<br>   - Architecture layer rules cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- layers — 0 violations;<br>   - Parity catalog cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- parity — command registered with Done status;<br>   - Localization linter i18n_lint_test — 2/2 passed (0% raw strings);<br>   - cargo clippy --workspace -j 1 -- -D warnings — 0 errors, 0 warnings.</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 6.3: Paired-Samples T Test (Compare Means)</h3><p>*Time: October 28, 2026, 11:00 (~35 minutes)*</p><p>Implemented the third procedure in the canonical IBM SPSS Statistics **Compare Means** module — **Paired-Samples T Test** (menu `Analyze -&gt; Compare Means -&gt; Paired-Samples T Test...`):<br>1. **Mathematical Engine L2 (`statcraft_algo::ttest_paired`):**<br>   - Paired sample descriptive statistics for both variables ($N, \bar{x}_1, \bar{x}_2, s_1, s_2, SE_1, SE_2$);<br>   - Pearson linear correlation coefficient ($r$), $t$-statistic for correlation and 2-tailed significance ($p_r$) with degrees of freedom $df = N - 2$;<br>   - Paired differences analysis $d_i = x_i - y_i$: mean difference $\bar{d}$, unbiased sample standard deviation of differences $s_d$, standard error of difference $SE_d$, Student&#39;s $t$-statistic, $df = N - 1$, 2-tailed $p$-value, and $100(1-\alpha)\%$ confidence interval of the difference;<br>   - **Golden Oracle:** Validated against Python `scipy.stats` (`ttest_rel` and `pearsonr`) with precision $\le 10^{-6}$;<br>   - **Never Crash** guarantees: robust handling of small samples ($N &lt; 2$