br>   - Made passing `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- design-guard` and `cargo test -p statcraft_app --test dialog_invariants -j 1` mandatory for Definition of Done (DoD).<br>7. **Quality &amp; Definition of Done:**<br>   - `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- design-guard` — 0 violations;<br>   - `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- file-guard` — 86 files scanned, 0 file size violations;<br>   - Invariant tests `dialog_invariants` — 9/9 passed;<br>   - All workspace tests `cargo test --workspace -j 1` — 93 passed (100%);<br>   - Architectural layers `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- layers` — 0 violations;<br>   - Parity catalog `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- parity` — clean;<br>   - Localization linter `i18n_lint_test` — 3/3 passed;<br>   - `cargo clippy --workspace -j 1 -- -D warnings` — 0 warnings;<br>   - `cargo fmt --check` — clean;<br>   - Clean release build `cargo build --package statcraft_app --release -j 1` — succeeded (1m 14s).</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 6.7: Hybrid Localization System — Embedded Catalogs and Dynamic External .ftl Discovery</h3><p>*Time: October 28, 2026, 18:45 (~25 minutes)*</p><p>Implemented a hybrid internationalization (i18n) architecture blending the canonical single-binary portability of the ArtCraft ecosystem with the flexibility of user-contributed translations:<br>1. **Guaranteed Base (Zero-Dependency Single Binary):**<br>   - Official `ru.ftl` and `en.ftl` catalogs remain embedded in the executable via `include_str!`. StatCraft is 100% self-contained, launches from any location, and never fails when external folders are missing.<br>2. **Dynamic Locale Discovery (`discover_and_load_locales`):**<br>   - On startup, the engine scans external paths: `STATCRAFT_LOCALES_DIR` environment variable, `locales/` directory adjacent to the binary (`current_exe()`), and the working `./locales` directory.<br>   - Any discovered `.ftl` file (e.g. `de.ftl`, `es.ftl`, `fr.ftl`) is registered at runtime and immediately surfaces in the `View -&gt; Language` menu without recompiling the application.<br>3. **Seamless Key Overriding (Resource Overriding):**<br>   - When a user supplies an existing language file (e.g. custom `ru.ftl`), external keys override defaults via `add_resource_overriding` without losing untranslated embedded strings.<br>4. **Intelligent Language Display Name (`language_name`):**<br>   - Native autonym is read from the language bundle itself (`lang-name-{lang}` or `lang-name`, e.g. `Deutsch`, `Español`);<br>   - Falls back to active language / English translation;<br>   - Final fallback displays the uppercase language code (`DE`, `ES`). Completely prevents raw keys such as `[lang-name-xx]`.<br>5. **Release Workflow Automation (`.github/workflows/release.yml`):**<br>   - Windows release ZIP `statcraft-windows-x64.zip` now packages the `locales/` directory alongside `statcraft_app.exe`.<br>6. **Testing &amp; Definition of Done:**<br>   - Authored end-to-end integration test `crates/statcraft_app/tests/i18n_external_locales_test.rs`;<br>   - Added 4 new unit tests in `crates/statcraft_i18n/src/lib.rs`;<br>   - Full test and static analysis pass via `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- ci` (`ALL CI QUALITY GATES PASSED!`);<br>   - Clean release build `cargo build --package statcraft_app --release -j 1` succeeded in 1m 08s.</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 7.1: Contingency Tables (Crosstabs) and Pearson&#39;s Chi-Square Test of Independence ($\chi^2$)</h3><p>*Time: October 28, 2026, 20:55 (~35 minutes)*</p><p>Implemented the fundamental procedure for analyzing categorical and discrete relationships — **Contingency Tables** (*Crosstabs*), association measures, and Pearson&#39;s Chi-Square Test of Independence ($\chi^2$, menu item `Analyze -&gt; Descriptive Statistics -&gt; Crosstabs...`):<br>1. **Mathematical Core L2 (`statcraft_algo::crosstabs` &amp; `crosstabs_types`):**<br>   - Construction of categorical $R \times C$ cross-classification grid supporting string categories and numeric value labels;<br>   - Computation of observed frequencies ($O_{ij}$), expected frequencies ($E_{ij} = \frac{R_i \cdot C_j}{N}$), residuals ($O_{ij} - E_{ij}$), and cell percentage breakdowns (row %, column %, and % of total table);<br>   - Pearson Chi-Square test: $\chi^2 = \sum \frac{(O_{ij} - E_{ij})^2}{E_{ij}}$ with degrees of freedom $df = (R - 1)(C - 1)$;<br>   - Likelihood Ratio test ($G^2$): $2 \sum O_{ij} \ln(O_{ij} / E_{ij})$ for cells with $O_{ij} &gt; 0$;<br>   - Double-precision $p$-value computation of the $\chi^2$ distribution survival function via regularized upper incomplete gamma function $Q(a, x)$ without external dependencies and with zero panics;<br>   - For $2 \times 2$ fourfold tables:<br>     * Yates&#39; Continuity Correction: $\chi^2_{Yates} = \frac{N (|ad - bc| - N/2)^2}{(a+b)(c+d)(a+c)(b+d)}$;<br>     * Two-sided Fisher&#39;s Exact Test computing exact hypergeometric probabilities via log-gamma functions and summing extreme outcomes $P(k) \le P(a) + 10^{-11}$;<br>   - Symmetric measures of association: $\phi = \sqrt{\chi^2 / N}$ and Cramér&#39;s $V$ with approximate asymptotic significance;<br>   - **Golden Oracle:** Unit test verification comparing contingency tables and test statistics against Python `scipy.stats` (`chi2_contingency`, `fisher_exact`) with precision $\le 10^{-6}$.<br>2. **Command Bus &amp; Syntax L5 (`statcraft_syntax::commands::crosstabs_cmd`):**<br>   - Typed engine command `CrosstabsCommand` (`stat.crosstabs`) equipped with JSON parameter specs for external AI agents;<br>   - Generates authentic IBM SPSS syntax:</p><p><em>[code block — open in CapsuleCraft web for its canvas]</em></p><p>3. **User Interface L6 (`statcraft_app::dialogs::crosstabs_dialog`):**<br>   - Fully unified `CrosstabsDialog` ($560 \times 430$ px) built exclusively with `DialogKit` design primitives:<br>     * Source variables picker (`VariablePicker`) on the left;<br>     * Target `Row(s)` and `Column(s)` list pickers in the center with vector `TransferButton`;<br>     * Right sidebar (`SubdialogSidebar`) hos