es or non-normally distributed continuous variables — **Two-Independent-Samples Tests** (`Analyze -&gt; Nonparametric Tests -&gt; Two Independent Samples...`):<br>1. **Mathematical Engine L2 (`statcraft_algo::nonparam_twosample` &amp; `nonparam_twosample_types`):**<br>   - Combined ranking algorithm with fractional mid-ranks and tie sum $T = \sum (t_i^3 - t_i)$;<br>   - Calculation of rank sums ($W_1, W_2$) and mean ranks ($\bar{R}_1, \bar{R}_2$) for both groups;<br>   - Mann-Whitney test statistic $U = \min(U_1, U_2)$, where $U_1 = W_1 - \frac{n_1(n_1 + 1)}{2}$;<br>   - Wilcoxon $W$ statistic definition adhering to the IBM SPSS Statistics standard (rank sum of the group with the smaller mean rank);<br>   - Expected value $\mu_U = \frac{n_1 n_2}{2}$ and tie-corrected variance $\sigma_U^2 = \frac{n_1 n_2}{12}\left[ (N + 1) - \frac{\sum (t_i^3 - t_i)}{N(N - 1)} \right]$;<br>   - Asymptotic $Z$-statistic and two-tailed significance derived from the regularized upper incomplete gamma function $Q(0.5, Z^2 / 2)$;<br>   - Wilcoxon Signed-Rank Test for paired observations with ranking of absolute differences $|d_i|$, exclusion of zero-ties, and $W = \min(W^+, W^-)$;<br>   - **Never Crash** protection: graceful handling of small sample sizes ($N &lt; 2$), degenerate zero-variance rank distributions, and flexible numeric/string group codes via `matches_group` on 100% safe Rust;<br>   - **Golden Oracle:** Test suite `nonparam_twosample_tests.rs` validating ranks, $U$, $W$, $Z$, and $p$-value against Python `scipy.stats` (`mannwhitneyu`, `wilcoxon`) and manual SPSS benchmarks with $\le 10^{-6}$ precision.<br>2. **Command Bus &amp; Syntax L5 (`statcraft_syntax::commands::nonparam_twosample_cmd`):**<br>   - Typed engine command `MannWhitneyCommand` (`stat.npar.mann_whitney`) with JSON parameter specs for external AI agents;<br>   - Canonical IBM SPSS Statistics syntax emission:</p><p><em>[code block — open in CapsuleCraft web for its canvas]</em></p><p>3. **User Interface L6 (`st