te relationship analysis procedure — **Bivariate Correlations** (`Analyze -&gt; Correlate -&gt; Bivariate...`):<br>1. **Mathematical Engine L2 (`statcraft_algo::correlations` &amp; `correlations_types`):**<br>   - Pearson linear correlation coefficient calculation ($r = \frac{\sum (x_i - \bar{x})(y_i - \bar{y})}{\sqrt{\sum (x_i - \bar{x})^2 \sum (y_i - \bar{y})^2}}$), cross-product sum of squares ($SS_{xy}$), and unbiased sample covariance ($Cov(x, y)$);<br>   - Spearman rank correlation ($\rho$) with fractional average ranking for tied observations;<br>   - Kendall rank correlation ($\tau$-b) with concordant ($P$) and discordant ($Q$) pair computation and analytical tie adjustments $T_x, T_y$;<br>   - Rigorous $p$-value derivation for two-tailed and one-tailed hypotheses via Student&#39;s $t$ survival function (Pearson and Spearman) and asymptotic normal $Z$ statistics (Kendall);<br>   - Automatic significance flag annotations in matrix cells (`*` at $p &lt; 0.05$, `**` at $p &lt; 0.01$);<br>   - Missing value handling: pairwise and listwise case exclusions;<br>   - **Never Crash** protection: safe handling of zero-variance constants, degenerate pairs, and small sample edge cases ($N &lt; 2$) on 100% safe Rust;<br>   - **Golden Oracle:** Test suite `correlations_tests.rs` verifying correlation matrices and significance values against Python `scipy.stats` (`pearsonr`, `spearmanr`, `kendalltau`) within $\le 10^{-6}$ precision.<br>2. **Command Bus &amp; Syntax L5 (`statcraft_syntax::commands::correlations_cmd`):**<br>   - Typed engine command `CorrelationsCommand` (`stat.correlations`) with JSON parameter specs for external AI agents;<br>   - Canonical IBM SPSS Statistics syntax emission (`CORRELATIONS /VARIABLES=... /PRINT=TWOTAIL SIG /STATISTICS DESCRIPTIVES XPROD /MISSING=PAIRWISE.` and `NONPAR CORR`).<br>3. **User Interface L6 (`statcraft_app::dialogs::correlations_dialog`):**<br>   - Modal dialog `CorrelationsDialog` ($560 \times 430$ px) built with `DialogKit`:<