ng for grouping variable $[min, max]$ following SPSS canon `BY groupvar(min max)`;<br>   - Combined ranking across all $N = \sum n_i$ cases with mid-ranks for ties;<br>   - Group rank sums $R_i$ and mean ranks $\bar{R}_i = R_i / n_i$ across all $k$ groups;<br>   - Raw Kruskal-Wallis statistic $H = \frac{12}{N(N+1)} \sum \frac{R_i^2}{n_i} - 3(N+1)$;<br>   - Tie correction factor $C = 1 - \frac{\sum (t_j^3 - t_j)}{N^3 - N}$ and adjusted statistic $H_{adj} = H / C$;<br>   - Degrees of freedom $df = k - 1$ and asymptotic 2-tailed $p$-value from $\chi^2$ distribution (`chi_square_sf(H_adj, df)`);<br>   - **Golden Oracle:** Test suite `kruskal_wallis_tests.rs` verified against Python `scipy.stats.kruskal` to $\le 10^{-6}$ precision for both unique and tied distributions;<br>   - **Never Crash** protection for empty datasets, single groups ($k &lt; 2$), and degenerate cases on 100% safe Rust.<br>3. **Command Bus &amp; Syntax L5 (`statcraft_syntax::commands::kruskal_wallis_cmd`):**<br>   - Typed engine command `KruskalWallisCommand` (`stat.npar.kruskal_wallis`) with JSON parameter specs for external AI agents;<br>   - Canonical SPSS syntax generator:</p><p><em>[code block — open in CapsuleCraft web for its canvas]</em></p><p>4. **User Interface L6 (`statcraft_app::dialogs::kruskal_wallis_dialog` &amp; `kruskal_define_range`):**<br>   - Modal dialog `Tests for Several Independent Samples` ($560 \times 430$ px) built with `DialogKit`:<br>     * Available variables list `VariablePicker` with scale icons;<br>     * `Test Variable List:` target list and `Grouping Variable:` display box showing range `var(min max)`;<br>     * Adaptive vector transfer buttons `TransferButton`;<br>     * Right sidebar `SubdialogSidebar` with `[ Define Range... ]` button;<br>     * Modal subdialog `Define Range` ($360 \times 300$ px) using `DialogShell::subdialog` with `Minimum:` and `Maximum:` fields;<br>     * `Test Type` group box with `[x] Kruskal-Wallis H` checkbox;<br>     * Bottom action bar 