al measurement procedure — **Reliability Analysis** (`Analyze -&gt; Scale -&gt; Reliability Analysis...`, engine command `stat.scale.reliability` / syntax `RELIABILITY /VARIABLES=... /SCALE(&#39;ALL VARIABLES&#39;) ALL /MODEL=ALPHA`):</p><p>1. **Mathematical Engine L2 (`statcraft_algo::reliability` &amp; `reliability_types`):**<br>   - Internal consistency estimation via Cronbach&#39;s Alpha: $\alpha = \frac{k}{k - 1} \left( 1 - \frac{\sum s_i^2}{s_{total}^2} \right)$;<br>   - Standardized Alpha based on average inter-item correlation $\bar{r}$: $\alpha_{std} = \frac{k \bar{r}}{1 + (k - 1) \bar{r}}$;<br>   - Listwise missing data deletion across all analyzed scale items;<br>   - Case Processing Summary: Valid ($N, \%$), Excluded ($N, \%$), and Total ($N, 100.0\%$);<br>   - Item Statistics: Mean ($\bar{x}_i$), Standard Deviation ($s_i$), Valid Sample Count ($N$);<br>   - Item-Total Statistics:<br>     * Scale Mean if Item Deleted: $\mu_{-i} = \mu_{total} - \bar{x}_i$;<br>     * Scale Variance if Item Deleted: $s_{-i}^2 = s_{total}^2 + s_i^2 - 2 \text{Cov}(X_i, X_{total})$;<br>     * Corrected Item-Total Correlation: $r_{i(total - i)} = \frac{\text{Cov}(X_i, X_{total}) - s_i^2}{\sqrt{s_i^2 \cdot s_{-i}^2}}$;<br>     * Cronbach&#39;s Alpha if Item Deleted: $\alpha_{-i} = \frac{k - 1}{k - 2} \left( 1 - \frac{\sum_{j \neq i} s_j^2}{s_{-i}^2} \right)$ for $k &gt; 2$;<br>   - Summary Scale Statistics: Mean, Variance, Standard Deviation, Item Count;<br>   - Seamless synergy with active sample filtering (`Select Cases`) and frequency weighting (`Weight Cases`);<br>   - **Golden Oracle:** Unit and validation tests in `reliability_tests.rs` with analytical precision $\le 10^{-6}$;<br>   - **Never Crash** protection: safe handling of $k &lt; 2$, zero-variance degenerate scales, identical survey responses, and missing values on 100% safe Rust.</p><p>2. **Command Bus &amp; Syntax L5 (`statcraft_syntax::commands::reliability_cmd`):**<br>   - Strongly-typed `ReliabilityCommand` (`stat.scale.reliability`) with parameter `specs()` for external AI agents;<br>   - Canonical IBM SPSS Statistics syntax generator:</p><p><em>[code block — open in CapsuleCraft web for its canvas]</em></p><p>- Full `Undo` / `Redo` lifecycle support.</p><p>3. **DialogKit Desktop User Interface L6 (`statcraft_app::dialogs::reliability_dialog`):**<br>   - Centered canonical modal dialog ($560 \times 430$ px, `DialogShell::standard`);<br>   - Two-panel `VariablePicker` with measurement scale icons and vector transfer buttons `TransferButton` (`-&gt;` / `&lt;-`);<br>   - `Items:` target list (requires at least 2 items to enable `[ OK ]`);<br>   - Model selector dropdown: `Model: Alpha`;<br>   - Text input for scale identifier: `Scale label:` (default `ALL VARIABLES`);<br>   - Right sidebar `SubdialogSidebar` with `[ Statistics... ]` button;<br>   - Modal statistics subdialog ($360 \times 300$ px, `DialogShell::subdialog`):<br>     * Checkboxes `[x] Item`, `[x] Scale`, `[x] Scale if item deleted`;<br>     * Bottom action row `SubdialogActionBar` (`[ Continue ] [ Cancel ] [ Help ]`);<br>   - Canonical bottom action bar `DialogActionBar` (`[ OK ] [ Paste ] [ Reset ] [ Cancel ] [ Help ]`).</p><p>4. **Summary Pivot Tables in Output Viewer (`tables_reliability.rs`):**<br>   - **Case Processing Summary:** Cases (Valid, Excluded, Total) with $N$ and $\%$, listwise note footnote;<br>   - **Reliability Statistics:** Cronbach&#39;s Alpha, Cronbach&#39;s Alpha Based on Standardized Items, N of Items;<br>   - **Item Statistics:** Item, Mean, Std. Deviation, N;<br>   - **Item-Total Statistics:** Item, Scale Mean if Item Deleted, Scale Variance if Item Deleted, Corrected Item-Total Correlation, Cronbach&#39;s Alpha if Item Deleted;<br>   - **Scale Statistics:** Mean, Variance, Std. Deviation, N of Items;<br>   - TSV clipboard export and Outline Tree integration.</p><p>5. **Reactivity, Menu &amp; Status Bar:**<br>   - Activated main menu item `Analyze -&gt; Scale -&gt; Reliability Analysis