 via numerical inversion of $S = R^{-1}$ and $\text{KMO} = \frac{\sum_{i \ne j} r_{ij}^2}{\sum_{i \ne j} r_{ij}^2 + \sum_{i \ne j} a_{ij}^2}$;<br>     * **Bartlett&#39;s Test of Sphericity**: $\chi^2 = -(n - 1 - (2p + 5)/6) \ln |R|$ at $df = p(p - 1)/2$ with exact $p$-value from Chi-square survival function;<br>   - Principal Component Analysis (**PCA**) Extraction:<br>     * Spectral decomposition of real symmetric matrix $R$ via cyclic Jacobi rotations on 100% safe Rust without external linear algebra dependencies (`jacobi_eigen_symmetric`);<br>     * Kaiser criterion ($\lambda \ge 1.0$) or fixed factor count extraction;<br>     * Deterministic sign convention for positive dominant loadings;<br>     * Factor loadings $l_{ik} = \sqrt{\lambda_k} \cdot v_{ik}$;<br>     * Communalities (*Communalities*): initial 1.000 for PCA, extraction $h_i^2 = \sum_{k=1}^m l_{ik}^2$;<br>     * Total Variance Explained (*Total Variance Explained*): initial eigenvalues, % of variance, cumulative %, and extraction sums of squared loadings;<br>     * Component Matrix (*Component Matrix*);<br>   - **Golden Oracle:** `factor_tests.rs` unit tests verified against Python `scipy.linalg.eigh` and `factor_analyzer` with precision $\le 10^{-6}$;<br>   - **Never Crash** protection against singular matrices, $n &lt; 2$, zero-variance variables, and missing cases.</p><p>2. **Command Bus &amp; Syntax L5 (`statcraft_syntax::commands::factor_cmd`):**<br>   - Typed engine command `FactorCommand` (`stat.factor`) with JSON parameter specs for external AI agents;<br>   - Canonical IBM SPSS Statistics syntax generator and parser:</p><p><em>[code block — open in CapsuleCraft web for its canvas]</em></p><p>- Full `Undo` / `Redo` lifecycle support.</p><p>3. **DialogKit Desktop User Interface L6 (`statcraft_app::dialogs::factor_dialog`):**<br>   - Centered canonical modal dialog ($560 \times 430$ px, `DialogShell::standard`);<br>   - Two-panel `VariablePicker` with measurement scale icons and vector transfer buttons `TransferButton` (`-&gt;` / `&lt;-`);<br>   - `Variables:` target list (requires at least 2 items to enable `[ OK ]`);<br>   - Right sidebar `SubdialogSidebar` with modal configuration triggers:<br>     * `[ Descriptives... ]`: subdialog with `[x] KMO and Bartlett&#39;s test of sphericity`;<br>     * `[ Extraction... ]`: subdialog with PCA method and factor retention criteria (Eigenvalues over 1.0 / Fixed number of factors);<br>     * Action row `SubdialogActionBar` (`[ Continue ] [ Cancel ] [ Help ]`);<br>   - Canonical bottom action bar `DialogActionBar` (`[ OK ] [ Paste ] [ Reset ] [ Cancel ] [ Help ]`).</p><p>4. **Summary Pivot Tables in Output Viewer (`tables_factor.rs`):**<br>   - **KMO and Bartlett&#39;s Test:** Kaiser-Meyer-Olkin Measure of Sampling Adequacy, Bartlett&#39;s Test of Sphericity (Approx. Chi-Square, df, Sig.);<br>   - **Communalities:** Variable, Initial (1.000), Extraction;<br>   - **Total Variance Explained:** Component, Initial Eigenvalues (Total, % of Variance, Cumulative %), Extraction Sums of Squared Loadings;<br>   - **Component Matrix:** variables $\times$ components;<br>   - TSV clipboard export and Outline Tree integration.</p><p>5. **Reactivity, Menu &amp; Status Bar:**<br>   - Activated main menu item `Analyze -&gt; Dimension Reduction -&gt; Factor...`;<br>   - Canonical syntax automatically recorded to Output Viewer (Log);<br>   - Status bar feedback notification (`Factor analysis computed for &lt;n&gt; case(s), &lt;m&gt; component(s) extracted`).</p><p>6. **Quality Control &amp; Definition of Done:**<br>   - Full automated CI quality gate passed (`cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- ci` — 100% OK);<br>   - Strict adherence to file size limits (`file-guard` $\le 500$ lines on leaf modules);<br>   - Strict adherence to DialogKit standards (`design-guard` — 100% compliant);<br>   - Architectural and parity linters (`layers`, `parity` — 38 documented procedures) reporting 0 violations;<br>   - Synchronous localization without string hardcoding (`locales/en.ftl`, `locales/ru.ftl`);<br>   - Compiler linter `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -j 1 -- -D warnings` — 0 warnings;<br>   - Release binary built and deployed to `C:\StatCraft\statcraft_app.exe`.</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 12.1: Subgroup Means Breakdown and One-Way ANOVA (Subgroup Means Breakdown: `MEANS`)</h3><p>*Time: October 29, 2026, 19:40 (~45 minutes)*</p><p>Implemented the classical exploratory procedure for subgroup analysis of IBM SPSS Statistics — **Subgroup Means Breakdown** (`Analyze -&gt; Compare Means -&gt; Means...`), combining detailed cell-level summary statistics across factor levels, one-way analysis of variance (ANOVA), and measures of association:</p><p>1. **Mathematical Engine L2 (`statcraft_algo::means`, `means_types`, `means_tests`):**<br>   - Listwise missing case deletion per table and full support for observation weights (`row_weight`);<br>   - Natural sorting of group categories (numeric ordering for numeric groups, lexicographic for strings);<br>   - Complete set of cell statistics per group and for the overall Total row:<br>     * Case count ($N$), weighted mean ($\bar{x}$), unbiased standard deviation ($s$), sample variance ($s^2$);<br>     * Median (with proper linear interpolation), minimum ($\min$), maximum ($\max$), weighted sum of values ($\sum x$);<br>   - **One-Way ANOVA Table (ANOVA Table):**<br>     * Between Groups variation: $SS_{between} = \sum n_j (\bar{x}_j - \bar{x})^2$, $df = k - 1$;<br>     * Within Groups variation: $SS_{within} = \sum \sum (x_{ij} - \bar{x}_j)^2$, $df = N - k$;<br>     * Total variation: $SS_{total} = SS_{between} + SS_{within}$, $df = N - 1$;<br>     * Mean Squares ($MS$), Fisher&#39;s $F$-test ($F = MS_{between} / MS_{within}$), and exact $p$-value from Fisher distribution survival function (`f_distribution_sf`);<br>   - **Measures of Association:**<br>     * Coefficient of determination $\eta^2 = SS_{between} / SS_{total}$ (proportion of variance explained) and correlation ratio $\eta = \sqrt{\eta^2}$;<br>   - **Golden Oracle:** `means_tests.rs` unit tests verified against analytical standards and Python `scipy.stats.f_oneway` with precision $\le 10^{-6}$;<br>   - **Never Crash** resilience against empty samples, single-case groups ($N &lt; 2$), zero within-group variance, and missing data on 100% safe Rust.</p><p>2. **Command Bus &amp; Syntax L5 (`statcraft_syntax::commands::means_cmd`):**<br>   - Typed engine command `MeansCommand` (`stat.means`) with JSON parameter specs for external AI agents;<br>   - Canonical IBM SPSS Statistics syntax generator:</p><p><em>[code block — open in CapsuleCraft web for its canvas]</em></p><p>- Full `Undo` / `Redo` lifecycle support.</p><p>3. **DialogKit Desktop User Interface L6 (`statcraft_app::dialogs::means_dialog`):**<br>   - Centered canonical modal dialog ($560 \times 430$ px, `DialogShell::standard`);<br>   - Two-panel `VariablePicker` with measurement scale icons and adaptive vector transfer buttons `TransferButton` (`-&gt;` / `&lt;-`);<br>   - Target lists `Dependent List:` and `Layer 1 of 1:` (independent factor variables);<br>   - Right sidebar `SubdialogSidebar` with `[ Options... ]` button:<br>     * Modal subdialog for selecting statistics (Mean, Number of Cases, Std. Deviation, Variance, Median, Minimum, Maximum, Sum) and checkbox `[x] Anova table and eta`;<br>     * Action row `SubdialogActionBar` (`[ Continue ] [ Cancel ] [ Help ]`);<br>   - Canonical bottom action bar `DialogActionBar` (`[ OK ] [ Paste ] [ Reset ] [ Cancel ] [ Help ]`).</p><p>4. **Summary Pivot Tables in Output Viewer (`tables_means.rs`):**<br>   - **Case Processing Summary:** Dependent $\times$ Grouping, Included ($N$, %), Excluded ($N$, %), Total ($N$, %);<br>   - **Report:** factor level breakdown with statistics (Mean, N, Std. Deviation, Variance, Median, Minimum, Maximum, Sum) and summary Total row;<br>   - **ANOVA Table:** Sum of Squares, df, Mean Square, F, Sig. for Between Groups, Within Groups, and Total