ent files)` when empty, and separator with `Clear Recent Files`.<br>2. **Session Lifecycle Coordination L6 (`app_session.rs`):**<br>   - `File -&gt; New -&gt; Data` (`Ctrl+N`): clears current dataset to a blank sheet, resets `current_file_path`, resets `CommandBus` history and active filter/weight/split states, activates `Data View` tab, reports to status bar, and appends `NEW DATASET.` to the `Output Viewer` Log;<br>   - `File -&gt; New -&gt; Syntax`: shifts focus to the `Syntax Editor` tab, initializes canonical header `* StatCraft Syntax Editor. / * Created: &lt;timestamp&gt;.`, reports status;<br>   - `File -&gt; New -&gt; Project` (`Ctrl+Shift+N`): full state reset (dataset, output viewer log, syntax editor, active path);<br>   - `File -&gt; Close Project`: resets active project state, restores status bar to `Ready`;<br>   - Unsaved changes guard `has_unsaved_changes()`: modal confirmation `ConfirmSaveDialog` (`[ Save ] [ Don&#39;t Save ] [ Cancel ]`) built on `DialogShell::subdialog` prevents accidental loss of data.<br>3. **Syntax Editor Interactive Screen L6 (`views/syntax_editor.rs`):**<br>   - Interactive view `SyntaxEditorState` and `render_syntax_editor`;<br>   - Monospace multiline code editor tab docked in the workspace (`Tab::SyntaxEditor`);<br>   - Shortcut navigation via `Window -&gt; Syntax Editor` (`Ctrl+4`).<br>4. **Quality Control &amp; Definition of Done:**<br>   - Dedicated unit and integration test suite `crates/statcraft_app/tests/session_lifecycle_tests.rs` (queue rotation, change detection, session reset flows, headless rendering);<br>   - Full automated CI quality gate passed (`cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- ci` — 100% OK);<br>   - File guard compliance: coordinator `app.rs` stays strictly under limit (1407 of 1500 lines);<br>   - DialogKit design compliance `design-guard` — 100% OK;<br>   - Synchronous bilingual localization (`locales/en.ftl`, `locales/ru.ftl`);<br>   - Compiler linter `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -j 1 -- -D warnings` — 0 warnings.</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase MP-3: Export Data &amp; Export Output Reports</h3><p>*Time: October 29, 2026, 22:15 (~35 minutes)*</p><p>Implemented complete export workflows for data and analysis outputs in the `File -&gt; Export` menu:<br>1. **Data Export L0/L1 (`statcraft_io::csv_writer`, `statcraft_core::csv_export`):**<br>   - L0 module `csv_writer.rs` supporting `CsvExportOptions` (comma, semicolon, tab delimiters, quote escaping, newline/carriage return handling, decimal comma conversion, and configurable missing value `sysmis_repr`);<br>   - L1 module `csv_export.rs` implementing `export_dataset_to_csv` for streaming `DataSet` export with value labels substitution (`ValueLabels`) or raw numeric codes, empty dataset safety (0 rows/cols), and streaming `std::io::Write`;<br>   - Save file dialog filters: `Comma-Separated Values (*.csv)`, `Tab-Delimited Values (*.tsv, *.txt)`, `Semicolon-Separated Values (*.csv)` with automatic delimiter resolution from path.<br>2. **Reporting Architectural Layer L4 (`crates/statcraft_reporting`):**<br>   - Created new standalone L4 layer crate `statcraft_reporting` (registered in `xtask/src/layers.rs` maintaining strict top-to-bottom hierarchy L4 $\to$ Utility, L6 $\to$ L4);<br>   - Universal reporting model: `ReportDocument`, `ReportSection`, `ReportItem` (Log, Notes, Table, Text, Warning), `ReportTable`, `ReportNotes`, `CellAlignment`;<br>   - HTML report generator `html_export.rs`: standalone single-file HTML5 document with authentic SPSS table styling (sans-serif typography, double header borders, zebra striping, accent procedure headings, italic footnotes, monospace syntax logs, and HTML entity escaping);<br>   - Monospace plain text generator `txt_export.rs`: ASCII border tables with dynamic column width calculation and text alignment;<br>   - TSV bundle generator `tsv_export.rs`: joins all session tables separated by double newlines for direct spreadsheet pasting (Excel, Google Sheets).<br>3. **User Interface &amp; Integration L6 (`crates/statcraft_app`):**<br>   - Module `views/output_view/export.rs`: converts `OutputViewerState` into `ReportDocument` across all statistical procedures;<br>   - Module `export_handlers.rs`: activates `File -&gt; Export -&gt; Export Output...` and `File -&gt; Export -&gt; Export Data...` (with `requires_dataset_status` availability guard);<br>   - Native OS save file dialogs via `rfd::FileDialog::save_file()`;<br>   - Status bar feedback notifications (`status-data-exported`, `status-output-exported`);<br>   - Syntax logging in `Output Viewer`: `SAVE TRANSLATE OUTFILE=&#39;...&#39; /TYPE=... /REPLACE /FIELDNAMES.` and `OUTPUT EXPORT /CONTENTS=ALL /TYPE=... /DESTINATION=&#39;...&#39;`.<br>4. **Quality Control &amp; Definition of Done:**<br>   - 100% pass on full CI pipeline: `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- ci` (`fmt`, `clippy -D warnings`, `cargo test --workspace -j 1`, `parity`);<br>   - Strict layer validation `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- layers` (L4Reporting verification);<br>   - File size guard compliance `file-guard` ($\le 500$ lines on all new modules);<br>   - DialogKit design compliance `design-guard`;<br>   - Synchronous bilingual localization without string hardcoding (`locales/en.ftl`, `locales/ru.ftl`);<br>   - Test suites added for `statcraft_io::csv_writer`, `statcraft_core::csv_export`, `statcraft_reporting` (HTML, TXT, TSV), `statcraft_app::export_handlers`, and `output_view::export`.</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase MP-5: SPSS Binary Data Files Import (.sav / .zsav)</h3><p>*Time: October 29, 2026, 22:20 (~30 minutes)*</p><p>Implemented full-featured import of original binary IBM SPSS Statistics files (`.sav` and compressed `.zsav`) with complete extraction of data matrices and dictionary metadata without relying on proprietary third-party libraries:<br>1. **Low-Level Binary Decoder L0 (`crates/statcraft_io::spss_loader`):**<br>   - Modular architecture: `header.rs`, `records.rs`, `decompress.rs`, `mod.rs` (each strictly $\le 500$ lines compliant with `file-guard`);<br>   - System Header Record 0 parsing (`$FL2` / `$FL3`, automatic endianness detection via `layout_code`, compression bias `bias = 100.0`, case weight index `weight_index`, case count `case_cnt`);<br>   - Variable Records Record 2 handling: numeric &amp; string variables, labels, user missing value specifications (discrete values, ranges);<br>   - Value Labels Records Record 3 &amp; 4: pairs `(f64, label)` mapped to target variable slots;<br>   - Extension Records Record 7: subtype 4 (Display parameters: Measure Scale/Ordinal/Nominal, alignment, column widths), subtype 13 (Long Variable Names mapping short 8-char names to UTF-8 names), subtype 20 (Character Encoding), subtype 24 (ZLIB chunk metadata for `.zsav`);<br>   - Bytecode streaming decompressor Record 999: opcode decoding 1..251 (`code - bias`), 252 (EOF), 253 (8-byte IEEE 754 floats or string literals), 254 (whitespace), 255 (system missing `SYSMIS` / `Null`);<br>   - Compressed `.zsav` support: reads `ztrailer`, streams block decompression via `flate2::read::ZlibDecoder` into uniform bytecode reader.<br>2. **Core Layer Integration L1 (`crates/statcraft_core::spss`):**<br>   - Module `spss.rs`: `DataSet::from_spss_data`, `DataSet::load_spss_from_path`, `DataSet::load_spss_from_reader`;<br>   - Converts `SpssVariableInfo` into `VariableMetadata`: 9 canonical SPSS types, `Measure`, `Alignment`, `ValueLabels`, `MissingValues`, and `weight_var`;<br>   - Typed error integration `CoreError::Io(#[from] statcraft_io::IoError)`.<br>3. **Command Bus L5 (`crates/statcraft_syntax`):**<br>   - Typed engine command `ImportSpssCommand` (`data.import_spss`) with JSON schema `specs()`, execution and Undo support;<br>   - Registered in `CommandBus::with_defaults()`;<br>   - SPSS syntax equivalent generator `GET FILE=&#39;&lt;path&gt;&#39;.`;<br>   - Transparent `.sav` and `.zsav` support added to `OpenFileCommand` (`data.open_file`).<br>4. **Desktop UI L6 (`crates/statcraft_app`):**<br>   - Activated menu item `File -&gt; Import Data -&gt; SPSS Data...` (`menu-file-import-spss`) with `SPSS Statistics Data (*.sav, *.zsav)` file dialog;<br>   - Added SPSS file filters to general `File -&gt; Open Data...` dialog (`open_data_dialog`);<br>   - `load_file_from_path` in `app_session.rs` automatically detects `.sav`/`.zsav`, loads dataset via command bus, logs `GET FILE=&#39;&lt;path&gt;&#39;.` into Output Viewer, updates `RecentFiles`, and focuses `Data View`.<br>5. **Quality Control &amp; Definition of Done:**<br>   - 100% pass on CI quality gate: `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- ci` (`fmt`, `clippy -D warnings`, `cargo test --workspace -j 1`, `parity`, `layers`, `file-guard`, `design-guard`);<br>   - Unit tests in `statcraft_io::spss_loader::tests`: bytecode compression, uncompressed streams, corrupt header handling;<br>   - Session lifecycle integration test `crates/statcraft_app/tests/session_lifecycle_tests.rs::test_load_spss_sav_session_lifecycle`;<br>   - 100% bilingual localization (`locales/en.ftl`, `locales/ru.ftl`);<br>   - 100% Safe Rust without `unwrap`/`expect`/`panic` in non-test code.</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase MP-2: Native Project Format (.stc) &amp; Save Commands</h3><p>*Time: October 29, 2026, 22:25 (~30 minutes)*</p><p>Implemented full native project format (`.stc`) persistence and file operations across the main `File` menu:<br>1. **Native Project Format Codec L0 (`statcraft_io::stc_codec`):**<br>   - Project container structure `StcContainer` (`format_version = 1`, `dataset_name`, `metadata_json`, `table: RawTable`, `active_filter_var`, `weight_var`, `split_file_json`);<br>   - Streaming Gzip compression via `flate2::write::GzEncoder` with automatic detection of the GZIP header (`0x1f 0x8b`) and fallback JSON deserialization on read;<br>   - Clean codec APIs: `save_stc_container`, `load_stc_container`, `save_stc_container_to_path`, `load_stc_container_from_path`;<br>   - CSV/TSV table export `crates/statcraft_io/src/csv_writer.rs` (`export_raw_table_to_csv_path`) with localized decimal separator and escaping support.<br>2. **Comprehensive Metadata Dictionary Serialization L1 (`statcraft_core::stc_codec`):**<br>   - 100% loss-free serialization and restoration of dataset state:<br>     * All 9 canonical SPSS variable data types (`Numeric`, `Comma`, `Dot`, `Scientific`, `Date`, `Dollar`, `CustomCurrency`, `String`, `RestrictedNumeric`);<br>     * Measurement scales (`Scale`, `Ordinal`, `Nominal`), text alignments (`Left`, `Right`, `Center`), column widths, and decimal digits;<br>     * Complete value label dictionaries `ValueLabels` (`BTreeMap&lt;String, String&gt;`);<br>     * Discrete and range missing values `MissingValues`;<br>     * Active filter configuration (`active_filter_var`), frequency weight variable (`weight_var`), and split-file settings (`split_file`);<br>   - Unified methods: `save_stc_to_writer`, `load_stc_from_reader`, `save_stc_to_path`, `load_stc_from_path`, and `save_csv_to_path`.<br>3. **Command Bus &amp; Canonical Syntax L5 (`statcraft_syntax::commands::file_cmds`):**<br>   - Save command `SaveFileCommand` (`data.save_file`) with parameter specs `specs()` and canonical syntax generator `SAVE OUTFILE=&#39;&lt;path&gt;&#39;.\nEXECUTE.`;<br>   - Open command `OpenFileCommand` (`data.open_file`) with syntax generator `GET FILE=&#39;&lt;path&gt;&#39;.\nEXECUTE.`;<br>   - Default registration in `CommandBus::with_defaults()`.<br>4. **Main Menu &amp; Native Dialog Integration L6 (`statcraft_app::app_session` &amp; `app.rs`):**<br>   - Transitioned menu items `File -&gt; Save` (`Ctrl+S`), `File -&gt; Save As...` (`Ctrl+Shift+S`), `File -&gt; Save Data As...`, `File -&gt; Open Project...` (`Ctrl+Shift+O`), `File -&gt; Open Data...` (`Ctrl+O`) to `MenuItemStatus::Ready`;<br>   - Native system file dialog integration via `rfd::FileDialog` with file extensions, filters, and smart default filenames;<br>   - Responsive keyboard shortcuts in `update()` (`Ctrl+S` -&gt; `save_project`, `Ctrl+Shift+S` -&gt; `save_project_as`, `Ctrl+Shift+O` -&gt; `open_project_dialog`);<br>   - Dynamic window title displaying the active file name and dirty state indicator `*`;<br>   - Automatic `RecentFiles` queue tracking and Output Viewer log recording (`SAVE OUTFILE=...` / `GET FILE=...`);<br>   - Safe session transition guard: prompt to save project before creating/opening new projects via `ConfirmSaveDialog`.<br>5. **Architectural Decomposition (&quot;Divide, don&#39;t prune&quot;):**<br>   - Extracted status message coordination into `crates/statcraft_app/src/status_message.rs`, slimming `app.rs` from 1453 down to ~1300 lines, ensuring healthy safety margin under the 1500 line limit.<br>6. **Quality Control &amp; Definition of Done:**<br>   - Full automated CI quality gate passed (`cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- ci` — 100% OK);<br>   - 202 Rust files verified within strict size limits (`file-guard` — 100% OK);<br>   - Architecture layer rules `layers` (L0-L6) and design rules `design-guard` — 100% compliant;<br>   - 125+ workspace unit and integration tests passing;<br>   - 100% synchronous localization (`locales/en.ftl`, `locales/ru.ftl`);<br>   - Compiler linter `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -j 1 -- -D warnings` — 0 warnings.</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase MP-4: Microsoft Excel Import (.xlsx / .xls / .ods)</h3><p>*Time: October 29, 2026, 23:05 (~35 minutes)*</p><p>Implemented direct tabular data reading and importing from Microsoft Excel and OpenDocument spreadsheets without needing prior conversion to CSV:<br>1. **I/O Layer L0 (`statcraft_io::excel_loader`):**<br>   - Integrated modern crate `calamine = &quot;0.37&quot;` (100% safe Rust, memory-efficient streaming parser without COM or Office dependencies);<br>   - Functions `load_excel_from_path`, `load_excel_from_reader`, and `load_excel_from_range` supporting `.xlsx`, `.xlsm`, `.xls`, `.ods`;<br>   - Worksheet parsing engine:<br>     * Default selection of the first sheet (`workbook.sheet_names()[0]`) or by explicit sheet name;<br>     * Canonical SPSS variable name sanitization and deduplication (`sanitize_and_dedup_headers`): invalid character conversion to `_`, `V_` prefix for leading digits, `VAR00001` generation for empty headers, and sequential `_1`, `_2` disambiguation;<br>     * High-fidelity cell type mapping from `calamine::Data` (integers `Int`, floats `Float`, booleans `Bool` -&gt; `1.0`/`0.0`, dates/times `DateTime`/`DateTimeIso`, strings `String`, empty/error cells `Empty`/`Error`/`&quot;NA&quot;`/`&quot;.&quot;` -&gt; `RawValue::Null`);<br>     * Automated column type inference: columns where all non-null values parse as numbers are typed as `RawDataType::Numeric`, while mixed columns cast numbers to formatted text as `RawDataType::Text`;<br>   - **Never Crash** guarantees: robust handling of empty workbooks, 0-row sheets, and header-only sheets without panics.<br>2. **Command Bus &amp; Syntax L5 (`statcraft_syntax::commands::import_excel`):**<br>   - Strongly-typed `ImportExcelCommand` (`data.import_excel`) with parameter specification `specs()` (`file_path`, `sheet_name`, `dataset_name`) for external AI agents;<br>   - Direct population of active `DataSet` with full `Undo` support (dataset reset);<br>   - Registered in default command bus `CommandBus::with_defaults()`.<br>3. **User Interface &amp; Integration L6 (`crates/statcraft_app`):**<br>   - Activated menu items `File -&gt; Import Data -&gt; Excel...` (`menu-file-import-excel`) and `File -&gt; Import Data -&gt; CSV...` (`menu-file-import-csv`);<br>   - Added `open_excel_dialog` using `rfd::FileDialog` with filter `Excel Spreadsheets (*.xlsx, *.xls, *.ods, *.xlsm)`;<br>   - Enhanced `load_file_from_path`: automated detection of spreadsheet extensions, execution of `data.import_excel`, addition to `RecentFiles` queue;<br>   - Canonical syntax logging in Output Viewer:</p><p><em>[code block — open in CapsuleCraft web for its canvas]</em></p><p>- Real-time status bar notification: `Dataset imported: &lt;name&gt; (&lt;n&gt; cases, &lt;m&gt; variables)`.<br>4. **Quality Control &amp; Definition of Done:**<br>   - 100% pass on full CI pipeline: `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- ci` (`cargo fmt --check`, `clippy -D warnings`, `cargo test --workspace -j 1`, `parity`);<br>   - Architecture layer integrity verified via `xtask layers` and `xtask parity` (40 documented commands);<br>   - File guard compliance: `excel_loader.rs` (344 of 500 lines), coordinator `app.rs` (1471 of 1500 lines);<br>   - DialogKit design compliance `design-guard`;<br>   - Synchronous bilingual localization without string hardcoding (`locales/en.ftl`, `locales/ru.ftl`);<br>   - Comprehensive test coverage for Excel parsing in `statcraft_io`, command execution in `statcraft_syntax`, and session lifecycle integration.</p><p>---</p><h3>Final Phase: Seamless File Menu Integration, Save Dialog Guard &amp; Global Shortcuts</h3><p>*Time: October 29, 2026, 22:45 (~20 minutes)*</p><p>Completed comprehensive end-to-end integration for the 12 File Menu operations within StatCraft (`crates/statcraft_app`):<br>1. **Window Close Interception &amp; Data Loss Prevention (Window Close Guard):**<br>   - Intercepted window close requests via `ctx.input(|i| i.viewport().close_requested())` when unsaved changes exist (`has_unsaved_changes() == true`);<br>   - Instantly canceled unprompted exit via `ctx.send_viewport_cmd(egui::ViewportCommand::CancelClose)`;<br>   - Triggered canonical modal `ConfirmSaveDialog` while capturing the requested deferred action in `pending_session_action`;<br>   - Full support for actions: `[ Save ]` (persists changes to `.stc` / `.csv` before proceeding), `[ Don&#39;t Save ]` (discards changes and executes deferred action), and `[ Cancel ]` (retains changes and aborts transition).<br>2. **Global Keyboard Accelerators:**<br>   - Universal shortcuts accessible across all active application panes:<br>     * `Ctrl+Shift+N` — New Project (`NewProject`);<br>     * `Ctrl+N` — New Dataset (`NewDataset`);<br>     * `Ctrl+O` — Open Data (`open_data_dialog` supporting `.stc`, `.sav`, `.zsav`, `.csv`, `.xlsx`);<br>     * `Ctrl+Shift+O` — Open StatCraft Project (`open_project_dialog`);<br>     * `Ctrl+S` — Save Project (`save_project`);<br>     * `Ctrl+Shift+S` — Save Project As (`save_project_as`).<br>3. **Repository Cleanliness &amp; Dialog Invariant Testing (DoD):**<br>   - Added headless regression test `test_headless_render_confirm_save_dialog` in `crates/statcraft_app/tests/dialog_invariants.rs` ensuring panic-free rendering and state compliance;<br>   - Ignored runtime `.statcraft/` session folders in `.gitignore`;<br>   - 100% pass across all 130+ workspace unit and integration tests with `-j 1` and complete pass on `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- ci` (`cargo fmt --check`, `clippy -D warnings`, `file-guard`, `design-guard`, `layers`, `parity`).</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 41: Full Project Workspace Persistence &amp; Restoration (.stc)</h3><p>*Time: October 29, 2026, 23:40 (~35 minutes)*</p><p>Implemented monolithic persistence of the complete StatCraft analytical workspace in the native `.stc` container format (analogous to `.psd` in Adobe Photoshop):<br>1. **L0 Project Container Extension (`statcraft_io::stc_codec`):**<br>   - Extended `StcContainer` with optional fields `output_viewer_json` and `syntax_text` preserving full backward compatibility (`Format Version 1`, `#[serde(default, skip_serializing_if = &quot;Option::is_none&quot;)]`);<br>   - Added constructor `StcContainer::with_project_data` for unified packaging of all session artifacts;<br>   - Guaranteed backward compatibility: legacy `.stc` files without viewer or syntax data load seamlessly without error.<br>2. **Output Viewer Serialization L6 (`statcraft_app::views::output_view`):**<br>   - Implemented `static_str_serde` module for safe deserialization of static localization keys (`&amp;&#39;static str` via `Box::leak`);<br>   - Full serialization support across all 19 `OutputItemKind` variants (descriptive statistics, frequency tables, t-tests, ANOVA, crosstabs, correlations, non-parametric tests, linear regression, reliability analysis, factor analysis, means, execution logs, notes, warnings, and dataset summaries);<br>   - Added `OutputViewerState::to_json()` and `OutputViewerState::load_from_json()` with automated `next_id = max(id) + 1` recalculation preventing identifier collisions during subsequent computations.<br>3. **L1 Core Bridge (`statcraft_core::stc_codec`):**<br>   - Implemented `project_to_stc`, `save_project_stc_to_path`, and `load_project_stc_from_path` coordinating dataset raw tables, metadata dictionary, and application project components.<br>4. **Session Lifecycle Integration L6 (`statcraft_app::app_session`):**<br>   - In `save_to_path`: saving `.stc` captures the right-hand Output Viewer procedures and active syntax script;<br>   - In `load_file_from_path`: opening an `.stc` restores 100% of the analytical space — raw data table, variable dictionary, active case filter, weights, split file configuration, all output procedures/pivot tables, and syntax editor script;<br>   - Strict menu decoupling: `File -&gt; Save Data As...` excludes `.stc` and exports only tabular data (`.csv` / `.tsv`), while `File -&gt; Save Project` (`Ctrl+S`) and `File -&gt; Save Project As...` (`Ctrl+Shift+S`) persist the complete monolithic workspace.<br>5. **Quality Control &amp; Definition of Done:**<br>   - Added end-to-end integration test `test_save_and_load_full_project_with_output_and_syntax` in `session_lifecycle_tests.rs`;<br>   - Full workspace test suite `cargo test --workspace -j 1` passing with 0 failures;<br>   - Complete CI quality gate passed: `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- ci` (`file-guard`, `design-guard`, `layers`, `parity`, `clippy -D warnings`, `cargo fmt --check`).</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 42: Toolbar Save Action, Saved State Checkpoint (SavedCheckpoint) &amp; Status Indication</h3><p>*Time: October 30, 2026, 05:35 (~25 minutes)*</p><p>Resolved lifecycle defects in project persistence, dirty state synchronization, and user feedback:<br>1. **Toolbar Action Dispatching L6 (`crates/statcraft_app/src/app.rs`):**<br>   - Implemented `ToolbarAction::SaveData`: clicking the diskette icon on the main toolbar now triggers `self.save_project()`, presenting a save dialog or updating the active `.stc` project file;<br>   - Implemented `ToolbarAction::Redo` dispatching to `ds.redo()`, dynamically synchronizing `can_redo` availability with `ds.delta.redo_stack`.<br>2. **Saved State Checkpoint `SavedCheckpoint` (`crates/statcraft_app/src/app_session.rs`):**<br>   - Designed a lightweight `SavedCheckpoint` tracking document state (column and row counts, cell undo stack length `delta_undo_len`, command history length `command_history_len`, syntax text length `syntax_len`, and output viewer procedure count);<br>   - Added `saved_checkpoint: Option&lt;SavedCheckpoint&gt;` to `StatCraftApp`;<br>   - Refactored `has_unsaved_changes(&amp;self)` to evaluate current document deviation from `saved_checkpoint`: the dirty marker (`*`) in the window caption bar turns off immediately after saving and also when reverting changes via `Undo` (`Ctrl+Z`);<br>   - Automated checkpoint capture via `update_saved_checkpoint()` across `save_to_path`, `load_file_from_path` (supporting `.stc`, `.sav`, `.xlsx`, `.csv`), `execute_new_dataset`, `execute_new_project`, and `execute_close_project`.<br>3. **Status Bar Visual Feedback (`crates/statcraft_app/src/status_message.rs`):**<br>   - Added `StatusMessage::color(&amp;self) -&gt; egui::Color32`: save and export confirmations (`ProjectSaved`, `DataSaved`, `DataExported`, `OutputExported`) are rendered in `Tokens::MEASURE_NOMINAL` emerald green; error alerts in `Color32::from_rgb(235, 80, 80)`; standard operational status in `Tokens::TEXT_MUTED`;<br>   - Used `ui.colored_label(...)` in the bottom status panel for immediate peripheral recognition.<br>4. **Quality Control &amp; Definition of Done:**<br>   - Extended `test_has