nuous variable discretization algorithm `compute_visual_binning` and `compute_visual_binning_with_labels` based on a list of `Cutpoint` specifications (upper bound `upper_bound` and inclusion boundary `inclusive`);<br>   - Automated value labels generation according to SPSS conventions (`&quot;&lt;= 25000&quot;`, `&quot;25000 - 50000&quot;`, `&quot;&gt; 50000&quot;`);<br>   - Cutpoint generators for three canonical discretization strategies:<br>     - `generate_equal_width_cutpoints`: equal-width intervals with width $W = (max - min) / N$;<br>     - `generate_equal_percentile_cutpoints`: equal-percentile quantile binning (equal number of observations per bin) using the SPSS HAVERAGE percentile method;<br>     - `generate_stddev_cutpoints`: standard deviation intervals at $\pm 1\sigma, \pm 2\sigma$ around sample mean $\mu$;<br>   - 100% Safe Rust without `unwrap` in runtime code, safe preservation of missing cases `RawValue::Null`, and unit tests covering all methods and generators.<br>2. **Command Bus L5 (`statcraft_syntax::commands::binning_cmd`):**<br>   - Engine command `VisualBinningCommand` (`transform.visual_binning`) with JSON Schema `specs()`;<br>   - Creation and overwriting of numeric target variables with `Measure::Ordinal`, `DataType::Numeric { decimals: 0 }`, and attached `ValueLabels` dictionary;<br>   - Canonical SPSS syntax generation:</p><p><em>[code block — open in CapsuleCraft web for its canvas]</em></p><p>- Comprehensive `Undo` support (`Ctrl+Z`).<br>3. **DialogKit Desktop User Interface L6 (`statcraft_app::dialogs::binning_dialog` and `binning_cutpoints_dialog`):**<br>   - Canonical DialogKit modal dialog `VisualBinningDialog` (`DialogShell::standard`);<br>   - Left-hand variable picker `render_variable_list_panel`;<br>   - Right-hand control area: target variable name and label, upper endpoint inclusion radio buttons (*Included (&lt;=) / Excluded (&lt;)*), `Make Cutpoints...` subdialog trigger, manual cutpoint addition, and interactive `Cutpoint Grid` table with editable labels;<br>   - Subdialog `binning_cutpoints_dialog` (`DialogShell::subdialog`, `SubdialogActionBar`) for method selection and number of cutpoints;<br>   - Canonical Type 1 action bar `DialogActionBar` (`[ OK ] [ Paste ] [ Reset ] [ Cancel ] [ Help ]`);<br>   - Activated main menu item `menu-transform-visual-binning` (status `InDev` removed), integration in `app_dialogs_data.rs`, status bar feedback, and syntax logging to `Output Viewer`.<br>4. **Quality Control &amp; Definition of Done:**<br>   - 100% Safe Rust, 0 panics;<br>   - `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- layers` — 0 violations;<br>   - `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- file-guard` — all 232 files within size limits;<br>   - `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- design-guard` — all dialogs strictly conform to DialogKit;<br>   - `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- parity` — command registered;<br>   - `cargo test --workspace -j 1` — 100% passing tests across all crates;<br>   - `cargo clippy --workspace -j 1 -- -D warnings` — 0 warnings.</p><p>---</p><h3>Microplan #7: Replace Missing Values (RMV) — `transform.replace_missing`</h3><p>*Time: October 30, 2026, 09:15 (~30 minutes)*</p><p>Implemented the canonical IBM SPSS Statistics missing data imputation procedure — **Replace Missing Values...** (`Transform -&gt; Replace Missing Values...`, command ID `transform.replace_missing`):<br>1. **Mathematical Engine L2 (`statcraft_algo::replace_missing`):**<br>   - Implemented `impute_missing_values` supporting all five canonical SPSS imputation methods (`ImputationMethod`):<br>     - `SeriesMean` (SMEAN): imputes missing values with the mean of all valid cases in the series;<br>     - `MeanOfNearby(span)` (MEAN): mean of valid nearby values within window $[i - \text{span} .. i + \text{span}]$;<br>     - `MedianOfNearby(span)` (MEDIAN): median of valid nearby values within window $[i - \text{span} .. i + \text{span}]$;<br>     - `LinearInterpolation` (LINEAR): linear interpolation between preceding valid $(i_0, y_0)$ and succeeding valid $(i_1, y_1)$ values, with endpoint nearest-neighbor carry for edge missing cases;<br>     - `LinearTrendAtPoint` (TREND): linear regression trend $y = a + b \cdot x$ using case observation index $x_i = i + 1$;<br>   - Robust Never Crash protection: safe handling of edge missing cases, series consisting entirely of missing values, empty or single-element series using 100% safe Rust.<br>2. **Command Bus L5 (`statcraft_syntax::commands::replace_missing_cmd`):**<br>   - Engine command `ReplaceMissingCommand` (`transform.replace_missing`) with JSON Schema `specs()` for AI agents;<br>   - Appending new numeric columns (`DataType::Numeric { decimals: 2 }`, `Measure::Scale`) or replacing existing columns;<br>   - Canonical SPSS syntax generation:</p><p><em>[code block — open in CapsuleCraft web for its canvas]</em></p><p>- Comprehensive batch `Undo` support (`Ctrl+Z`) restoring original columns, metadata, and values.<br>3. **DialogKit Desktop User Interface L6 (`statcraft_app::dialogs::replace_missing_dialog`):**<br>   - Modal window designed according to DialogKit standards (`DialogShell::standard`, $560 \times 430$ px);<br>   - Left-hand source variable selection panel, central `TransferButton`, right-hand list of replacement rules `target -&gt; METHOD(source)`;<br>   - Variable name editing field with `Change` button, `GroupBox` method selection radio buttons, and integer `span` input for nearby point methods;<br>   - Canonical Type 1 action bar `DialogActionBar` (`[ OK ] [ Paste ] [ Reset ] [ Cancel ] [ Help ]`);<br>   - Main menu item `Transform -&gt; Replace Missing Values...` activated (status `[dev]` removed);<br>   - Bilingual Fluent localization (`dialog-missing-*`, `output-missing-executed`, `status-missing-executed` in `ru.ftl` and `en.ftl`).<br>4. **Quality Control &amp; Definition of Done:**<br>   - 100% Safe Rust, 0 panics, 0 `unwrap` in production code;<br>   - `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- layers` — 0 violations;<br>   - `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- file-guard` — all 232 files strictly within line limits;<br>   - `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- design-guard` — all dialogs strictly conform to DialogKit;<br>   - `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- parity` — command registered in parity registry;<br>   - `cargo clippy --workspace -j 1 -- -D warnings` — 0 warnings;<br>   - `cargo test --workspace -j 1` — 100% passing tests across the entire workspace.</p><h3>Microplan #10: Date and Time Wizard — `transform.date_time_wizard`</h3><p>*Time: October 30, 2026, 10:00 (~30 minutes)*</p><p>Implemented the canonical IBM SPSS Statistics date and time manipulation facility — **Date and Time Wizard...** (`Transform -&gt; Date and Time Wizard...`, command ID `transform.date_time_wizard`):</p><p>1. **Mathematical Core L2 (`statcraft_algo::date_time`):**<br>   - Module `crates/statcraft_algo/src/date_time.rs` (393 lines, strictly within the $\le 500$ lines limit);<br>   - Safe date and timestamp parsing without panics: supports ISO 8601, RFC 3339, `YYYY-MM-DD`, `DD.MM.YYYY`, `MM/DD/YYYY`, `YYYY/MM/DD`, formats with timestamps `HH:MM:SS`, and numeric unix timestamps or epochs;<br>   - Operation enum `DateTimeOperation`:<br>     - `ExtractPart(DatePart)`: extracts year (`Year`), month (`Month`), day (`Day`), hour (`Hour`), minute (`Minute`), second (`Second`), day of week (`DayOfWeek`, 1 = Sunday per SPSS standard), and quarter (`Quarter`);<br>     - `Difference { unit: DateUnit }`: computes exact calendar intervals between two dates in years, months, weeks, days, hours, minutes, or seconds;<br>     - `AddDuration { amount, unit }`: adds or subtracts time durations with automated leap-year adjustment (e.g., Jan 31 + 1 month = Feb 29 in a leap year);<br>     - `ConstructDate`: normalizes string or numeric data into standard canonical date format;<br>   - Full support for missing values (`RawValue::Null`) and unparseable input with null preservation and zero crashes.</p><p>2. **Command Bus L5 (`statcraft_syntax::commands::date_time_cmd`):**<br>   - Engine command `DateTimeWizardCommand` (`transform.date_time_wizard`) with JSON Schema `specs()` for MCP and AI agents;<br>   - Adds new columns with `Measure::Scale` and `DataType::Numeric` (for extracted parts and differences) or `DataType::Date` (for date outcomes);<br>   - Canonical SPSS syntax generation:</p><p><em>[code block — open in CapsuleCraft web for its canvas]</em></p><p>- Comprehensive batch `Undo` support (`Ctrl+Z`) restoring original columns and dictionary metadata.</p><p>3. **DialogKit Desktop User Interface L6 (`statcraft_app::dialogs::date_time_dialog`):**<br>   - Modal dialog constructed with `DialogKit` (`DialogShell::standard`, $560 \times 430$ px);<br>   - Header `GroupBox` for selecting the wizard task (Extract part / Calculate interval between two dates / Add or subtract duration / Convert to standard date);<br>   - Left-hand available variable panel `render_variable_list_panel`, adaptive `TransferButton`, slots for primary and secondary dates;<br>   - Dropdown selectors `ComboBox::from_id_salt` for extracted parts and time units, `DragValue` counter for duration amount, text inputs for target variable name and label;<br>   - Bottom Type 1 action bar `DialogActionBar` (`[ OK ] [ Paste ] [ Reset ] [ Cancel ] [ Help ]`);<br>   - Main menu item `Transform -&gt; Date and Time Wizard...` activated (status `[dev]` removed);<br>   - Synchronous bilingual Fluent localization (`dialog-datetime-*`, `status-datetime-executed` in `locales/en.ftl` and `locales/ru.ftl`).</p><p>4. **Quality Control &amp; Definition of Done:**<br>   - 100% Safe Rust, 0 panics, 0 `unwrap()` calls in production code;<br>   - `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- layers` — 0 architectural violations;<br>   - `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- file-guard` — all 237 files strictly within line limits;<br>   - `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- design-guard` — 100% DialogKit compliance;<br>   - `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- parity` — command registered in parity checklist;<br>   - `cargo test --workspace -j 1` — 100% passing test suite across all workspace crates and invariant tests.</p><p>---</p><h3>Microplan #11: Optimal Binning — `transform.optimal_binning`</h3><p>*Time: October 30, 2026, 10:35 (~35 minutes)*</p><p>Implemented the supervised discretization procedure of continuous attributes from IBM SPSS Statistics — **Optimal Binning...** (`Transform -&gt; Optimal Binning...`, command ID `transform.optimal_binning`):</p><p>1. **Algorithmic Core L2 (`statcraft_algo::optimal_binning`):**<br>   - New module `crates/statcraft_algo/src/optimal_binning.rs` (289 lines, strictly $\le 500$ lines);<br>   - MDLP Discretization Algorithm (Minimum Description Length Principle, Fayyad &amp; Irani 1993):<br>     * Sorting of $(x_i, y_i)$ pairs by continuous feature $x$;<br>     * Entropy and Information Gain optimization: $\Delta Ent = Ent(S) - \frac{|S_1|}{|S|}Ent(S_1) - \frac{|S_2|}{|S|}Ent(S_2)$;<br>     * Minimum Description Length stopping rule: candidate cutpoint is accepted only when Information Gain exceeds model complexity threshold $\frac{\log_2(N - 1) + \Delta}{N}$;<br>     * Global Priority Queue to iteratively split intervals with maximal global gain while strictly enforcing `max_bins` (default 5, min 2);<br>     * Robust Never Crash handling of constant features, single-class targets, and missing values (`Null`);<br>     * Automated interval boundary labeling (`&lt;= bound`, `prev - curr`, `&gt; bound`) and `ValueLabels` dictionary generation.</p><p>2. **Engine Command Bus L5 (`statcraft_syntax::commands::optimal_binning_cmd`):**<br>   - Typed engine command `OptimalBinningCommand` (`transform.optimal_binning`) with JSON Schema `specs()` for MCP and AI agents;<br>   - Creation of new numeric columns with `Measure::Ordinal` and 0 decimals, attaching generated category labels `ValueLabels`;<br>   - Canonical IBM SPSS Statistics syntax generator:</p><p><em>[code block — open in CapsuleCraft web for its canvas]</em></p><p>- Full batch `Undo` support (`Ctrl+Z`) removing generated columns in reverse index order.</p><p>3. **DialogKit Desktop User Interface L6 (`statcraft_app::dialogs::optimal_binning_dialog`):**<br>   - Modal dialog constructed with `DialogKit` (`DialogShell::standard`, $560 \times 430$ px);<br>   - Left-hand source variable picker `render_variable_list_panel`;<br>   - Vector adaptive `TransferButton` buttons for variables to bin and the categorical guide variable;<br>   - Right-hand panel: variables list, guide variable slot with clear button, settings `GroupBox` with `max_bins` counter (2..20) and target prefix input (`OB_`);<br>   - Canonical Type 1 action bar `DialogActionBar` (`[ OK ] [ Paste ] [ Reset ] [ Cancel ] [ Help ]`);<br>   - Main menu item `Transform -&gt; Optimal Binning...` activated (status `[dev]` removed);<br>   - Handled in `app_dialogs_transform.rs`, status message `StatusMessage::OptimalBinningExecuted`, and log recording in `Output Viewer`.</p><p>4. **Architectural Decomposition for File Size Guard:**<br>   - Decomposed `StatCraftApp` menu rendering into an isolated package `crates/statcraft_app/src/app_menus/` (`mod.rs`, `file_edit_view.rs`, `data_transform.rs`, `analyze_etc.rs`), reducing `app.rs` from 1557 to 585 lines (below the 1500 ceiling);<br>   - Decomposed `date_time_dialog` into `date_time_dialog/` (`mod.rs`, `view.rs`), satisfying the $\le 500$ lines limit.</p><p>5. **Quality Control &amp; Definition of Done:**<br>   - 100% Safe Rust, 0 panics and 0 unwraps in application code;<br>   - `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- layers` — 0 violations;<br>   - `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- file-guard` — all 245 files strictly within line limits;<br>   - `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- design-guard` — 100% DialogKit compliance;<br>   - `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- parity` — 51 documented commands;<br>   - `cargo clippy --workspace -j 1 -- -D warnings` — 0 warnings;<br>   - `cargo test --workspace -j 1` — 100% passing test suite across the entire workspace.</p><p>---</p><h3>Version 0.2.0: Multi-Platform Binary Builds Across All OSes (Windows, Linux, macOS)</h3><p>*Time: October 30, 2026, 14:15 (~15 minutes)*</p><p>Released version **0.2.0** and configured an automated CI/CD pipeline for building desktop release distributions across all key platforms:</p><p>1. **Ecosystem Version Bump to 0.2.0:**<br>   - Updated workspace root `Cargo.toml`: `version = &quot;0.2.0&quot;`;<br>   - Updated crates `statcraft_reporting` and `xtask` to inherit `version.workspace = true`;<br>   - Synchronized package metadata across all workspace members.</p><p>2. **Cross-Platform GitHub Actions Release Workflow (`.github/workflows/release.yml`):**<br>   - Configured matrix builds for both portable archives and native system installers across all target environments:<br>     * **Windows x64** (`windows-latest`, `x86_64-pc-windows-msvc`): portable archive `statcraft-windows-x64.zip` and full Inno Setup installer `statcraft-windows-x64-installer.exe` (`packaging/windows/installer.iss`);<br>     * **Linux x64** (`ubuntu-22.04`, `x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu`): portable archive `statcraft-linux-x64.tar.gz` and Debian/Ubuntu installer package `statcraft-linux-x64.deb` with application menu integration (`packaging/linux/statcraft.desktop`);<br>     * **macOS Apple Silicon** (`macos-latest`, `aarch64-apple-darwin`): portable archive `statcraft-macos-arm64.tar.gz` and mountable DMG image `statcraft-macos-arm64.dmg` with `StatCraft.app` bundle (`packaging/macos/Info.plist`);<br>     * **macOS Intel** (`macos-13`, `x86_64-apple-darwin`): portable archive `statcraft-macos-x64.tar.gz` and mountable DMG image `statcraft-macos-x64.dmg`;<br>   - All bundles are packaged with external Fluent translation catalogs (`locales/`), documentation (`README.md`, `README.ru.md`), and license `LICENSE-MIT`;<br>   - Enhanced `statcraft_i18n` with automatic runtime locale discovery for Linux system paths (`/usr/share/statcraft/locales`) and macOS app bundles (`Contents/Resources/locales`);<br>   - Automated