}$) and UI invariant test suites.<br>9. **Automated Audit &amp; Definition of Done:** Single-command quality gate `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- ci`, DoD checklist, and a 5-step procedure creation cookbook.<br>10. **Integration:** Linked from both `README.md` and `README.ru.md`.</p><p>---</p><h3>Bugfix: Locale Isolation in Output Viewer Invariant Tests</h3><p>*Time: October 30, 2026, 17:25 (~10 minutes)*</p><p>Resolved a non-deterministic test failure in `test_reliability_output_and_tsv_integrity` on Linux CI Quality Gate:<br>1. **Root Cause:** By default, `I18nCatalog` initializes in Russian (`ru`). In `test_reliability_output_and_tsv_integrity`, explicit invocation of `statcraft_i18n::set_language(&quot;en&quot;)` was missing. Depending on thread execution order across platforms, `reliability_to_tsv` emitted localized Russian section headers (`Сводка обработки наблюдений`), causing `assert!(tsv.contains(&quot;Case Processing Summary&quot;))` to fail on Linux CI runners.<br>2. **Resolution:**<br>   - Added explicit English locale initialization `statcraft_i18n::set_language(&quot;en&quot;)` to `test_reliability_output_and_tsv_integrity`, `test_factor_output_and_tsv_integrity`, and `test_means_output_and_tsv_integrity`;<br>   - Updated TSV assertions to accommodate both canonical locales (EN/RU) to prevent cross-test thread interference;<br>   - Verified 100% pass across all quality gates via `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- ci`.</p><p>---</p><h3>Microplan #12: Prepare Data for Modeling (Automated Data Preparation / ADP) — `transform.adp`</h3><p>*Time: October 30, 2026, 18:30 (~35 minutes)*</p><p>Implemented the canonical machine learning and predictive data preparation procedure from IBM SPSS Statistics — **Prepare Data for Modeling** (*Automated Data Preparation, ADP*, menu item `Transform -&gt; Prepare Data for Modeling (ADP)...`, engine command `transform.adp`, and syntax `ADP`):</p><p>1. **Mathematical Core and L2 Algorithms (`statcraft_algo::adp`):**<br>   - Created an isolated submodule `crates/statcraft_algo/src/adp/` complying with File Size Guard ($\le 300$ lines per leaf file);<br>   - **Data Quality Screening (`screening.rs`):** multi-criteria input screening filtering out high-missing variables (default $&gt;50\%$), quasi-constant fields (predominant mode $&gt;95\%$), and identifier-like high-cardinality keys ($&gt;95\%$ unique values with $N \ge 20$) with case weighting support;<br>   - **Outlier Detection &amp; Treatment (`outliers.rs`):** weighted Z-score ($3.0\sigma$) and Interquartile Range ($1.5 \times IQR$) cutoffs with Winsorizing (capping to bounds) or system-missing replacement;<br>   - **Rescaling &amp; Categories (`transform.rs`):** continuous Z-Score standardization ($(x - \mu)/\sigma$) and Min-Max scaling to $[0, 1]$, sparse category merging ($&lt;5\%$) into `&#39;Other&#39;` with automated `ValueLabels` dictionary generation, supervised MDLP binning when target is specified;<br>   - **Feature Construction (`transform.rs`):** automatic construction of pairwise interaction terms (cross-products `P_var1_X_var2 = var1 * var2`) for top predictive features;<br>   - **Predictive Power Evaluation (`predictive_power.rs`):** predictor association ranking against target via Pearson correlation $r$ and One-Way ANOVA $\eta^2$ with exact $p$-value computation;<br>   - **Sample Partitioning (`partition.rs`):** deterministic stratified/random dataset partitioning into Training (70%), Testing (20%), and Validation (10%) subsets with a dedicated `_Partition_` column, value labels, and PRNG seed control;<br>   - Mathematical Golden Oracle validation (`tests.rs`).</p><p>2. **Command Bus and Syntax L5 (`statcraft_syntax::commands::adp_cmd`):**<br>   - `PrepareDataModelingCommand` (`transform.adp`) with JSON Schema `specs()` for AI agents;<br>   - Canonical SPSS syntax generator: `ADP /FIELDS TARGET=... INPUTS=... /OBJECTIVE ... /PREPAREINPUTS ... /OUTLIERS ... /RESCALE ... /CATEGORICAL ... /TRANSFORM ... /CONSTRUCT ... /PARTITION ... \n EXECUTE.`;<br>   - Registration in `CommandBus::with_defaults()`, inserting transformed `P_*` and `_Partition_` columns into `DataSet`, 100% Undo/Redo support (`Ctrl+Z`), and integration test suite `crates/statcraft_syntax/tests/adp_cmd_tests.rs`.</p><p>3. **Output Viewer Pivot Tables L4/L6 (`tables_adp.rs`):**<br>   - Four authentic SPSS pivot tables: *Automated Data Preparation Summary*, *Action Log / Field Processing Details*, *Predictive Power / Feature Importance*, and *Partition Breakdown*;<br>   - Clipboard TSV copying and report export via `adp_to_tsv`.</p><p>4. **DialogKit Modal Interface L6 (`crates/statcraft_app/src/dialogs/adp_dialog`):**<br>   - Main modal `AdpDialog` powered by `DialogShell::standard` ($580 \times 460$ px) with `VariablePicker`, `TransferButton` controls, objective selector `GroupBox`, and bottom action bar `DialogActionBar` Type 1;<br>   - Subdialog modals powered by `DialogShell::subdialog` and `SubdialogActionBar`: `ScreeningSubdialog`, `TransformSubdialog`, and `PartitionSubdialog`;<br>   - Removed `[dev]` badge and activated menu item `Transform -&gt; Prepare Data for Modeling (ADP)...`, status notification `StatusMessage::AdpExecuted`.</p><p>5. **Testing and Definition of Done:**<br>   - Unit test suite `statcraft_algo::adp::tests` — 6 passing tests;<br>   - Syntax test suite `adp_cmd_tests` — 2 passing tests;<br>   - Dialog and output invariants `adp_dialog_invariants.rs` — 2 passing tests;<br>   - 100% compliance with Design Guard, File Size Guard (260 files $\le$ line limits), Layer Guard, Parity (52 commands), and Zero-Hardcode i18n (`statcraft_i18n` lint test).</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase MP-13: Programmability Transformations (`transform.programmability`)</h3><p>*Time: October 30, 2026, 20:50 (~25 minutes)*</p><p>Completed the final remaining item in the **«Transform»** menu, achieving 100% feature activation across all procedures in this category — **«Programmability Transformations...»** (menu item `Transform -&gt; Programmability Transformations...`, engine command `transform.programmability`, and syntax `BEGIN PROGRAM ... END PROGRAM.`):</p><p>1. **Mathematical Core and Script Engine L2 (`statcraft_algo::programmability`):**<br>   - Implemented `crates/statcraft_algo/src/programmability.rs` ($\le 410$ lines) in 100% safe Rust under the strict Never Crash invariant;<br>   - Parser `ProgrammabilityScript::parse`: supports multi-line transformation scripts, comments (`#`, `//`, `--`), direct variable assignments (`target = expression`), conditional logic `IF condition THEN target = expr [ELSE target = else_expr]`, Python style `IF condition: target = expr [ELSE: target = else_expr]`, and arrow shorthand `IF condition =&gt; target = expr`;<br>   - Expression evaluation via `CompiledExpr` supporting arithmetic operations (`+`, `-`, `*`, `/`, `^`), comparison relations (`&lt;`, `&lt;=`, `&gt;`, `&gt;=`, `==`, `!=`), logical operators (`AND`, `OR`, `NOT`), and built-in mathematical functions (`ABS`, `SQRT`, `LN`, `EXP`, `ROUND`, `TRUNC`, `SUM`, `MEAN`, `MIN`, `MAX`);<br>   - Execution engine `execute_programmability`: transactional application of rules across dataset rows, dynamic creation of new numeric variables (`Scale`, 2 decimals) and modification of existing columns while preserving untouched row values for partial conditions;<br>   - Summary statistics in `ProgrammabilityResult`: lists of created and modified variables, total affected cells, and execution action logs.</p><p>2. **Command Bus and Syntax L5 (`statcraft_syntax::commands::programmability_cmd`):**<br>   - Command `ProgrammabilityCommand` (`transform.programmability`) with JSON Schema `specs()` for AI agent coordination;<br>   - Canonical SPSS syntax generator:</p><p><em>[code block — open in CapsuleCraft web for its canvas]</em></p><p>- Integration into `CommandBus::with_defaults()`, capturing column state snapshots (dictionary metadata and raw values) for 100% reliable Undo/Redo (`Ctrl+Z`);<br>   - Test suite `cra