 (L0–L6), and Zero-Hardcode i18n (`statcraft_i18n`).</p><p>---</p><h3>Release v0.2.1: Mathematical Clean-Room Audit (Craft Anything) &amp; Transform Block Finalization</h3><p>*Time: November 1, 2026, 12:15 (~30 minutes)*</p><p>Prepared and published **StatCraft v0.2.1** for all supported operating systems (Windows, Linux, macOS ARM64/x64). This release consolidates the results of a rigorous evidence-based mathematical audit verifying full parity with the canonical IBM SPSS Statistics 24 algorithms, alongside finalization of the Transform procedures:</p><p>1. **Clean-Room Mathematical Audit via Craft Anything:**<br>   * Utilized the open-source MCP engine **[Craft Anything](https://github.com/storytold/craft-anything)** in strict `clean-room: true` mode to verify each mathematical formula in `statcraft_algo` against the *IBM SPSS Statistics 24 Algorithms Guide* (1,271 pp.);<br>   * Published synchronized bilingual audit documentation: primary English guide [`docs/SPSS_ALGORITHMS_AUDIT.md`](SPSS_ALGORITHMS_AUDIT.md) and Russian mirror [`docs/SPSS_ALGORITHMS_AUDIT_RU.md`](SPSS_ALGORITHMS_AUDIT_RU.md) with header language switches;<br>   * Verified 100% formula equivalence with Golden Oracle precision $\le 10^{-6}$ across all 5 procedure blocks:<br>     1. *Descriptives &amp; Basic Statistics:* Spicer provisional moments, Bliss sample kurtosis, HAVERAGE quartiles, Yates correction, Pearson $\chi^2$, Fisher&#39;s exact test, ANOVA $\eta^2$;<br>     2. *Mean Comparisons:* Mean-centered Levene test, Student&#39;s $t$, Welch&#39;s $t$ with Satterthwaite fractional $df$, paired $t$-test, One-Way ANOVA;<br>     3. *Associations &amp; Multivariates:* Pearson, Spearman, Kendall $\tau_b$ with full tie adjustments, OLS/WLS regression, Tolerance/VIF, cyclic Jacobi eigensolver for PCA, Bartlett sphericity, KMO measure, Cronbach&#39;s $\alpha$;<br>     4. *Nonparametric Tests:* Mann-Whitney $U$, Wilcoxon $W$, Kruskal-Wallis $H_{adj}$, Wilcoxon signed-rank test with tie-corrected variance, exact binomial Sign test;<br>     5. *Data Transformations:* Blom, Tukey, Rankit, Van der Waerden normal proportions, Acklam inverse normal CDF, MDLP entropy discretization (Fayyad &amp; Irani), linear interpolation and trend.</p><p>2. **Finalization of the Data Transformation Suite (`Transform`):**<br>   * Production activation of Automated Data Preparation (`adp`) and Programmability Transformations (`programmability`), removing all `[dev]` badges;<br>   * 100% coverage of the Transform menu with native DialogKit modal interfaces and Output Viewer pivot tables.</p><p>3. **Version Synchronization &amp; Multi-Platform Distribution:**<br>   * Version `0.2.1` synchronized byte-for-byte in `Cargo.toml`, `packaging/windows/installer.iss`, `packaging/macos/Info.plist`, and `packaging/linux/control`;<br>   * Added `*.pdf` rule to `.gitignore` preventing repository bloat from reference PDFs;<br>   * Automated GitHub Actions multi-platform release pipeline for Windows (ZIP + Inno Setup Installer), Linux (TAR.GZ + .deb), and macOS ARM64/x64 (TAR.GZ + DMG).</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase: Instrumental Clean-Room Core Audit via Craft Anything MCP (Blocks 7–10)</h3><p>*Time: November 2, 2026, 17:30 (~50 minutes)*</p><p>Executed a rigorous, line-by-line instrumental Clean-Room audit of the `statcraft_algo` core and `statcraft_syntax` command bus against the *IBM SPSS Statistics 24 Algorithms Guide* (1,271 pp.), recording full evidentiary proof into **Craft Anything MCP** (`hyp_1` through `hyp_15`):</p><p>1. **Block 7: Mathematical Expressions &amp; Evaluator (COMPUTE &amp; expr_eval):**<br>   * **Identified Divergences from IBM SPSS Canon:**<br>     1. *Exponentiation vs Unary Minus Precedence:* in SPSS, `**` binds tighter than unary minus (`-2**2 = -4`). In `parser.rs`, unary minus holds precedence 7 against 6 for exponentiation, yielding `(-2)**2 = +4`;<br>     2. *Logical NOT Precedence:* in SPSS, `NOT` is evaluated after relational operators (`NOT a = b` $\to$ `NOT (a = b)`). In `parser.rs`, `NOT` holds precedence 7 (above relational operators at 3), erroneously parsing as `(NOT a) = b`;<br>     3. *Kleene 3-Valued Logic (3VL):* in `mod.rs`, any `NaN` unconditionally short-circuits to `NaN` instead of following Kleene 3VL (`TRUE OR MISSING = TRUE`, `FALSE AND MISSING = FALSE`);<br>     4. *Functions:* `eval.rs` lacks trigonometric functions `SIN`, `COS`, `TAN`, modulo operator `MOD`, and SPSS alias `LG10`.<br>   * **Confirmed:** Dijkstra&#39;s Shunting-yard AST parser for basic arithmetic, safe `NaN` and divide-by-zero isolation (`Never Crash`), elementary functions `SQRT`, `EXP`, `LN`, `LOG10`, `ABS`, `RND`, `TRUNC`, and aggregates `SUM`, `MEAN`, `MIN`, `MAX`.</p><p>2. **Block 8: Time Series Transformations &amp; Case Shifts (DIFF, SDIFF, SMA, CSUM, LAG, LEAD):**<br>   * **Confirmed:** exact formula match for $\Delta^d X_t$ and $\Delta_s X_t = X_t - X_{t-s}$, `SYSMIS` cascade in `CSUM`, and shift operators `LAG(k)` and `LEAD(k)` with preservation of underlying data types (`hyp_4`, `hyp_6`, `hyp_7: supported`);<br>   * **Identified Divergence:** `SimpleMovingAverage(span)` in `time_series.rs` implements a trailing/prior window (known in SPSS as `PMA` — Prior Moving Average), whereas canonical SPSS `SMA(span)` computes a centered moving average (`hyp_5: refuted`).</p><p>3. **Block 9: Date &amp; Time Wizard (DATEDIFF, DATEADD, XDATE):**<br>   * **Confirmed:** exact calendar interval computation in `DATEDIFF` across completed calendar years and months with day-boundary adjustments, calendar-aware `DATEADD` with month-end day clamping (`checked_add_months`), component extraction `XDATE.*` matching Sunday = 1 canonical index in `XDATE.WKDAY`, and multi-format parsing for ISO 8601, European, American formats and unix timestamps (`hyp_8` .. `hyp_11: supported`). Continuous floating-point fractions noted for minutes and hours.</p><p>4. **Block 10: Recoding, Dummy Variables &amp; Value Counting:**<br>   * **Confirmed 100% Match to SPSS Canon:**<br>     * `RECODE` with deterministic declaration-order rule matching, ranges `low THRU high`, `LOWEST THRU`, `THRU HIGHEST`, `SYSMIS`, `MISSING`, `ELSE`, `COPY`, and `.sps` syntax round-trip (`hyp_12: supported`);<br>     * `AUTORECODE` with consecutive integer encoding $1..K$ and automatic `ValueLabels` dictionary synthesis (`hyp_13: supported`);<br>     * `CREATE DUMMIES` with indicator coding $\{0.0, 1.0\}$, column name sanitization, and the $K-1$ rule (`omit_first`) to eliminate multi-collinearity (`hyp_15: supported`);<br>     * `COUNT VALUES` with row-wise multi-column criteria summation (`hyp_14: supported`).</p><p>5. **Documentation Finalization &amp; Quality Control (DoD):**<br>   * Exported Craft Anything investigation report: [`docs/CRAFT_ANYTHING_AUDIT_REPORT.md`](CRAFT_ANYTHING_AUDIT_REPORT.md);<br>   * Synchronized bilingual audit specifications [`docs/SPSS_ALGORITHMS_AUDIT.md`](SPSS_ALGORITHMS_AUDIT.md) and [`docs/SPSS_ALGORITHMS_AUDIT_RU.md`](SPSS_ALGORITHMS_AUDIT_RU.md) with exact code references and documented divergences;<br>   * 100% pass across test suite: `cargo test --workspace -j 1`, `xtask file-guard` (267 files), `xtask layers` (L0–L6), `xtask design-guard`.</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase: Finalization of Phase 2 Clean-Room Core Audit via Craft Anything MCP (Blocks 11–14, Microplans M-09 through M-20)</h3><p>*Time: November 2, 2026, 18:20 (~35 minutes)*</p><p>Completed the comprehensive, line-by-line Clean-Room audit of all remaining StatCraft core modules and subsystems according to the Phase 2 Microplans Register (M-09 through M-20, Blocks 11–14). The entire evidentiary ledger is recorded in **Craft Anything MCP** (`hyp_16` through `hyp_32: supported`):</p><p>1. **Block 11: Programmability &amp; Random Number Generation (M-09, M-10):**<br>   * **M-09 (`programmability.rs`, `programmability_cmd.rs`):** line-by-line verification of expression assignments `VAR = EXPR` and conditional statements `IF COND THEN ... ELSE ...`. Verified statement atomicity, structured `ProgrammabilityResult` output, safe division-by-zero/missing mapping to `RawValue::Null` (`Never Crash`), and 100% Undo/Redo restoration via snapshots of overwritten and newly created columns;<br>   * **M-10 (`rng.rs`, `random_seed_cmd.rs`):** confirmed thread-safe atomic `GLOBAL_SEED` lifecycle, SPSS boundary validation $[1, 2\,000\,000\,000]$, `SET SEED = n`, and `SET SEED = RANDOM`. Noted modern 64-bit SplitMix64 PRNG ($2^{64}$ period, passes BigCrush) in `adp/partition.rs` replacing SPSS&#39;s 1970s LCG.</p><p>2. **Block 12: Data Management, Filtering, Subsets &amp; Metadata (M-11 — M-15):**<br>   * **M-11 (`select_cases_cmd.rs`, `dataset.rs`):** verified non-destructive `FILTER BY` via `active_row_indices(ds)` and destructive `SELECT IF` with 100% Undo table restoration. Synthesized `filter_$` variable with labels `Selected` / `Not Selected` fully confirmed;<br>   * **M-12 (`sort_cases.rs`, `sort_cases_cmd.rs`):** verified stable multi-key sorting. Missing value positioning invariant confirmed: `compare_raw_values` assigns `Ordering::Less` to missing values (smallest / $-\infty$), placing them at the beginning in ascending sort (A) and at the end in descending sort (D), exactly matching IBM SPSS canon;<br>   * **M-13 (`weight_cases_cmd.rs`, `dataset.rs`):** verified `ds.weight_var` binding. In `row_weight(r)`, cases with $w_i \le 0$, $w_i = \text{NaN}$, and filtered rows receive zero weight and are excluded from statistics;<br>   * **M-14 (`split_groups.rs`, `split_file_cmd.rs`):** confirmed combinatorial partitioning into `SplitSubgroup`, filter awareness, missing value isolation into `.` groups, and automated prepending of `SORT CASES BY ... (A)`;<br>   * **M-15 (`variable.rs`, `var_metadata_cmds.rs`):** confirmed model for all 11 canonical SPSS dictionary attributes, discrete and range `MissingValues`, and deterministic `ValueLabels`.</p><p>3. **Block 13: Input/Output Codecs (M-16 — M-19):**<br>   * **M-16 (`spss_loader/`):** confirmed decod