tiary ledger is confirmed and recorded in **Craft Anything MCP** (`hyp_33` through `hyp_45: supported`):</p><p>1. **Section E: Output Viewer &amp; Canonical Pivot Tables (M-21 — M-24):**<br>   * **M-21 (Base Statistics Output Tables):** confirmed SPSS canonical pivot tables model. Descriptives table (N, Min, Max, Mean, Std. Dev, Variance, Skewness, Kurtosis); Frequencies with the 4 standard columns (Frequency, Percent, Valid Percent, Cumulative Percent) and distinct sections for valid cases and Missing; Crosstabs with nested two-tier layout (Count, Expected Count, Row %, Col %, Total %, Residuals) and Chi-Square Tests table; probability formatting with leading zero suppression `&lt; .001` (`hyp_33: supported`);<br>   * **M-22 (Compare Means):** confirmed two-tier header for Independent Samples Test with Levene&#39;s Test ($F$, Sig.) and the two mutually exclusive canonical rows `Equal variances assumed` and `Equal variances not assumed`; 3 tables for Paired Samples Test (Statistics, Correlations, Test); 3-section One-Way ANOVA table (Between Groups, Within Groups, Total) (`hyp_34: supported`);<br>   * **M-23 (Advanced Statistics &amp; Nonparametric Suite):** confirmed correlation matrices with significance flags `*` and `**` and explanatory footnotes; linear regression 4-table block (Variables Entered/Removed, Model Summary, ANOVA, Coefficients with Beta, t, Sig., Tolerance, VIF); factor analysis (KMO and Bartlett, Communalities, Total Variance Explained, Component Matrix); reliability analysis (Cronbach&#39;s alpha, Item-Total Statistics); Mann-Whitney, Wilcoxon, and Kruskal-Wallis nonparametrics (`hyp_35: supported`);<br>   * **M-24 (Outline Tree Navigation &amp; Export):** document hierarchy Output Root $\to$ Procedure Node $\to$ Log (.sps) $\to$ Notes $\to$ Pivot Tables, smooth click-to-scroll navigation, context menu for copying TSV/text, and clean export to TSV, HTML, and Plain Text via `statcraft_reporting` (`hyp_36: supported`). 11/11 `output_viewer_invarian