`, `CROSSTABS`, `T-TEST`, `ONEWAY`, `REGRESSION`, `RELIABILITY`);<br>     2. `statcraft_load_dataset`: direct injection of raw tabular data (CSV/TSV text) into active memory without intermediate disk files;<br>     3. `statcraft_list_variables`: inspection of variable dictionary metadata (measures, types, labels, missing values);<br>     4. `statcraft_get_data_preview`: preview sample of the first $N$ rows for rapid distribution checks;<br>     5. `statcraft_insert_output_note`: insertion of formatted analytical findings and scientific conclusion cards into the Output Viewer tree;<br>     6. `statcraft_set_active_tab`: intentional tab switching (`data`, `variable`, `output`, `syntax`) without stealing user focus.<br>   - JSON-RPC 2.0 wire protocol over local TCP socket `127.0.0.1:18493` (Loopback);<br>   - Non-blocking socket listener with clean `AtomicBool` exit and guaranteed socket liberation upon `Drop`.</p><p>2. **Long-Running Service in App (`statcraft_app::bridge_service`):**<br>   - Dedicated `BridgeService` managing the server lifecycle within `StatCraftApp`;<br>   - Inter-thread channels (`BridgeAppRequest` and `oneshot` responders) bridging the TCP server thread to the UI frame loop in `update()`;<br>   - Direct execution via `syntax_runner::run_syntax_batch` and `DataSet::from_raw_table`;<br>   - In-memory ring buffer `BridgeLogRing` holding up to 100 entries with zero disk footprint.</p><p>3. **Interactive Semantic Activity Log &amp; Dialog (`dialogs/mcp_bridge_dialog`):**<br>   - Modular dialog built on canonical `DialogKit` (`DialogShell::standard`, `GroupBox`, `SubdialogActionBar`);<br>   - 100% vector-first UI: circular status indicator (`ui.painter().circle_filled`) with dynamic colors (emerald green / amber / gray) and zero Unicode tofu emojis;<br>   - One-click copy buttons for MCP configuration and agent Skill prompts;<br>   - Semantic live activity log: stores typed `BridgeLogEvent` variants, enabling on-the-fly bilingual translation of historical log entries via Fluent catalogs (`en.ftl` / `ru.ftl`).</p><p>4. **CLI Flag and Agent Assistant Skill:**<br>   - Added `--mcp` CLI flag to `main.rs`: `statcraft.exe --mcp` launches a lightweight stdio MCP proxy without initializing DirectX/GUI;<br>   - Authored system skill `.agents/skills/statcraft-assistant/SKILL.md` documenting agent workflows, syntax rules, and data auditing scenarios.</p><p>5. **Quality Control &amp; Definition of Done:**<br>   - 100% test pass across the entire workspace via `cargo test --workspace -j 1`;<br>   - Static architecture and design checks: `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- layers`, `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- file-guard` (289 files strictly within size limits), `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- design-guard`, and `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- parity`;<br>   - Strict compiler and linting gate: `cargo clippy --workspace -j 1 -- -D warnings` (0 warnings).</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 62: StatCraft Bridge v2 — Autonomous Code Mode, Output Return &amp; Dynamic Self-Documentation</h3><p>*Time: November 7, 2026, 12:00 (~50 minutes)*</p><p>Delivered a comprehensive architectural modernization of the StatCraft Socket Bridge (Bridge v2), transforming the bridge interface into an **autonomous Code Mode (SPSS Syntax REPL)**. External AI agents (Claude, Antigravity, local LLMs) are now 100% self-sufficient without access to Rust source code or manual documentation:</p><p>1. **Closing the Feedback Loop (Code Mode REPL Output Return):**<br>   - Extended the batch syntax execution engine `syntax_runner::run_syntax_batch` with `SyntaxBatchOutcome { count: usize, output_text: String }`;<br>   - Formatted all newly created procedures (SPSS Pivot Tables: ANOVA, Descriptives, Frequencies, T-Tests, Regression, Reliability) into clean monospace ASCII tables via `export_procedures_to_txt` and returned them directly in the text body of `statcraft_run_syntax`;<br>   - External agents immediately receive exact sample sizes, means, standard errors, Student&#39;s $t$ and Fisher&#39;s $F$ statistics, exact $p$-values, and confidence intervals in their conversation context.</p><p>2. **Dynamic Self-Documentation &amp; MCP Resources (Zero-Manual-Docs):**<br>   - Implemented syntax commands `HELP.` (general catalog of analytical procedure categories) and `HELP &lt;COMMAND&gt;.` (canonical syntax template, subcommands, and usage examples, e.g. `HELP ONEWAY.`);<br>   - Registered `HelpCommand` (`util.help`) in `CommandBus`, making syntax help accessible through both the parser and direct command execution;<br>   - Added native MCP Resources support to the stdio bridge server (`statcraft.exe --mcp`):<br>     - `resources/list`: exposes dynamic resource descriptor `statcraft://syntax-reference`;<br>     - `resources/read`: dynamically compiles comprehensive syntax and procedure manuals via `statcraft_syntax::generate_full_syntax_reference()` directly from the binary;<br>   - Intelligent Self-Correction: when encountering an unknown command or typo, the parser evaluates Levenshtein distance against known commands and suggests the closest valid procedure (`Did you mean &#39;ONEWAY&#39;? Type &#39;HELP.&#39; for available commands.`).</p><p>3. **SPSS Variable Dictionary Syntax Mappers (`variables.rs`):**<br>   - Implemented syntax mappers for dataset variable metadata management:<br>     - `VARIABLE LEVEL varlist (SCALE | ORDINAL | NOMINAL).` -&gt; `&quot;var.set_measure&quot;`;<br>     - `VARIABLE LABELS var &#39;Label&#39;.` -&gt; `&quot;var.set_label&quot;`;<br>     - `VALUE LABELS var code &#39;Label&#39;.` -&gt; `&quot;var.set_value_labels&quot;`;<br>     - `MISSING VALUES var (val1, val2) | (low THRU high).` -&gt; `&quot;var.set_missing_values&quot;`;<br>   - Upgraded core commands `SetMeasureCommand`, `SetLabelCommand`, `VarSetValueLabelsCommand`, and `VarSetMissingValuesCommand` to accept variable names (`var_name`, `variables`, `assignments`) alongside column indices.</p><p>4. **Statistical Procedure Mapping Fixes:**<br>   - `ONEWAY`: align