er schemas on the fly, eliminating the need to read or guess the codebase;<br>   - Added `CommandBus::find_by_syntax_keyword` for dynamic command resolution.<br>2. **Universal Code Mode (`statcraft_execute_command` &amp; `RUN COMMAND` Directive):**<br>   - Added universal execution tool `statcraft_execute_command` to the MCP bridge and IPC protocol: agents can invoke any engine command by `command_id` and JSON arguments with automatic parameter validation;<br>   - Added universal syntax directive in `SyntaxParser` and `SyntaxDispatcher`:<br>     `RUN COMMAND &quot;&lt;command_id&gt;&quot; { &lt;json_params&gt; }.` (with `CALL &quot;&lt;command_id&gt;&quot; { ... }.` alias);<br>   - Every newly registered `EngineCommand` becomes instantly executable both directly through MCP and inside batch `.sps` syntax scripts without requiring dedicated syntax mappers.<br>3. **Universal Output Viewer Renderer (Zero-Match Fallback):**<br>   - Replaced hardcoded `match parsed.name.as_str()` in `syntax_runner.rs` with an open two-tier rendering model;<br>   - Introduced `OutputItemKind::GenericReport` and isolated rendering module `tables_generic.rs`: arbitrary command results are automatically formatted into SPSS-styled summary tables and key-value cards, recorded into the `OutputViewer` tree, and streamed to `output_text` in bridge responses;<br>   - Synchronously updated Fluent localization catalogs `locales/en.ftl` and `locales/ru.ftl` with `output-generic-title` and `output-table`.<br>4. **Quality Control &amp; Definition of Done:**<br>   - 100% test pass across the workspace via `cargo test --workspace -j 1` (0 failures, 0 regressions);<br>   - Full pass of dialog and output viewer invariant suites: `cargo test -p statcraft_app --test dialog_invariants -j 1` and `output_viewer_invariants -j 1`;<br>   - Architecture and code guard verifications: `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- layers`, `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- file-guard` (295 files strictly within size limits), `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- design-guard`, and `cargo fmt --check`;<br>   - Strict compiler and linting gate: `cargo clippy --workspace -j 1 -- -D warnings` (0 warnings);<br>   - Localization linter pass: `cargo test -p statcraft_i18n -j 1` (4/4 passed).</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 64: System Language Auto-Detection &amp; Session Storage Persistence (Auto-Locale &amp; Storage Persistence)</h3><p>*Time: November 7, 2026, 15:50 (~40 minutes)*</p><p>Implemented seamless adaptation of the application to the user&#39;s OS language environment and guaranteed reliable persistence of user settings across restarts:<br>1. **System Language Auto-Detection (`statcraft_i18n::detect`):**<br>   - Added an isolated autodetection module `detect.rs` in `statcraft_i18n` adhering strictly to the `file-guard` limit ($\le 500$ lines);<br>   - Tiered cascade for OS language discovery:<br>     1. `STATCRAFT_LANG` environment variable (explicit process override for CI/headless runs);<br>     2. Native OS API call via cached `sys-locale` (`GetUserDefaultLocaleName` on Windows, `CFBundleCopyLocalizationsForPreferences` on macOS, POSIX API on Linux);<br>     3. Standard POSIX environment variables `LC_ALL`, `LC_MESSAGES`, `LANG`;<br>   - Added language tag normalizer `normalize_language_tag` stripping encodings (`.UTF-8`), modifiers (`@euro`), and country subtags (`-RU`, `_US` $\to$ `ru`, `en`, `de`);<br>   - Automatic activation of detected language during initial catalog setup `I18nCatalog::new_with_defaults()` with graceful international fallback to English (`en`) for non-Russian locales.<br>2. **Ensure Initialized Guard:**<br>   - Functions `set_language`, `current_language`, `available_languages`, `language_name`, `reload_locales`, `tr`, and `tr_args` now guarantee catalog initialization via atomic flag `INITIALIZED`, preventing multi-thread race conditions.<br>3. **Session State Persistence in `eframe::Storage`:**<br>   - Introduced persistent storage keys in `crates/statcraft_app/src/app.rs`:<br>     * `STORAGE_KEY_LANGUAGE = &quot;statcraft_language&quot;`;<br>     * `STORAGE_KEY_BRIDGE_AUTOSTART = &quot;statcraft_mcp_bridge_autostart&quot;`;<br>   - In `StatCraftApp::save`, serialized the current language and bridge autostart flag on window close and autosave ticks;<br>   - In `StatCraftApp::new`, restored the user&#39;s explicitly selected language (taking precedence over system autodetection) and bridge autostart flag (defaulting to `true` for seamless pairing with AI agents);<br>   - Created dedicated integration test `crates/statcraft_app/tests/storage_persistence_test.rs` using `MockStorage` validating persistence of language and bridge autostart across sessions.<br>4. **Quality Control &amp; Definition of Done:**<br>   - 100% test pass across workspace: `cargo test --workspace -j 1` (140+ unit and integration tests passing);<br>   - `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- layers`, `file-guard` (296 files), `design-guard` — 0 violations;<br>   - `cargo fmt --check` and `cargo clippy --workspace -j 1 -- -D warnings` — 0 warnings;<br>   - Optimized release binaries `target/release/statcraft_app.exe` and `target/release/statcraft.exe` compiled and synchronized.</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 65: Universal Theme System (Dark, Light, System)</h3><p>*Time: November 7, 2026, 16:40 (~45 minutes)*</p><p>Implemented complete theme system support across the application — **Dark (Dark Pro)**, **Light (SPSS Classic Light)**, and **System (System Auto)** with persistent storage and autonomous out-of-the-box styling for all future windows:<br>1. **High-Performance Lock-Free Theme Engine (`statcraft_app::theme`):**<br>   * Added `ThemeMode` enum (`Dark`, `Light`, `System`) with automated `serde` serialization/deserialization;<br>   * Developed academic `LIGHT_PALETTE` (SPSS Classic Light): pure white background `#FFFFFF`, soft gray panels/dialogs background `#F7F8FA`, high-contrast header gray `#E9ECEF`, subtle cyan selection `#DDF4FF`, and accent blue `#0969DA`;<br>   * Guaranteed WCAG AAA contrast ratio: primary text to background $\ge 15.6:1$ (exceeding AAA $7:1$), muted text $\ge 5.1:1$ (exceeding AA $4.5:1$);<br>   * Built on 100% Safe Rust without mutexes or `unsafe`: global atomic flag `IS_DARK_MODE: AtomicBool` with `Ordering::Relaxed` delivers zero-allocation, instant static reference access to `&amp;DARK_PALETTE` / `&amp;LIGHT_PALETTE` on the hot egui frame rendering path.<br>2. **Exhaustive Codebase Migration (Zero-Core Hardcoding for Themes):**<br>   * Migrated all static `Tokens::BG_*`, `Tokens::TEXT_*`, `Tokens::BORDER` constants to dynamic accessor methods `Tokens::bg_app()`, `Tokens::bg_panel()`, `Tokens::border()`, `Tokens::text_primary()`, etc.;<br>   * Updated all 53 application source files across the workspace (DataView, VariableView, Output Viewer, Custom Titlebar, Toolbar, DialogKit, and all 16 statistical procedure dialogs);<br>   * **Autonomy Principle:** Any future window or dialog built using `DialogKit` or `Tokens::*()` automatically adopts the active theme without modifying the theme engine.<br>3. **FPS Guard &amp; Preference Persistence:**<br>   * In `StatCraftApp::update`, `ctx.set_visuals` and `theme::set_dark_mode` calls are protected by `applied_dark_mode != Some(is_dark)` caching, eliminating redundant egui style invalidations and protecting FPS;<br>   * Theme configuration persists in `eframe::Storage` under `STORAGE_KEY_THEME = &quot;statcraft_theme&quot;` and seamlessly restores on relaunch;<br>   * Menu `View -&gt; Theme` activated from `MenuItemStatus::InDev` stubs to active `ui.selectable_label` toggles with 100% Fluent key coverage `t!(&quot;menu-view-theme-*&quot;)`.<br>4. **Quality Control &amp; Definition of Done:**<br>   * Unit tests `theme::tests::test_theme_mode_switching` and `theme::tests::test_wcag_contrast` verify runtime switching and mathematical WCAG compliance;<br>   * Integration test `test_theme_mode_persistence_serialization` validates `ThemeMode` serde roundtrips;<br>   * 100% workspace test suite 