t_align`, `var.set_label`, `var.set_measure`, `data.add_row`, and `data.delete_row`.<br>2. **Full-Featured Redo Stack &amp; History Management (`CommandBus`):**<br>   * Introduced `redo_stack`, `bus.redo(&amp;mut ds)`, `can_undo()`, `can_redo()`, wired to the application toolbar (`ToolbarAction::Redo`) and `Edit -&gt; Redo` menu;<br>   * **History Depth Ceiling:** Fixed a 100-step depth cap with automatic FIFO eviction (verified via a 120-operation stress test);<br>   * **Linear History Branching:** Executing a new mutating command after an undo operation strictly clears the redo stack;<br>   * **Interactive Cell Coalescence:** `execute_coalesced` merges rapid keystrokes within the same cell into a single history entry.<br>3. **Architectural Decomposition for File Size Guard:**<br>   * Extracted unit tests from `dataset.rs` into `dataset/tests.rs` (295 lines), bringing `dataset.rs` down to 713 lines ($\le 1000$ lines for GeneralModule).<br>4. **Testing, Audit Runner &amp; CI Quality Gate:**<br>   * Authored 38 modular matrix tests in `crates/statcraft_syntax/tests/undo_matrix/` (100% PASS);<br>   * Built `cargo xtask test-undo` runner and added it as quality gate #9 to `cargo xtask ci`;<br>   * Published comprehensive bilingual audit documentation in `docs/UNDO_REDO_AUDIT_REPORT.md` (EN) and `docs/UNDO_REDO_AUDIT_REPORT_RU.md` (RU).<br>5. **Quality Control &amp; Definition of Done:**<br>   * Complete CI gate `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- ci` passed cleanly (fmt, clippy, layers, file-guard [307 files], design-guard, full test suite, parity, corpus, test-undo).</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 68: Performance &amp; Memory Stress Benchmark (Extreme Scale &amp; Zero Memory Leaks)</h3><p>*Time: November 11, 2026, 17:45 (~35 minutes)*</p><p>Implemented a comprehensive stress-testing and benchmarking utility `cargo xtask bench-stress` to verify StatCraft&#39;s performance limits on large datasets (100,000 and 1,000,000 rows) and guarantee zero memory leaks:<br>1. **Synthetic Stress Dataset Generator (`xtask/src/bench_stress.rs`):**<br>   * Realistic multi-type dataset synthesis: continuous scales (`salary`, `prevas`, `postvas`, `perf_score`), ordinal scales (`educ`, Likert items `item1..item4`), nominal categories (`gender`, `jobcat`), text labels (`dept`), and 1% missing values;<br>   * Instantiated 2,000,000 cells (100k rows $\times 20$ columns) in **16.13 ms** (throughput ~124M cells/sec);<br>   * Instantiated extreme scale dataset of 20,000,000 cells (1M rows $\times 20$ columns) in **170.10 ms** (~320 MB RAM).<br>2. **UI Virtualization Stability (FPS Guard):**<br>   * Measured single frame rendering latency under simulated table scrolling via `ScrollArea::show_rows` across 100k and 1M rows;<br>   * Average frame rendering time: $6.42\text{ ms}$ on 100k rows and $6.40\text{ ms}$ on 1M rows (equivalent to **156 FPS**, exceeding the $\ge 60$ FPS requirement);<br>   * Confirmed $O(1)$ constant-time viewport rendering with zero frame rate degradation.<br>3. **Total Coverage of All 21 Statistical Procedures on 100,000 Rows:**<br>   * Basic Statistics: `DESCRIPTIVES` (55.3 ms), `FREQUENCIES` (76.0 ms), `CROSSTABS` (75.8 ms), `MEANS` (47.2 ms);<br>   * Compare Means: `ONE-SAMPLE T-TEST` (21.2 ms), `INDEPENDENT SAMPLES T-TEST` (37.7 ms), `PAIRED SAMPLES T-TEST` (35.2 ms), `ONE-WAY ANOVA` (47.6 ms);<br>   * Association &amp; Multivariate: `BIVARIATE CORRELATIONS` (91.7 ms), `LINEAR REGRESSION` (69.6 ms), `FACTOR ANALYSIS` (65.5 ms), `RELIABILITY` (75.6 ms);<br>   * Nonparametric: `MANN-WHITNEY U` (43.8 ms), `KRUSKAL-WALLIS H` (55.8 ms), `WILCOXON SIGNED-RANK` (36.9 ms), `SIGN TEST` (35.9 ms);<br>   * Transformations: `SORT CASES` (40.0 ms), `RANK CASES` (5.3 ms), `OPTIMAL BINNING` (29.9 ms), `COMPUTE VARIABLE` (4.9 ms), `ADP PIPELINE` (141.4 ms);<br>   * Every procedure completes in under 150 ms interactive response time.<br>4. **Memory Integrity &amp; Zero Leak Audit:**<br>   * 1,000 iterative cycles of `CommandBus::execute` $\to$ `undo` in the live