hms Guide*, resolved the 4 point divergences in Blocks 7 and 8 of the `statcraft_algo` and `statcraft_syntax` core:<br>1. **`COMPUTE` AST Operator Precedences (`parser.rs`, BUG-006):**<br>   * Configured the canonical SPSS Universals precedence hierarchy: exponentiation `**` (precedence 8, right-associative) binds tighter than unary minus/plus (precedence 7), ensuring `-2**2 == -4.0` and `(-2)**2 == 4.0`;<br>   * Relational operators `=`, `&lt;&gt;`, `&lt;`, `&lt;=`, `&gt;`, `&gt;=` (precedence 4) now precede logical negation `NOT` (precedence 3), parsing `NOT a = b` strictly as `NOT (a = b)`.<br>2. **Kleene 3-Valued Logic (3VL) under `NaN` (`mod.rs`, BUG-007):**<br>   * Removed blanket missing drops in Boolean binary operators;<br>   * Implemented strict Kleene 3VL short-circuiting: `TRUE OR SYSMIS` evaluates to `1.0` (even when the second operand is `NaN`), and `FALSE AND SYSMIS` evaluates to `0.0`.<br>3. **`COMPUTE` Math Functions &amp; Strict `MEAN` (`eval.rs`, BUG-008):**<br>   * Added trigonometric functions `SIN`, `COS`, `TAN` (evaluating to `NaN` at points of discontinuity) and remainder `MOD(x, y)` with zero-division safeguard;<br>   * Supported canonical SPSS alias `LG10` for `LOG10`;<br>   * Implemented strict canonical `MEAN(x1..xk)` mode — requiring all arguments to be valid unless a `.n` suffix is explicitly specified.<br>4. **Centered Moving Average `SMA` &amp; Separation with `PMA` (`time_series.rs`, `time_series_cmd.rs`, BUG-009):**<br>   * Refactored `SimpleMovingAverage` (`SMA`) to the canonical centered SPSS algorithm: symmetric window $[t - m \dots t + m]$ for odd $k = 2m + 1$, and endpoint-halved weights (0.5 on boundaries) for even $k = 2m$, with boundaries $t &lt; m$ and $t \ge N - m$ assigned to `Null`;<br>   * Trailing moving average over $[t - span + 1 \dots t]$ separated into dedicated `PriorMovingAverage` (`PMA`) function;<br>   * Updated `CREATE` syntax command to support both `SMA(var, span)` and `PMA(var, span)`.<br>5. **Quality Control &amp; Audit Clearance (DoD):**<br>   * Registered and resolved issues `BUG-006` through `BUG-009` in `docs/BUGS_AND_ISSUES.md`;<br>   * Audit registries `docs/SPSS_ALGORITHMS_AUDIT.md` and `docs/SPSS_ALGORITHMS_AUDIT_RU.md` updated: all 14 blocks upgraded to **100% Verified (0 Divergences)**;<br>   * All 314 workspace files adhere to size limits (`cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- file-guard`);<br>   * 100% test pass on full workspace suite (`cargo test --workspace -j 1`).</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 72: Exploratory Data Analysis (EXAMINE / Explore &amp; Normality Tests — Branch C)</h3><p>*Time: November 12, 2026, 00:55 (~50 minutes)*</p><p>In strict accordance with the *IBM SPSS Statistics 24 Algorithms Guide* and the evidence-backed Craft Anything MCP protocol, fully implemented the `EXAMINE` / `EXPLORE` exploratory data analysis procedure:<br>1. **Mathematical Core L2 (`crates/statcraft_algo/src/explore/`):**<br>   * **5% Trimmed Mean:** canonical SPSS algorithm trimming exactly $0.05 \cdot N$ observations from each tail with fractional boundary weighting of $(1 - r)$;<br>   * **Shapiro-Wilk $W$ Normality Test (`normality_sw.rs`):** Royston (1992) polynomial approximations for $3 \le N \le 5000$, Blom normal order statistics scores, exact $p$-value for $N=3$ via arcsine, and $z$-transforms for $4 \le N \le 11$ and $12 \le N \le 5000$. Verified against the Golden Oracle (`scipy.stats.shapiro`) with tolerance $\le 10^{-6}$ ($W = 0.970165$, $p = 0.8924$);<br>   * **Lilliefors Kolmogorov-Smirnov Test (`normality_ks.rs`):** Dallal-Wilkinson significance approximation with canonical SPSS bounds $[0.001, 0.20]$ and footnote `*. This is a lower bound of the true significance`;<br>   * **Extreme Values (`extremes.rs`):** 5 lowest and 5 highest values retaining original 1-based case row numbers and handling ties;<br>   * **Procedure Coordinator (`mod.rs`):** descriptive metrics ($IQR$ via HAVERAGE, skewness, kurtosis, 95% mean CI), factor grouping (`BY factor`), listwise/pairwise missing value treatment.<br>2. **Syntax Engine L5 (`crates/statcraft_syntax/`):**<br>   * Implemented `ExploreCommand` (`stat.explore`) with `specs()` JSON schema, `EXAMINE` and `EXPLORE` syntax identifiers, and `to_sps()` syntax generator;<br>   * Parser in `mappers/stats.rs`: mapping subcommands `VARIABLES=... BY ...`, `/PLOT NPPLOT`, `/STATISTICS DESCRIPTIVES EXTREME`, `/MISSING PAIRWISE/LISTWISE`;<br>   * Integration roundtrip test `test_roundtrip_explore` via `SyntaxDispatcher::execute_batch`.<br>3. **Output Viewer Tables L4/L6 (`crates/statcraft_app/src/views/output_view/tables_explore/`):**<br>   * Architecturally decomposed into `mod.rs`, `tables.rs`, and `tsv.rs`, strictly maintaining $\le 500$ lines per file;<br>   * Rendered 4 authentic SPSS Pivot Tables: *Case Processing Summary*, *Descriptives*, *Tests of Normality*, *Extreme Values*;<br>   * Added TSV export (`explore_to_tsv`) for reporting and clipboard copy.<br>4. **DialogKit UI (`crates/statcraft_app/src/dialogs/explore_dialog.rs`):**<br>   * Canonical SPSS dialog based on `DialogShell::standard(560, 430)`:<br>     - Left panel `VariablePicker` with measurement scale indicators;<br>     - `TransferButton` controls for Dependent List and Factor List;<br>     - `SubdialogSidebar` panels: Statistics, Plots (normality tests), Options (missing cases);<br>     - Bottom `DialogActionBar` (`[ OK ] [ Paste ] [ Reset ] [ Cancel ] [ Help ]`);<br>   * Main menu activation: &quot;Analyze -&gt; Descriptive Statistics -&gt; Explore...&quot; (`menu-analyze-explore`).<br>5. **Localization &amp; Quality Control (DoD):**<br>   * 100% bilingual Fluent catalogs in `locales/en.ftl` and `locales/ru.ftl` with 0 raw strings and 0 emojis;<br>   * Interface invariant suite `crates/statcraft_app/tests/explore_invariants.rs`;<br>   * 100% successful pass across all 9 Quality Gate stages via `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- ci` (fmt, clippy, layers, file-guard [325 files], design-guard, workspace tests, parity, test-corpus, test-undo).</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 73: Advanced Regression &amp; Partial Correlations (PARTIAL CORR, LOGISTIC REGRESSION, CURVEFIT — Branch feat/001-advanced-regression)</h3><p>*Time: November 14, 2026, 21:30 (~60 minutes)*</p><p>Following the approved architectural plan `plan_1_regression_and_correlations.md` and in strict accordance with the *IBM SPSS Statistics 24 Algorithms Guide*, ArtCraft ecosystem canon, and the evidence-backed Craft Anything MCP protocol, fully implemented three major analytical procedures:<br>1. **Partial Correlations (`PARTIAL CORR` / `stat.correlations.partial`):**<br>   * **Mathematical Core L2 (`crates/statcraft_algo/src/partial_corr/`):** Decomposed into `math.rs`, `listwise.rs`, `pairwise.rs`, `types.rs`, `tests.rs`. Implemented symmetrized Schur complement for the residual covariance matrix $S = R_{XX} - R_{XZ} R_{ZZ}^{-1} R_{ZX}$, degrees of freedom $df = N - k - 2$, and exact two-tailed/one-tailed Student&#39;s $t$ significance values.<br>   * **Golden Oracle:** Verified against Python `scipy.stats` with diff $&lt; 10^{-12}$ ($r = -0.1719967316$).<br>2. **Binary Logistic Regression (`LOGISTIC REGRESSION` / `stat.regression.logistic`):**<br>   * **Mathematical Core L2 (`crates/statcraft_algo/src/logistic/`):** Decomposed into `engine.rs`, `diagnostics.rs`, `types.rs`, `math.rs`, `tests.rs`. Built an IRLS (Newton-Raphson) optimizer with adaptive diagonal Fisher matrix damping $\lambda = 10^{-11} \dots 10^{-5}$ to prevent singular matrix panics. Computed asymptotic covariance matrix, Wald statistic, 95% C.I. for $\text{Exp}(B)$, Cox &amp; Snell and Nagelkerke pseudo-$R^2$.<br>   * **Goodness-of-Fit Diagnostics:** Implemented Hosmer-Lemeshow deciles of risk with $\chi^2$ and $df = g - 2$, and a $2 \times 2$ Classification Table (cutoff 0.5) with percentage correct.<br>   * **Golden Oracle:** Verified against Python `statsmodels.Logit` confirming identical coefficients, standard errors, Wald statistics, and log-likelihood.<br>3. **Curve Estimation Models (`CURVEFIT` / `stat.regression.curve`):**<br>   * **Mathematical Core L2 (`crates/statcraft_algo/src/curvefit/`):** Simultaneous estimation of 6 canonical SPSS regression curves (Linear, Logarithmic, Inverse, Quadratic, Power, Exponential) via analytical linearizations, computing $R^2, F, df_1, df_2, p, b_0, b_1, b_2$ and validated against SciPy/NumPy Golden Oracle.<br>4. **Engine Commands and Syntax Parsers L5 (`crates/statcraft_syntax/`):**<br>   * Implemented `PartialCorrCommand`, `LogisticRegressionCommand`, `CurveFitCommand` with parameter schemas `specs()`, syntax generators `to_sps()`, and syntax mappers in `mappers/advanced_regression.rs`;<br>   * Enabled compound keyword parsing for `PARTIAL CORR` and `LOGISTIC REGRESSION` in `parser.rs`.<br>5. **Output Viewer Pivot Tables &amp; Reporting (`crates/statcraft_app/src/views/output_view/`):**<br>   * Dedicated modules `tables_partial_corr.rs`, `tables_logistic.rs`, `tables_curvefit.rs` rendering authentic SPSS Pivot Tables (Omnibus Tests, Model Summary, Hosmer-Lemeshow, Classification Table, Variables in the Equation, Curve Estimation Parameter Estimates);<br>   * Full clipboard and document export support to TSV, HTML, TXT, and ReportDocument.<br>6. **DialogKit UI &amp; Application Menus L6 (`crates/statcraft_app/`):**<br>   * Modal dialogs `PartialCorrDialog`, `LogisticRegressionDialog`, `CurveFitDialog` built on canonical `DialogShell::standard(560, 430)` and `DialogActionBar`;<br>   * Central coordinator in `app_dialogs_advanced.rs`;<br>   * Enabled menu items: `Analyze -&gt; Correlate -&gt; Partial...`, `Analyze -&gt; Regression -&gt; Binary Logistic...`, and `Analyze -&gt; Regression -&gt; Curve Estimation...`.<br>7. **Quality Control &amp; Definition of Done (DoD):**<br>   * Interface invariant suites `advanced_regression_dialog_invariants.rs` and `advanced_regression_output_invariants.rs`;<br>   * 100% successful pass across all 9 Quality Gate stages via `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- ci` (fmt, clippy [0 warnings], layers, file-guard [355 files], design-guard, workspace tests, parity, test-corpus, test-undo).</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 74: General Linear Model (UNIANOVA, MANOVA &amp; Repeated Measures — Branch feat/002-general-linear-model)</h3><p>*Time: November 14, 2026, 22:35 (~65 minutes)*</p><p>Following the approved architectural plan `plan_2_general_linear_model.md` and in strict adherence to the ArtCraft ecosystem canon, Clean-Room guidelines, and the evidence-backed Craft Anything MCP protocol, fully implemented the **General Linear Model (GLM)** analytical suite:<br>1. **Univariate Analysis of Variance and Covariance (`UNIANOVA` / `stat.glm.univariate`):**<br>   * **Mathematical Core L2 (`crates/statcraft_algo/src/glm/`):** Decomposed into `design_matrix.rs`, `type3_ss.rs`, `univariate.rs`, `types.rs`. Constructs an orthogonal design matrix supporting factor deviation contrasts (sum-to-zero coding), continuous covariates, and two-way interaction terms $A \times B$.<br>   * **Type III Sum of Squares (Type III SS):** Marginal reduction of full model vs. term-excluded models via SVD-based pseudo-inversion (Jacobi SVD) to prevent collinearity issues. Computes $MS, F, p$, Partial $\eta^2$, alongside model fit indicators ($R^2$ and Adjusted $R^2$).<br>   * **Golden Oracle:** Validated against `statsmodels.api.stats.anova_lm(typ=3)` confirming exact match within $10^{-7}$.<br>2. **Multivariate Analysis of Variance (`GLM Multivariate` / `stat.glm.multivariate` — MANOVA):**<br>   * **Mathematical Core L2 (`crates/statcraft_algo/src/glm/multivariate.rs` and `eigen.rs`):** Multivariate extension supporting $p \ge 2$ dependent variables. Computes Error ($E$) and Hypothesis ($H$) Sum of Squares and Cross-Products matrices.<br>   * **Generalized Eigenvalue Decomposition:** Symmetrized $E^{-1/2} H E^{-1/2}$ decomposition via Jacobi method to extract eigenvalues $\lambda_i$.<br>   * **4 Canonical SPSS Test Criteria:**<br>     1. *Wilks&#39; Lambda* ($\Lambda = \prod \frac{1}{1 + \lambda_i}$) with Rao&#39;s exact $F$-approximation;<br>     2. *Pillai&#39;s Trace* ($V = \sum \frac{\lambda_i}{1 + \lambda_i}$);<br>     3. *Hotelling-Lawley Trace* ($T = \sum \lambda_i$);<br>     4. *Roy&#39;s Largest Root* ($\theta = \frac{\lambda_{\max}}{1 + \lambda_{\max}}$) with upper-bound $F$.<br>   * **Golden Oracle:** Validated against `statsmodels.multivariate.manova.MANOVA`.<br>3. **Repeated Measures Analysis of Variance (`GLM Repeated Measures` / `stat.glm.repeated`):**<br>   * **Mathematical Core L2 (`crates/statcraft_algo/src/glm/repeated.rs`):** Within-subjects factor ($k \ge 2$ repeated measures) with normalized Helmert contrast matrix of size $k \times (k-1)$.<br>   * **Mauchly&#39;s Test of Sphericity:** Computes $W = \frac{\det(C^T S C)}{(\text{tr}(C^T S C) / d)^d}$, approximate $\chi^2$, degrees of freedom $df = \frac{k(k-1)}{2} - 1$, and $p$-value.<br>   * **Epsilon Corrections to Degrees of Freedom:** Greenhouse-Geisser ($\hat{\varepsilon}$), Huynh-Feldt ($\tilde{\varepsilon}$), and Lower-bound ($1/(k-1)$) corrections with adjusted $df$ and $p$-values.<br>4. **Command Bus and Syntax Parser L5 (`crates/statcraft_syntax/`):**<br>   * Implemented `UnivariateGlmCommand`, `MultivariateGlmCommand`, `RepeatedGlmCommand` with parameter schemas `specs()`, canonical syntax generator `to_sps()` (`UNIANOVA`, `GLM ... /WSFACTOR = ... Polynomial`);<br>   * Syntax parser and mappers `mappers/glm.rs` recognizing `UNIANOVA`, `GLM`, and `GLM REPEATED`;<br>   * 100% reversible command history verified by `undo_redo_matrix_tests`.<br>5. **Output Viewer Pivot Tables and Architecture L4/L6 (`crates/statcraft_app/src/views/output_view/tables_glm/`):**<br>   * Modularized into `mod.rs`, `univariate.rs`, `multivariate.rs`, `repeated.rs` strictly respecting the $\le 500$ lines limit (Rule 12.2);<br>   * Renders 4 authentic SPSS Pivot Tables: *Tests of Between-Subjects Effects*, *Multivariate Tests*, *Mauchly&#39;s Test of Sphericity*, *Tests of Within-Subjects Effects*;<br>   * TSV export (`univariate_glm_to_tsv`, `multivariate_glm_to_tsv`, `repeated_glm_to_tsv`) for clipboard and Outline tree integration.<br>6. **DialogKit UI and Menu Integration L6 (`crates/statcraft_app/`):**<br>   * Canonical modal dialogs `UnivariateGlmDialog`, `MultivariateGlmDialog`, `RepeatedGlmDialog` based on `DialogShell::standard(560, 430)`, `VariablePicker`, `TransferButton`, and `DialogActionBar`;<br>   * Central coordinator in `app_dialogs_glm.rs`;<br>   * Activated menu items under `Analyze -&gt; General Linear Model -&gt; Univariate... / Multivariate... / Repeated Measures...` with `[dev]` badges removed.<br>7. **Localization and Quality Gate (DoD):**<br>   * 100% bilingual Fluent coverage in `locales/en.ftl` and `locales/ru.ftl` (passed `i18n_lint_test`, 0 raw strings, 0 emojis, Vector-First UI);<br>   * UI invariant suite `glm_dialog_invariants.rs`;<br>   * 100% successful pass across all 9 Quality Gate stages via `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- ci` (fmt, clippy [0 warnings], layers, file-guard [378 files], design-guard, workspace tests, parity, test-corpus, test-undo).</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 75: Clustering, Reports &amp; Survival Analysis (K-Means, Codebook, Summarize, Kaplan-Meier, Life Tables — Branch feat/003-clustering-reports-survival)</h3><p>*Time: November 15, 2026, 01:10 (~70 minutes)*</p><p>Following the approved architectural plan `plan_3_clustering_reports_survival.md` and in strict adherence to the ArtCraft ecosystem canon, Clean-Room principles, and the IBM SPSS Statistics Algorithms Guide, fully implemented the **Feature 003** analytical suite, providing five foundational statistical procedures across clustering, reporting, and biostatistical survival analysis:<br>1. **K-Means Cluster Analysis (`QUICK CLUSTER` / `stat.cluster.kmeans`):**<br>   * **Mathematical Core L2 (`crates/statcraft_algo/src/cluster_kmeans.rs`):** Deterministic center initialization using the Maximin (furthest point heuristic) algorithm, iterative reassignment cycle based on Euclidean distance, distance matrix between final cluster centers, and one-way ANOVA decomposition for each clustering variable ($SS_{between}, SS_{within}, F$-statistics, and exact Fisher $p$-values).<br>   * **Dynamic Column Generation &amp; 100% Reversible Undo/Redo L5 (`crates/statcraft_syntax/src/commands/kmeans_cmd.rs`):** When cluster saving is requested, dynamically creates and registers `QCL_1` (Cluster Membership, `Measure::Nominal`) and `QCL_2` (Distance from Cluster Center, `Measure::Scale`) in `DataSet` and `VariableDictionary`. The `undo()` execution cleanly removes these columns, restoring the exact previous state.<br>   * **Golden Oracle:** Validated cluster centroids and assignments against Python `scipy.cluster.vq.kmeans2` confirming precision $\le 10^{-6}$.<br>2. **Variable Codebook (`CODEBOOK` / `stat.reports.codebook`):**<br>   * **Mathematical Core L2 (`crates/statcraft_algo/src/codebook_core.rs`):** Extracts metadata properties (name, label, measurement level, format), constructs discrete frequency tables with counts, percentages, and valid percentages for categorical variables, and calculates descriptive statistics (Mean, StdDev, Median, Quartiles via SPSS HAVERAGE interpolation) for scale variables.<br>3. **Case Summaries (`SUMMARIZE` / `stat.reports.summarize`):**<br>   * **Mathematical Core L2 (`crates/statcraft_algo/src/summarize_core.rs`):** Row-by-row case listing with optional case limit truncation, factor-based hierarchical grouping with intermediate subtotals and grand totals ($N$, Mean, Sum, StdDev).<br>4. **Kaplan-Meier Survival Analysis (`KM` / `stat.survival.km`):**<br>   * **Mathematical Core L2 (`crates/statcraft_algo/src/survival_km.rs`):** Product-limit survival function $\hat{S}(t) = \prod (1 - d_i/n_i)$, Greenwood&#39;s standard error formula $\widehat{\text{Var}}(\hat{S}(t)) = \hat{S}(t)^2 \sum \frac{d_i}{n_i(n_i - d_i)}$, mean and median survival time estimation with 95% confidence intervals, and Mantel-Cox Log-Rank $\chi^2$ test ($df = G - 1, p$) for comparing survival distributions across strata.<br>   * **Golden Oracle:** Survival tables and log-rank statistics verified against Python `lifelines.KaplanMeierFitter` with precision $\le 10^{-6}$.<br>5. **Actuarial Life Tables (`SURVIVAL` / `stat.survival.lifetables`):**<br>   * **Mathematical Core L2 (`crates/statcraft_algo/src/survival_lifetables.rs`):** Actuarial analysis across specified time intervals $[t_k, t_{k+1})$, effective sample size under risk $n&#39;_k = n_k - w_k/2$, conditional mortality probability $q_k = d_k / n&#39;_k$, survival probability $p_k = 1 - q_k$, cumulative survival $P_k$, probability density of event $f_k$, and hazard rate $h_k$.<br>6. **Command Bus and Syntax Parser L5 (`crates/statcraft_syntax/`):**<br>   * Implemented engine commands: `KMeansClusterCommand`, `CodebookCommand`, `SummarizeCommand`, `KaplanMeierCommand`, `LifeTablesCommand` with complete `specs()` schemas and canonical `to_sps()` syntax generators;<br>   * Syntax parser support for compound keywords `QUICK CLUSTER`, `LIFE TABLES`, `KAPLAN MEIER` in `parser.rs` and mappers in `syntax_parser/mappers/pkg3.rs`;<br>   * Integration test suite in `feature_003_syntax_tests.rs`.<br>7. **Output Viewer Pivot Tables and Architecture L4/L6 (`crates/statcraft_app/src/views/output_view/`):**<br>   * Dedicated output rendering modules: `tables_cluster.rs`, `tables_reports.rs`, `tables_survival.rs` with SPSS canonical Pivot Table formatting and TSV clipboard export;<br>   * Architecture modularization of `views/output_view/mod.rs` by extracting `view.rs` to maintain strict compliance with the $\le 500$ lines limit (Rule 12.1 and 12.2 Anti-Goodhart Counterweight).<br>8. **DialogKit UI and Menu Integration L6 (`crates/statcraft_app/`):**<br>   * Canonical modal dialogs `KMeansDialog`, `CodebookDialog`, `SummarizeDialog`, `KaplanMeierDialog`, `LifeTablesDialog` utilizing `DialogShell::standard(560, 430)`, `VariablePicker`, `TransferButton`, and `DialogActionBar`;<br>   * Central coordinator in `app_dialogs_pkg3.rs` wired into `app.rs`;<br>   * Removed `[dev]` badges and enabled corresponding menu items under `Analyze -&gt; Reports`, `Analyze -&gt; Classify`, and `Analyze -&gt; Survival`.<br>9. **Localization and Quality Gate (DoD):**<br>   * 100% bilingual Fluent coverage in `locales/en.ftl` and `locales/ru.ftl` (passed `i18n_lint_test`, 0 raw strings, 0 emojis, Vector-First UI);<br>   * UI invariant suite `crates/statcraft_app/tests/feature_003_pkg3_invariants.rs`;</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 95: Eliminating Windows 10 Borderless Window Artifacts and Dialog Bloating Protection</h3><p>*Time: November 22, 2026, 01:15 (~35 minutes)*</p><p>Following the architectural plan `win10_csd_and_dialog_fix_plan.md`, successfully eliminated OS-level borderless window artifacts on Windows 10 and implemented robust protection against modal dialog bloating:<br>1. **Fixing the 26 px Black Bar and Mouse Offset on Windows 10 (BUG-017):**<br>   * Integrated safe Win32 API wrapper `winsafe = &quot;0.0.29&quot;` in `crates/statcraft_app/Cargo.toml` (100% Safe Rust without `unsafe` keywords in application code);<br>   * Implemented dedicated window frame guard `crates/statcraft_app/src/window_frame.rs` based on the proven PhotoCraft canon:<br>     - `strip(hwnd)`: dynamically strips `WS_CAPTION | WS_BORDER` styles forced by `winit` and triggers immediate non-client frame recalculation (`SWP_FRAMECHANGED`);<br>     - `keep_clear_of_the_taskbar(hwnd)`: prevents maximized borderless windows from slipping under the Windows taskbar, respecting both standard and auto-hiding taskbars;<br>     - Frame guard is initialized in `StatCraftApp::new` via safe HWND resolution (`EnumWindows`) and invoked each frame in `eframe::App::update`;<br>     - 100% preserves custom Client-Side Decoration (CSD) appearance while restoring 1:1 mouse hit-testing precision;<br>     - Added 7 unit tests for window frame geometry, all passing.<br>2. 