large external matrices;<br>   * **Auto-Fill Series (dragging Fill Handle):** computes linear progression slopes for numeric sequences (`[1, 2, 3] -&gt; [4, 5, 6]`) and cyclic repetition for text or categorical variables.<br>5. **Testing &amp; Quality Gate (DoD):**<br>   * Authored integration test suite `crates/statcraft_app/tests/grid_selection_clipboard_invariants.rs` (4 tests: `CellRange` normalization, roundtrip TSV copy/paste into `DataSet`, arithmetic auto-fill series, and editor lifecycle);<br>   * 100% successful pass across all CI Quality Gates via `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- ci` (fmt, clippy, file-guard [415 files], design-guard, workspace test suites, and 41-command Undo/Redo mathematical reversibility matrix).</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 79: Column AutoFilter, Quick Sort &amp; Data Integrity Guards (Feature 008)</h3><p>*Time: November 16, 2026, 06:20 (~40 minutes)*</p><p>Under Phase 3 of the table modernization roadmap (specification `specs/008-grid-autofilter-integrity`, branch `feat/008-grid-autofilter-integrity`), delivered a comprehensive suite of interactive filtering, rapid sorting, and automated data type integrity inspection tools in Data View:<br>1. **Column AutoFilter &amp; Dropdown Interface (`filter_menu.rs`, `dataset.rs`):**<br>   * Integrated an interactive filter button in variable column headers: displays a discrete vector chevron in the idle state and an accent filled funnel icon when a column filter is active (`paint_filter_button`);<br>   * Floating filter popup (`render_filter_popup`):<br>     - Quick sorting Ascending and Descending (A-Z, Z-A) dispatching `data.sort_cases` through `CommandBus` with full Undo/Redo reversibility and SPSS syntax parity (`SORT CASES BY ...`);<br>     - Real-time search filter across distinct column values;<br>     - Bulk toggles: &quot;Select All&quot; and &quot;Clear All&quot;;<br>     - Interactive multi-select checklist of unique values with an explicit &quot;(Blanks)&quot; category for `MissingValues`;<br>     - Dedicated &quot;Apply Filter&quot; and &quot;Clear Filter&quot; action buttons;<br>   * `DataSet::is_row_matched_by_filter` evaluates row eligibility against all active column filter constraints.<br>2. **Cell Context Menu (`context_menu.rs`):**<br>   * Accessible via right-click on any grid cell:<br>     - &quot;Filter by selected cell value&quot; — instantly narrows the active view to matching records;<br>     - &quot;Clear column filter&quot; — quickly lifts constraints on the active column;<br>     - &quot;Sort Ascending / Descending&quot; directly from the cell context;<br>     - Quick clipboard shortcuts (&quot;Copy&quot;, &quot;Paste&quot;).<br>3. **Filtering Visualization (SPSS FILTER BY Parity):**<br>   * Inactive / filtered cases are not silently hidden from view: row headers in the left quadrant display a diagonal vector strikethrough, and cell values render in muted gray (`Tokens::text_muted()`);<br>   * Downstream statistical procedures automatically respect the active case mask in strict alignment with SPSS standards.<br>4. **Data Integrity Guards (&quot;Numbers Stored as Text&quot; — `integrity.rs`):**<br>   * Developed `is_number_stored_as_text` detector: identifies `RawValue::Text` fields containing parseable numeric sequences (supporting trimmed whitespace, comma/period decimals, and scientific notation);<br>   * Excel-parity vector warning indicator: green corner triangle badge (`paint_integrity_badge`) rendered in the cell&#39;s top-left corner;<br>   * Instant inline conversion: clicking the badge converts the string to `RawValue::Number`, protecting data fidelity before running statistical procedures.<br>5. **Testing &amp; Quality Gate (DoD):**<br>   * Authored integration test suite `crates/statcraft_app/tests/grid_autofilter_integrity_invariants.rs` (dataset row filtering, text-to-number detection &amp; conversion, and headless popup rendering);<br>   * 100% successful pass across all CI Quality Gates via `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- ci`:<br>     - `cargo fmt --all -- --check` — clean;<br>     - `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -j 1 -- -D warnings` — 0 warnings;<br>     - `cargo test --workspace -j 1` — all 120+ tests pass with zero failures;<br>     - `xtask file-guard` — 419 files strictly within limits;<br>     - `xtask layers` and `xtask design-guard` — 0 violations;<br>     - `xtask test-undo` — 41 commands verified for 100% reversible Undo/Redo;<br>   * Optimized release binary `target/release/statcraft_app.exe` compiled and verified.</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 80: Tabular Grid Stabilization, Auto-Release v0.4.0 &amp; Comprehensive Documentation Parity</h3><p>*Time: November 16, 2026, 11:15 (~45 minutes)*</p><p>Finalized stabilization of the modernized Data View tabular grid, prepared and published official release **StatCraft v0.4.0**, and completed a global audit bringing all documentation into parity:<br>1. **Grid Defect Elimination (BUGS_AND_ISSUES):**<br>   * **BUG-010 (Text occlusion by selection fill):** Selection background fill moved into `paint_data_cells` beneath cell text, restoring 100% text clarity and contrast across arbitrary selection areas;<br>   * **BUG-011 (Double-click inline editor autofocus):** Double-clicking any data cell now reliably spawns the floating `TextEdit` with immediate focus and text cursor;<br>   * **BUG-012 (Header hit-testing localization):** Column border resize grab zone strictly constrained to the top-right header quadrant (`quad_top_right`), preventing accidental resize cursor triggers while navigating data rows.<br>2. **Official Auto-Release v0.4.0:**<br>   * Synchronized application version across all 5 packaging definitions: `Cargo.toml`, `packaging/windows/installer.iss`, `packaging/linux/control`, `packaging/macos/Info.plist`, `.github/workflows/release.yml`;<br>   * Created bilingual `RELEASE_NOTES.md` and structured `CHANGELOG.md`;<br>   * Tag `v0.4.0` pushed to GitHub with automated multi-platform release runners (Windows, Linux, macOS).<br>3. **Comprehensive Documentation Parity (`FEATURES.md`, `FEATURES_RU.md`, `ROADMAP.md`, `ROADMAP.en.md`):**<br>   * Added all analytical procedures to the feature guides: Partial Correlations (`PARTIAL CORR`), General Linear Models (`UNIANOVA`, `GLM Multivariate`, `GLM Repeated Measures`), Binary Logistic Regression (`LOGISTIC REGRESSION`), Curve Estimation (`CURVEFIT`), $K$-Means Cluster Analysis (`QUICK CLUSTER`), Variable Codebook (`CODEBOOK`), Case Summaries (`SUMMARIZE`), Kaplan-Meier Survival Analysis (`KM`), and Actuarial Life Tables (`SURVIVAL`);<br>   * Updated MCP bridge documentation (headless stdio CLI and port 18493) and universal theming (Dark Pro, SPSS Classic Light, System Auto);<br>   * Updated roadmap status marking M1–M14 as delivered;<br>   * Synchronized `README.md` and `README.ru.md` with 4-quadrant grid capabilities and updated test suite count to 300+ tests.<br>4. **Quality Gate (DoD):**<br>   * 100% test pass on full workspace suite (`cargo test --workspace -j 1`);<br>   * 0 violations on layers, design-guard, and file-guard (`xtask ci`).</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 81: Multinomial Logistic Regression (Feature 009 — NOMREG)</h3><p>*Time: November 16, 2026, 14:30 (~50 minutes)*</p><p>Delivered a full-fledged Multinomial Logistic Regression (**`NOMREG`**) procedure in strict accordance with the Spec-Kit architectural framework, IBM SPSS Statistics 24 canon, and Craft Anything Clean-Room principles:<br>1. **L2 Computational Engine (`statcraft_algo::multinomial_logistic`):**<br>   * **Newton-Raphson Numerical Optimizer (Fisher Scoring):** high-performance matrix operations via `faer`, numerically stable `log-sum-exp` formulation preventing floating-point overflow, backtracking line search, and Ridge Hessian damping ($\lambda = 10^{-6}$) under ill-conditioning or quasi-complete separation (enforcing the `Never Crash` rule);<br>   * **Model Diagnostics &amp; Inference:** Likelihood Ratio Tests (LRT) for individual predictor effects, subpopulation grouping for Pearson and Deviance goodness-of-fit $\chi^2$ tests, pseudo $R^2$ statistics (Cox &amp; Snell, Nagelkerke, McFadden), parameter covariance matrix, Wald statistics, and Odds Ratios $\text{Exp}(B)$ with 95% confidence intervals;<br>   * **Classification Matrix:** observed vs. predicted category assignments and percentage of cases correctly classified;<br>   * **Categorical Factors:** discrete predictor support with automated dummy indicator contrast coding and reference category selection (defaulting to the last category).<br>2. **L5 Command Bus (`statcraft_syntax`):**<br>   * Strongly-typed `MultinomialLogisticCommand` (`stat.regression.multinomial`) providing declarative `specs()` schema for MCP AI agents;<br>   * Bidirectional serialization for SPSS syntax `NOMREG ... (BASE=LAST) BY ... WITH ... /MODEL ... /CRITERIA ... /PRINT ...`;<br>   * Extended syntax parser mapping `NOMREG` subcommands with support for `(BASE=LAST)` and `(BASE=FIRST)`.<br>3. **L6 User Interface (`statcraft_app`):**<br>   * Canonical `DialogKit` modal (`multinomial_logistic_dialog.rs`, $560 \times 430$ px): dependent variable slot, factors and covariates lists, `ReferenceCategoryDialog` subdialog, `StatisticsDialog` subdialog, and Type 1 `DialogActionBar`;<br>   * 7 authentic SPSS Pivot Tables (`tables_multinomial_logistic.rs`): Case Processing Summary, Model Fitting Information, Goodness-of-Fit, Pseudo R-Square, Likelihood Ratio Tests, Parameter Estimates, and Classification Table;<br>   * Activated `Analyze &gt; Regression &gt; Multinomial Logistic...` menu item and added TSV report export.<br>4. **Quality Gate &amp; Invariants (DoD):**<br>   * Developed unit and integration test suites across all architectural layers: `statcraft_algo` (4 tests), `statcraft_syntax` (`test_nomreg_syntax_and_command`), `advanced_regression_dialog_invariants.rs`, and `multinomial_logistic_tests.rs`;<br>   * 100% passing Quality Gate: `xtask file-guard` (428 files strictly within size limits), `xtask design-guard`, `xtask layers`, `xtask parity`, and `i18n_lint_test` (zero hardcoded strings).</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 82: Real-time Dependent Variable Cardinality Validation &amp; Output Outline Tree Guard (BUG-013)</h3><p>*Time: November 16, 2026, 15:45 (~25 minutes)*</p><p>Implemented robust validation guards across logistic regression dialogs to safeguard against invalid model specifications by inexperienced users and fixed output tree localization fallbacks:<br>1. **Interactive Target Cardinality Validation in Binary Logistic Regression (`crates/statcraft_app/src/dialogs/logistic_regression_dialog.rs`):**<br>   * Added real-time unique value counting (`dep_distinct_count`) across active dataset cases upon variable selection;<br>   * When a strictly binary target is selected (exactly 2 unique values, e.g. `gender`), renders a green status indicator `(binary, 2 values)` with `OK` and `Paste` buttons enabled;<br>   * When a continuous or multi-category variable is selected (e.g. `age` with 20 values), renders an amber indicator `({count} values — 2 required)` under the slot and an explanatory banner recommending *Multinomial Logistic Regression*;<br>   * Automatically disables the `OK` and `Paste` action buttons (`is_valid = false`), completely eliminating runtime command aborts in the status bar.<br>2. **Cardinality Guard in Multinomial Logistic Regression (`crates/statcraft_app/src/dialogs/multinomial_logistic_dialog/mod.rs`):**<br>   * Enforced minimum distinct category check ($\ge 2$), disabling execution on constant or empty variables with an informative warning banner.<br>3. **Outline Tree Fallback Guard (`crates/statcraft_app/src/views/output_view/model.rs`):**<br>   * Added an alias fallback in `OutputProcedure::title` mapping legacy parameterized `output-frequencies-title` to `output-frequencies` (&quot;Frequencies&quot;), preventing raw bracketed key fallbacks (`[output-frequencies-title]`) in restored output viewers.<br>4. **Quality Gate &amp; Testing (DoD):**<br>   * Added integration test `test_logistic_regression_validation_with_cases` in `crates/statcraft_app/tests/advanced_regression_dialog_invariants.rs`;<br>   * 100% Quality Gate pass: `xtask design-guard`, `xtask file-guard` (all 429 files compliant), and successful release binary build of `statcraft_app.exe`.</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 83: Cox Proportional Hazards Regression (Feature 010 — COXREG)</h3><p>*Time: November 16, 2026, 17:05 (~60 minutes)*</p><p>Fully implemented semiparametric Cox Proportional Hazards Regression (`COXREG`) with 100% mathematical parity to IBM SPSS Statistics 24, Spec-Kit open standard, and Clean-Room rules:<br>1. **Mathematical Core L2 (`crates/statcraft_algo/src/cox/`):**<br>   * **Log Partial Likelihood &amp; Newton-Raphson Optimization:** Evaluates log partial likelihood, gradient score vector $g(\beta)$, and Fisher Information matrix $I(\beta)$ over dynamic risk sets $R(t_{(k)})$;<br>   * **Tied Survival Times Approximation:**<br>     - Default **Breslow** method ensuring 100% equivalence to standard IBM SPSS baseline output;<br>     - Optional **Efron** method with adjusted risk denominator $S^{(0)}_l = S^{(0)} - \frac{l}{d_k} W_k^D$ for higher accuracy with frequent event ties;<br>   * **Stratification Support (Strata):** Joint coefficient vector $\beta$ estimated across multiple clinical strata with stratum-specific baseline hazard functions $h_{0s}(t)$;<br>   * **Backtracking Line Search Optimization:** Adaptive step halving ensuring monotonic likelihood improvement and Never Crash guarantee on ill-conditioned data;<br>   * **Baseline Hazard &amp; Survival Curves:** Nonparametric cumulative baseline hazard $\hat{H}_{0s}(t)$, baseline survival $\hat{S}_{0s}(t)$, and survival step function at covariate means $\hat{S}(t \mid \bar{x}) = [\hat{S}_{0s}(t)]^{\exp(\hat{\beta}^T \bar{x})}$;<br>   * **Hypothesis Testing &amp; Effect Sizes:** Model omnibus tests ($-2\ln L$, $\chi^2$, $df$, Sig.), standard errors $SE(B)$, Wald tests $\text{Wald} \sim \chi^2(1)$, hazard ratios $\text{Exp}(B)$, and 95% asymptotic Wald confidence intervals;<br>   * Decomposed into 5 modular files (`types.rs`, `engine.rs`, `baseline.rs`, `mod.rs`, `tests.rs`), strictly obeying the $\le 500$ lines limit (File Size Guard).<br>2. **Command Bus L5 (`crates/statcraft_syntax`):**<br>   * Typed command `CoxRegressionCommand` (`stat.survival.cox`) with `specs()` schema for MCP AI agents;<br>   * Dual-direction syntax serialization: `COXREG ... /STATUS = ...(1) /PATTERN = BY ... /METHOD = ENTER ... /CRITERIA = ITERATE(20) TIES(BRESLOW) /PRINT = CI(95) BASELINE /PLOT = SURVIVAL.`;<br>   * SPSS command-line mapper `map_coxreg` integrated into `pkg3.rs`.<br>3. **User Interface L6 (`crates/statcraft_app`):**<br>   * Canonical modal dialog `CoxRegressionDialog` based on `DialogKit` ($560 \times 430$ px): time variable, status with event value definition, covariate picker, stratification slot, tie method selector (Breslow / Efron), and standard `DialogActionBar`;<br>   * 4 authentic SPSS Pivot Tables in Output Viewer (`tables_cox.rs`):<br>     1. *Case Processing Summary* (Total $N$, Event $N$, Censored $N$, Censored %);<br>     2. *Omnibus Tests of Model Coefficients* ($-2\ln L$, $\chi^2$, $df$, $p$);<br>     3. *Variables in the Equation* ($B$, $SE$, Wald, $df$, $p$, $\text{Exp}(B)$, $95\%$ CI);<br>     4. *Survival Table at Mean of Covariates* (Time, Baseline Cum Hazard, Baseline Survival, Survival at Mean);<br>   * Vector step-function Survival Plot rendered using egui painter primitives and Tokens design system;<br>   * Main menu item activated: &quot;Analyze -&gt; Survival -&gt; Cox Regression...&quot; (`menu-analyze-survival-cox`) with TSV export.<br>4. **Quality Gate &amp; Testing (DoD):**<br>   * Added Golden Oracle unit tests in `statcraft_algo` verified against Python `lifelines.CoxPHFitter` with tolerance $\le 10^{-6}$;<br>   * Added headless render and TSV export invariant test `crates/statcraft_app/tests/output_viewer_cox_invariants.rs`;<br>   * 100% Quality Gate pass (`cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- ci`): `fmt`, `clippy -D warnings`, `layers`, `file-guard` (all 438 files compliant), `design-guard`, `i18n-lint` (100% translation coverage in `ru.ftl` and `en.ftl`), 41/41 Undo/Redo matrix.</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 84: &quot;Sort Variables&quot; (SORT VARIABLES) and &quot;Transpose&quot; (FLIP) Procedures</h3><p>*Time: November 16, 2026, 20:05 (~30 minutes)*</p><p>Turnkey implementation of the &quot;Data&quot; menu procedures in strict accordance with the IBM SPSS Statistics 24 canon, ArtCraft architecture principles, and Spec-Kit standard:<br>1. **Data Layer L0/L1 (`statcraft_io`, `statcraft_core`):**<br>   * **Column Reordering:** Method `RawTable::reorder_columns` with permutation bounds and bijective validation;<br>   * **Variable Dictionary:** Method `VariableDictionary::reorder` for structural metadata synchronization;<br>   * **Dataset:** `DataSet::reorder_variables` clearing transactional `DeltaBuffer`, and general `DataSet::restore_structure` for complete operation reversibility;<br>   * **Matrix Transposition (`DataSet::transpose`):** Rows-to-columns and columns-to-rows transformation with automatic first column `CASE_LBL` (original variable labels), variable subset support (`/VARIABLES`), and column names variable support (`/NEWNAMES`) with identifier sanitization. Isolated into `dataset/transform.rs` adhering to File Size Guard.<br>2. **Algorithm Layer L2 (`statcraft_algo`):**<br>   * Module `variable_sort.rs` with `VariableSortAttribute` enum (`Name`, `Type`, `Label`, `Measure`, `Role`, `Alignment`, `Width`, `Decimals`);<br>   * Stable permutation computation `compute_variable_sort_permutation` using secondary key by original index for guaranteed stability across equal attribute values.<br>3. **Command Bus Layer L5 (`statcraft_syntax`):**<br>   * Typed commands `SortVariablesCommand` (`data.sort_variables`) and `TransposeCommand` (`data.transpose`) with `specs()` JSON schemas for MCP AI agents;<br>   * 100% Undo/Redo reversibility using inverse permutation stack `invert_permutation` and snapshot restoration `restore_structure`;<br>   * Dual-direction SPSS syntax serialization and parsing: `SORT VARIABLES BY ... (A/D).` and `FLIP VARIABLES=... /NEWNAMES=... .`.<br>4. **User Interface Layer L6 (`statcraft_app`):**<br>   * Modal dialog `SortVariablesDialog` based on `DialogShell::standard` ($560 \times 430$ px): `GroupBox` attribute selector, order radio buttons (Ascending / Descending), Type 1 `DialogActionBar`;<br>   * Modal dialog `TransposeDialog` based on `DialogShell::standard`: left `VariablePicker`, dual-target `TransferButton` controls (`Variable(s):` and `Name Variable:`), and standard `DialogActionBar`;<br>   * Menu clicks hooked in &quot;Data -&gt; Sort Variables...&quot; and &quot;Data -&gt; Transpose...&quot;;<br>   * Real-time status bar messages (`SortVariablesExecuted`, `TransposeExecuted`) and syntax logging to Output Viewer.<br>5. **Quality Gate &amp; Localization (DoD):**<br>   * Zero-hardcode i18n: added keys to Fluent catalogs `locales/en.ftl` and `locales/ru.ftl`;<br>   * Tests: 100% pass on core, algorithm, syntax, and headless dialog rendering tests (`sort_and_transpose_dialog_tests.rs`);<br>   * Reversibility tests added to Undo/Redo matrix suite `undo_redo_matrix_tests.rs`;<br>   * Updated feature parity checklist `docs/parity-checklist.md` (60 documented commands);<br>   * 100% pass across all `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- ci` stages (`file-guard` across 445 files, `design-guard`, `layers`, `fmt`, `clippy -D warnings`, `test-corpus`, `test-undo`).</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 85: Multi-File Workspace, Dataset Tabs &amp; Memory Guard (Feature 010)</h3><p>*Time: November 18, 2026, 18:25 (~60 minutes)*</p><p>Turnkey implementation of the multi-file workspace architecture, dataset document tabs, and cross-platform Memory Guard in strict adherence to the IBM SPSS Statistics 24 canon and ArtCraft ecosystem principles:<br>1. **Storage Layer L0 (`statcraft_io::stc_codec`):**<br>   * Extended the `.stc` container with `StcDatasetRecord` and `StcContainer::with_workspace`, maintaining 100% backward compatibility with previously saved single-dataset project files;<br>   * Support for packing and extracting an arbitrary number of active dataset sessions, metadata dictionaries, active filters, and split-file states within a unified `.stc` archive.<br>2. **Core &amp; Compression Layer L1 (`statcraft_core`):**<br>   * Module `workspace.rs`: fully-featured `WorkspaceManager` and `DocumentSession` with isolated Undo/Redo delta history, metadata, and view states per dataset;<br>   * Module `compression.rs`: lossless in-memory compression — 1-bit `NullBitmask` for missing values, string dictionary encoding `DictionaryEncodedColumn`, and numeric compression `LosslessCompressedColumn` strictly preserving IEEE 754 `f64` precision (no lossy downcasting to `f32`);<br>   * Added `undo` and `redo` helpers to the transactional `DeltaBuffer`.<br>3. **Command Bus &amp; Syntax Layer L5 (`statcraft_syntax`):**<br>   * Implemented typed dataset management commands in `commands/dataset.rs`: `DATASET NAME`, `DATASET ACTIVATE`, `DATASET CLOSE`, `DATASET DISPLAY`;<br>   * Integrated `.sps` syntax parsing into `CommandBus` with support for `WINDOW=ASIS` modifiers.<br>4. **Cross-Platform Memory Guard L6 (`statcraft_app::system_memory`):**<br>   * Native physical memory polling with zero external dependencies: Windows API (`GlobalMemoryStatusEx`), Linux (`/proc/meminfo`), macOS (`sysctl`), WebAssembly (`core::arch::wasm32`);<br>   * Preflight checks before loading large files: triggers a non-blocking modal alert if opening large batches (&gt;10 files) or files &gt;250 MB under constrained system RAM (&lt;500 MB or &lt;15% available).<br>5. **Vector Document Tab Strip L6 (`views::document_tabs`):**<br>   * Horizontal `DocumentTabStrip` component (height 28 px) located directly above the active data grid;<br>   * Strict Vector-First UI: vector table icon, dirty marker `*`, tab close button `✕`, horizontal chevron navigation `[ ‹ ] [ › ]`, and new blank dataset button `[ ➕ ]`;<br>   * Mouse wheel horizontal scrolling and keyboard shortcuts: `Ctrl+Tab` / `Ctrl+Shift+Tab` (tab switching), `Ctrl+W` (close active dataset), `Ctrl+N` (new dataset), `Ctrl+Shift+N` (new project);<br>   * Safe closure confirmation dialog for dirty tabs, distinct active dataset saving (`Ctrl+S`), and complete project container saving (`Ctrl+Shift+S`).<br>6. **Architectural Decomposition of `app.rs`:**<br>   * Prevented monolithic bloat by cleanly extracting `app_workspace.rs` (dataset sessions), `app_shortcuts.rs` (keyboard input handling), and `app_tab_viewer.rs` (egui-dock `TabViewer` implementation), dropping `app.rs` from 1100+ lines down to ~800 lines.<br>7. **Quality Gate &amp; Localization (DoD):**<br>   * 100% bilingual Fluent localization (`locales/en.ftl`, `locales/ru.ftl`), clean `i18n_lint_test` without duplicate keys;<br>   * 100% pass across all stages of `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- ci` (formatting, clippy with 0 warnings, layer validation, file-guard across 454 files, design-guard, full workspace test suite, corpus, and 41-command Undo/Redo matrix).</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 86: Dataset Color Identity &amp; Cross-Pane Visual Linking (Feature 011)</h3><p>*Time: November 18, 2026, 23:40 (~35 minutes)*</p><p>Turnkey implementation of end-to-end dynamic dataset color identity and cross-pane visual linking (Brushing &amp; Linking) between document tabs, the outline tree, and report notes in strict accordance with the Feature 011 plan and ArtCraft ecosystem canon:<br>1. **Theme Color Engine (`statcraft_app::theme`):**<br>   * Implemented a deterministic harmonic color generator `dataset_color(name)` based on the Golden Ratio HSL distribution (FNV-1a hash + golden angle $137.50776^\circ$).<br>   * High contrast, guaranteed perceptual differentiation between concurrent datasets, theme-adaptive lightness (0.60 for dark, 0.45 for light), and 100% color stability across restarts.<br>   * Helper `color_with_alpha` for translucent tints and borders.<br>   * Unit tests for determinism, differentiation, and alpha blending in `theme::tests`.<br>2. **Vector Document Tabs (`views::document_tabs`):**<br>   * Table grid vector icon `[田]` styled in the dataset&#39;s identity color (full vibrancy on active tab, dimmed on inactive tabs).<br>   * Active underline indicator and subtle translucent background highlight (`alpha = 25`) matching the dataset&#39;s identity color.<br>3. **Output Viewer Model (`views::output_view::model`):**<br>   * Field `#[serde(default)] pub dataset_name: Option&lt;String&gt;` added to `OutputProcedure` with automatic association in all analytical procedures (`builder.rs` and `tables_*.rs`).<br>   * 100% backward compatibility verified via automated tests for legacy project JSON deserialization.<br>   * Active dataset tracking in `OutputViewerState` synchronized on each workspace tab change.<br>4. **Brushing &amp; Linking in Outline Tree (`views::output_view::outline`):**<br>   * Vector dataset badge chips rendered alongside procedure titles in the Outline navigation tree.<br>   * Dynamic Brushing &amp; Linking: badge chips matching the currently focused dataset tab are highlighted with full vibrancy, while historical calculations from background tabs are subtly muted.<br>5. **Report Notes Block (`views::output_view::blocks`):**<br>   * The `Active Dataset` row in procedure Notes displays the dataset name inside a styled vector badge chip with matching outline and background tint.<br>6. **Quality Gate &amp; Definition of Done (DoD):**<br>   * 100% pass across all `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- ci` Quality Gate checks (fmt, clippy with 0 warnings, layers, file-guard on 454 files, design-guard, `output_viewer_invariants`, and 41-command Undo/Redo matrix).</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 87: Data Merge Files (Add Cases &amp; Add Variables, Feature 012)</h3><p>*Time: November 19, 2026, 03:35 (~55 minutes)*</p><p>Turnkey implementation of dataset merging capabilities (menu &quot;Data &gt; Merge Files&quot;, items &quot;Add Cases...&quot; and &quot;Add Variables...&quot;), reviving the previous InDev placeholders into full-fledged interactive procedures in strict compliance with the IBM SPSS Statistics 24 canon (`ADD FILES` and `MATCH FILES`) and ArtCraft ecosystem principles:<br>1. **Core Layer L1 (`statcraft_core::dataset::merge`):**<br>   * Modularized into `crates/statcraft_core/src/dataset/merge/` strictly honoring the &lt;= 500 lines per leaf module limit (`types.rs`, `cases.rs`, `vars.rs`, `source.rs`, `mod.rs`).<br>   * Procedure `add_cases`: vertical row concatenation from two datasets with auto-pairing of compatible columns, `RawValue::Null` padding, automatic string width expansion, `/IN=source01` origin indicator, and optional interleaved case sorting via `/BY`.<br>   * Procedure `add_variables`: horizontal feature joins (1:1 with key matching, 1:N lookup table `/TABLE`, sequential row-order join), automatic name collision resolution, and `/IN` indicator variables.<br>   * Universal loader `source.rs`: loading secondary datasets seamlessly from `.sav`, `.zsav`, `.stc`, `.csv`, `.xlsx` files or directly from open sessions in `WorkspaceManager`.<br>2. **Command Bus &amp; Syntax Layer L5 (`statcraft_syntax`):**<br>   * Implemented typed engine commands `data.merge_cases` (`MergeCasesCommand`) and `data.merge_vars` (`MergeVarsCommand`) with full Undo/Redo reversibility registered in `CommandBus`.<br>   * Methods `to_sps`: generating canonical SPSS syntax for `ADD FILES` and `MATCH FILES`.<br>   * Syntax parser integration in `syntax_parser::mappers::data` recognizing `ADD FILES` and `MATCH FILES` clauses.<br>3. **Desktop GUI L6 (`statcraft_app`):**<br>   * Created `dialogs/merge_dialog/` built on `DialogKit` (`DialogShell::standard`, `VariablePicker`, `TransferButton`, `DialogActionBar`, `GroupBox`), strictly Vector-First with 0 emojis and 0 tofu.<br>   * Reusable `source_panel`: selection between concurrent open workspace tabs and external disk files via `rfd::FileDialog`.<br>   * Action dispatch encapsulated in `app_dialogs_merge.rs` keeping `app_dialogs_data.rs` under strict line limits.<br>   * Menu &quot;Data &gt; Merge Files&quot;: removed `InDev` status, activated real dialog opening handlers for `AddCasesDialog` and `AddVarsDialog`.<br>4. **Localization &amp; Quality Gate:**<br>   * 100% bilingual Fluent localization (`locales/en.ftl`, `locales/ru.ftl`) with zero hardcoded string literals in UI.<br>   * Successful verification across `file-guard` (468 files within limits), `design-guard`, `layers`, and `merge_dialog_invariants`.</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 88: Grid Interaction Modernization &amp; Invariants (Grid UX Invariants, Spec-Kit 013)</h3><p>*Time: November 19, 2026, 05:25 (~35 minutes)*</p><p>Resolved 5 critical user interaction defects in the virtualized spreadsheet grid (`Data View`), adapting clean-room reference patterns from **GridCraft** (`storytold/gridcraft`) in strict adherence to the ArtCraft canon (100% safe Rust, zero dataset pollution, physical case deletion managed via L5 `CommandBus`):<br>1. **Preserving Rectangular Selection on Right-Click:**<br>   * `GridSelection::contains(row, col)` verifies if a cell is within the active range; right-clicking inside an existing marquee selection preserves the block instead of collapsing to a single cell.<br>   * Dynamic context menu items adapt to selection bounds: multi-cell ranges surface &quot;Copy Range ({count} cells)&quot;, paste, and clear contents.<br>2. **Zero Pollution Invariant for Phantom Rows:**<br>   * In `EditorAction::Commit`, if the editor loses focus with empty or whitespace input on a phantom row (`trimmed.is_empty() &amp;&amp; row &gt;= ds.row_count()`), row allocation is completely bypassed, preventing accidental insertion of rows with system missing values (`RawValue::Null` / `.`).<br>   * The trailing new-case row header renders the canonical asterisk `*` (SPSS/GridCraft standard).<br>3. **Physical Case Deletion via Delete Key &amp; Menu Actions:**<br>   * Differentiated `Delete` key semantics: cell selections clear values to `Null` preserving dataset dimensions, whereas full-row selections (`is_full_rows`) physically remove observations from the dataset via the L5 `data.delete_row` engine command with reduced sample size $N$ and complete Undo/Redo reversibility.<br>4. **Row and Column Header Context Menus (`ContextMenuTarget`):**<br>   * `GridEvent::ContextMenuRow` and `ContextMenuCol` now pass screen position `pos`.<br>   * Extended `GridContextMenuState`: row headers provide &quot;Insert Case Above&quot; (`data.add_row`), &quot;Delete Selected Cases ({count})&quot; (`data.delete_row`), and &quot;Clear Cases Values&quot;; column headers provide ascending/descending sorts, &quot;Insert Variable&quot; (`var.add`), and &quot;Auto-fit Column Width&quot;.<br>5. **Click-Outside Dismissal (Eliminating Modal Traps):**<br>   * Both the context menu and the column auto-filter popup (`render_filter_popup`) measure `popup_rect` and utilize a `just_opened` frame guard, dismissing immediately when clicking anywhere outside their boundaries without requiring `Escape`.<br>6. **Testing &amp; Quality Gate:**<br>   * Added comprehensive integration suite `crates/statcraft_app/tests/grid_selection_and_phantom_row_invariants.rs` (5 tests covering right-click selection preservation, zero pollution phantom row commits, CommandBus deletion with undo, context menu targets, and full-row keyboard deletion);<br>   * 100% pass across all Quality Gate checks: `file-guard` (469 files), `design-guard`, `layers`, `cargo clippy --workspace -j 1 -- -D warnings`, and `cargo fmt --check`.</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 89: Eliminating False Fill Handle &amp; Stabilizing Grid Range Selection (Spec-Kit 014)</h3><p>*Time: November 19, 2026, 06:45 (~25 minutes)*</p><p>Resolved a critical regression where dragging the mouse from cell (0, 0) down the data table triggered unintended series auto-fill and corrupted data (defect `BUG-014`), aligning grid interaction with the reference IBM SPSS Statistics canon (cell range selection is strictly Read-Only):<br>1. **Root Cause Analysis:**<br>   * In `interact.rs`, `selection.hit_test_fill_handle(geo, pos, 4.0)` intercepted mouse clicks in a 14x14 px zone around the bottom-right corner of cell (0, 0), erroneously activating series extension `GridDrag::FillHandle` instead of marquee selection `GridDrag::SelectRange`.<br>   * On mouse release, `apply_auto_fill` ran `while ds.row_count() &lt;= target.max_row { ds.add_empty_row(); }`, forcibly appending phantom rows with system-missing values (`SYSMIS`) and replicating the cell (0, 0) value (e.g. `101.00`) down the column, overwriting existing records.<br>2. **Eliminating the Fill Handle Marker from UI (SPSS Canon):**<br>   * In `interact.rs`, completely removed the `hit_test_fill_handle` interceptor: clicking and dragging anywhere in `quad_center` is guaranteed to initiate pure range selection `SelectRange` or inline editing on double-click. In `handle_active_drag`, `GridDrag::FillHandle` is neutralized without producing mutation events.<br>   * In `selection.rs`, removed fill handle square rendering from `paint_selection`, leaving a crisp 1.5 px vector perimeter outline.<br>3. **Zero Allocation Invariant in Auto-Fill (`apply_auto_fill`):**<br>   * In `clipboard.rs`, constrained `apply_auto_fill` strictly within existing dataset rows (`target.max_row.min(ds.row_count().saturating_sub(1))`). Row allocation `ds.add_empty_row()` was removed, guaranteeing that auto-fill never allocates phantom rows with missing values.<br>4. **Testing &amp; Quality Gate:**<br>   * Added regression test `test_drag_selection_over_phantom_row_never_mutates_dataset` in `tests/grid_selection_and_phantom_row_invariants.rs`: verified that dragging selection from (0, 0) past existing rows into the phantom row `*` preserves row count (strictly 5) and preserves original values (101, 102, 103, 104, 105) intact.<br>   * Added unit test `test_auto_fill_never_allocates_phantom_rows` in `clipboard.rs`.<br>   * 100% pass across workspace tests, `file-guard` (469 files), `design-guard`, `layers`, `clippy -D warnings`, and `fmt --check`.</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 90: Dynamic Dataset Color Generation and .stc Persistence (Spec-Kit 015)</h3><p>*Time: November 19, 2026, 12:00 (~30 minutes)*</p><p>Implemented dynamic, collision-aware random color generation for dataset tabs with cross-pane visual identity and seamless `.stc` container persistence (resolving `BUG-015`):<br>1. **Root Cause of Clustering Defect:**<br>   * In v0.4.1, `dataset_color(name)` calculated hue blindly via 32-bit FNV-1a hash with fixed saturation ($S=0.65$) and lightness ($L=0.60$). Datasets with similar prefixes/suffixes (`merge_base.csv`, `merge_add_cases.csv`, `merge_add_vars.csv`) clustered into an identical purple hue slice ($280^\circ$–$308^\circ$), making tabs visually indistinguishable. Furthermore, tab colors were not saved to `.stc` projects and reset between sessions.<br>2. **Dynamic Contrast Color Generator (`generate_contrast_hex` / `generate_contrast_color`):**<br>   * Implemented high-quality 64-bit SplitMix64 hashing with continuous golden angle distribution ($137.50777^\circ$).<br>   * The generator dynamically scans all currently open document tabs and enforces minimum angular hue distance $\ge 45^\circ$, preventing visual collisions across any arbitrary number of tabs without hardcoded color sets (Zero-Hardcode Palette).<br>   * Dynamically modulates saturation ($0.65 \dots 0.85$) and tunes lightness for dark and light theme palettes.<br>3. **Persistence in `.stc` Project Container with 100% Backward Compatibility:**<br>   * Added `pub tab_color: Option&lt;String&gt;` with `skip_serializing_if = &quot;Option::is_none&quot;` across `StcDatasetRecord`, `StcContainer`, and `DocumentSession`.<br>   * Saving multi-dataset workspaces (`save_workspace_stc_to_path`) persists hex colors directly into the `.stc` container.<br>   * Reloading `.stc` restores exact colors byte-for-byte, while legacy `.stc` files without `tab_color` deserialize seamlessly with automatic contrast color assignment.<br>4. **End-to-End Synchronization with Output Viewer:**<br>   * Output Viewer now receives workspace context via `render_output_view_with_workspace`: procedure chips in Outline Tree and the `Active Dataset` badge in Notes tables query `workspace.session_color_by_name(name)`.<br>   * Tab headers and analysis output badges are guaranteed 100% color consistency.<br>5. **Testing &amp; Quality Gate:**<br>   * Added integration invariant test `test_dataset_color_generation_contrast_and_persistence` in `crates/statcraft_app/tests/dataset_color_persistence_tests.rs`: verified $\ge 45^\circ$ angular separation between `merge_base.csv`, `merge_add_cases.csv`, `merge_add_vars.csv` and verified byte-for-byte round-trip preservation in `.stc`.<br>   * Added unit tests in `statcraft_core::workspace` (`test_dynamic_contrast_colors_for_similar_prefixes`) and `statcraft_core::stc_codec` (`test_save_load_multi_file_workspace_stc_color_persistence`).<br>   * Validated backward compatibility with legacy containers in `statcraft_io::stc_codec`.<br>   * 100% Quality Gate pass: `file-guard` (470 files compliant), `design-guard`, `layers`, `clippy -D warnings`, `fmt --check`, `cargo test --workspace -j 1`.</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 91: Unsaved Changes Dirty Marker Positioning and False Titlebar Indicator Fix (BUG-016)</h3><p>*Time: November 19, 2026, 13:30 (~35 minutes)*</p><p>Eliminated visual overlap of the unsaved changes dirty marker (`*`) over tab title text and resolved the persistent false indicator in the application titlebar (defect `BUG-016`):<br>1. **Root Causes Analysis:**<br>   * In `document_tabs.rs`, asterisk X-coordinate was hardcoded as `text_x + display_name.len().min(12) as f32 * 6.5 + 4.0`. For any filename longer than 12 characters (e.g. `merge_add_cases.csv`, 19 chars), `min(12)` clamped the position, rendering the asterisk directly over the letters `cases` in the middle of the tab.<br>   * In the titlebar (`app.rs`), the title was formatted as `format!(&quot;{}{} •&quot;, file_name, asterisk)`. The bullet symbol ` •` (U+2022) was hardcoded at the end of the string and always appeared regardless of dirty state, creating a permanent visual impression of an unsaved marker (and violating Rule 8 of AGENTS.md).<br>   * In `has_unsaved_changes()`, `SavedCheckpoint` tracked `col_count` and `row_count` of a single dataset. In a multi-document workspace, switching between datasets with differing column or row counts (e.g. `merge_base.csv` 5x4 vs `merge_add_cases.csv` 4x5) triggered false positive `saved != current`, turning on the asterisk in the titlebar.<br>   * In `app_session.rs::save_to_path()`, saving data to CSV omitted `mark_clean()`, leaving the session dirty.<br>2. **Document Tab Strip Rendering Refinement (`DocumentTabStrip`):**<br>   * Guaranteed right padding reservation (`right_reserved = 32.0 px` when dirty, 20.0 px when clean).<br>   * Tab title text is safely truncated via `layout_job` with `TextWrapping::truncate_at_width` strictly before the marker, preventing collisions.<br>   * Amber asterisk `*` (`palette.measure_ordinal`) is positioned strictly after the text (`text_x + text_w + 3.0`) with vertical centering `Align2::LEFT_CENTER`.<br>3. **Application Titlebar Normalization (`app.rs`):**<br>   * Completely removed the prohibited ` •` glyph.<br>   * Window title now renders cleanly: `file_name` (clean) or `file_name *` (modified).<br>4. **Semantic Session Isolation in `has_unsaved_changes()` and CSV Clean Marking:**<br>   * `has_unsaved_changes()` now inspects session-specific state against its own dictionary, dimensions, and delta undo checkpoint, eliminating cross-session interference upon tab switching.<br>   * Saving to CSV marks the active session `sess.mark_clean()` and updates `delta_undo_checkpoint_len`.<br>5. **Testing &amp; Quality Gate:**<br>   * Added integration test `test_multi_dataset_dirty_marker_isolation_and_csv_clean` in `crates/statcraft_app/tests/session_lifecycle_tests.rs`.<br>   * 100% successful pass across all CI Quality Gates via `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- ci`.</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 92: Elimination of Procedure Calculation Precision Loss and Migration to get_cell_numeric (PR #5 by @jjohare)</h3><p>*Time: November 20, 2026, 21:15 (~35 minutes)*</p><p>Resolved a critical numerical precision defect in statistical procedures caused by inadvertent rounding through variable print format `F8.2` (discovered and fixed in PR #5 by contributor `@jjohare`):<br>1. **Root Cause of Precision Loss:**<br>   * Previously, all 21 procedures across `statcraft_syntax` (`descriptives`, `correlations`, `regression`, `anova`, `ttest`, `glm`, `factor`, etc.) read cell values via `ds.get_cell_display(r, col, false).parse::&lt;f64&gt;()`.<br>   * `get_cell_display` was designed strictly for on-screen representation and rounded numbers according to variable `decimals` format specification (defaulting to 2 decimals, `F8.2`).<br>   * As a consequence, input data was implicitly truncated to 2 decimals prior to mathematical calculation: `0.123456` became `0.12`, small deltas and concentrations were zeroed, distorting regression slopes and shifting $p$-values. Furthermore, for variables with `DataType::Dollar` or `DataType::Comma`, parsing strings with `$` or thousand separators always failed as `None`, making currency columns unreadable to all statistical procedures.<br>2. **Direct Numeric Access `get_cell_numeric` in Core (`statcraft_core`):**<br>   * Added `DataSet::get_cell_numeric(&amp;self, row: usize, col: usize) -&gt; Option&lt;f64&gt;` extracting `RawValue::Number(*n)` directly from memory with zero heap allocations and full 64-bit IEEE 754 precision.<br>   * Safely handles string missing values (`&quot;&quot;`, `&quot;.&quot;`, `&quot;NA&quot;`), while parsing valid numeric strings into `f64`.<br>   * Formatted currencies (`Dollar`, `CustomCurrency`) and grouped numbers (`Comma`, `Dot`) are now read as clean floating-point numbers without string parse failures.<br>3. **Refactoring of 21 Syntax Commands (`statcraft_syntax`):**<br>   * Migrated all statistical computation commands to `ds.get_cell_numeric(r, col_idx)`.<br>   * Grouping/factor keys and value labels intentionally remain on display strings to maintain categorical key behavior.<br>4. **GUI Dialog Precision Polish (`statcraft_app`):**<br>   * Updated `logistic_regression_dialog.rs` and `multinomial_logistic_dialog/mod.rs` dependent variable distinct level counting to use `ds.get_cell_numeric`, preventing erroneous collapsing of close decimal levels (such as 0.001 and 0.002).<br>5. **Testing &amp; Quality Gate:**<br>   * Added `crates/statcraft_syntax/tests/numeric_precision_tests.rs` testing exact linear data: mean, minimum, regression slope/intercept, and Pearson $r$ match analytical reference values to within $10^{-9}$.<br>   * Added `crates/statcraft_app/tests/numeric_dialog_precision_tests.rs` verifying level distinctness and currency format support.<br>   * 100% Quality Gate pass: `cargo test --workspace -j 1`, `xtask file-guard` (472 files compliant), `xtask design-guard`.</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 93: Full-Scale Math Core Audit via Craft Anything and 100% IBM SPSS Statistics Canon Coverage</h3><p>*Time: November 21, 2026, 00:30 (~25 minutes)*</p><p>Completed an end-to-end evidence-based mathematical audit of `statcraft_algo` core procedures using the **Craft Anything** MCP server (`storytold/craft-anything`) under strict Clean-Room methodology:<br>1. **Craft Anything Investigation &amp; Evidence Ledger:**<br>   * Set up investigation brief (`core_brief_write`) against the *IBM SPSS Statistics 24 Algorithms Guide* (1,271 pp.) under absolute tolerance threshold $\le 10^{-6}$.<br>   * Formulated and verified 3 targeted hypotheses (`hyp_1`, `hyp_2`, `hyp_3`): equivalence of advanced regression, General Linear Model (GLM), and Cox proportional hazards regression formulas.<br>   * All 26 Golden Oracle benchmark tests (`cargo test -p statcraft_algo -j 1`) passed with 0 failures and zero discrepancies.<br>   * Recorded final evidence report in `docs/CRAFT_ANYTHING_AUDIT_REPORT.md`.<br>2. **Specification Restoration and Synchronization (`SPSS_ALGORITHMS_AUDIT.md` &amp; `SPSS_ALGORITHMS_AUDIT_RU.md`):**<br>   * **Block 16:** Documented `PARTIAL CORR` (Schur complement $S = R_{XX} - R_{XZ} R_{ZZ}^{-1} R_{ZX}$, $df = N - k - 2$, $t$-statistic), `LOGISTIC REGRESSION` (IRLS Newton-Raphson, Hosmer-Lemeshow goodness-of-fit $H$, pseudo $R^2$, classification matrix) and `CURVEFIT` (6 regression curve models).<br>   * **Block 17:** Documented General Linear Model: `UNIANOVA` (Type III SS via marginal reduction of Yates&#39; weighted squares of means, deviation contrasts, SVD Jacobi), `GLM MULTIVARIATE` (generalized eigenvalues $E^{-1/2} H E^{-1/2}$, 4 MANOVA criteria: Wilks&#39; $\Lambda$, Pillai, Hotelling-Lawley, Roy) and `GLM REPEATED` (orthonormal Helmert contrasts, Mauchly&#39;s sphericity $W, \chi^2$ and Greenhouse-Geisser and Huynh-Feldt corrections).<br>   * **Block 20:** Synchronized Cox Proportional Hazards Regression `COXREG` (partial likelihood Newton-Raphson, Breslow and Efron tie handling, stratification, cumulative baseline hazard $\hat{H}_{0s}(t)$ and step survival function plot).<br>3. **Outcome:** Mathematical audit specification now covers 100% of all 20 computational blocks in both languages without gaps.</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 94: Official Web Portal, Interactive Wiki &amp; Anonymous Researcher Issue Engine</h3><p>*Time: November 21, 2026, 15:30 (~40 minutes)*</p><p>Architected and deployed the official web platform and high-usability Wiki/Documentation portal for **StatCraft** (`website/`) built with **Next.js 15 (App Router), React 19, Tailwind CSS v4, TypeScript, and KaTeX**, prepared for Vercel deployment:<br>1. **Academic Positioning Without Marketing Hype:**<br>   * Framed explicitly as an open-science computational experiment in 100% Safe Rust with strict academic disclaimers (not certified for critical clinical trials or formal legal evidence without independent verification);<br>   * Dual collaboration focus: inviting statisticians and researchers to test edge cases on real datasets and systems engineers to optimize mathematical kernels.<br>2. **Architectural Drafting Aesthetic (Blueprint Style):**<br>   * Adapted PhotoCraft Companion&#39;s drafting visual identity to StatCraft&#39;s theme tokens (`crates/statcraft_app/src/theme.rs`): dark graphite backgrounds `#14161a` / `#0c0d10`, hairline rules, `.tick` crosshairs, sticky `.hud-label` eyebrows, and measure scale accents (Scale `#4696e6`, Ordinal `#e6a028`, Nominal `#46be78`).<br>3. **Interactive Landing Page Modules:**<br>   * `Hero`: academic manifesto, v0.4.3 build status, 4 architectural guarantee chips (20/20 SciPy Oracle blocks, 0 panics, Apache Arrow, socket 18492);<br>   * `OracleBenchmark`: searchable and filterable 20-block verification matrix with live KaTeX mathematical formula rendering, IBM algorithm references, and inline discrepancy report triggers;<br>   * `AgentLab`: interactive terminal demonstrating Model Context Protocol (MCP) and local JSON-RPC socket 18492 integration with AI assistants (Claude, Antigravity, local LLMs);<br>   * `ArchitectureGuarantee`: L0–L6 layered hierarchy blueprint and comparative advantages of 100% Safe Rust over legacy C++ codebases;<br>   * `CallForResearchers`: scholarly collaboration guidelines with privacy-first protocols for sharing mock cases and covariance matrices.<br>4. **Ergonomic 3-Column Wiki / Knowledge Portal (`/docs` &amp; `/ru/docs`):**<br>   * Left navigation column with category grouping and real-time search;<br>   * Center reading pane with KaTeX LaTeX math blocks and copyable canonical SPSS `.sps` syntax examples;<br>   * Right floating on-page Table of Contents (&quot;On this page&quot;) and quick GitHub links.<br>5. **Anonymous Issue Engine (`/api/create-issue`):**<br>   * Vercel Serverless Function enabling researchers without GitHub accounts to report calculation discrepancies;<br>   * Anti-abuse protection with honeypot traps and IP rate limiting (5 requests per 10 minutes);<br>   * Automatic issue submission with `community-report` and `needs-triage` labels to repository `kobaltgit/StatCraft`.<br>6. **Verification &amp; Quality:**<br>   * Full Next.js static generation: 18 of 18 routes statically prerendered with 0 errors (exit code 0);<br>   * Rust workspace quality: `xtask file-guard` (472 files verified) and `output_viewer_invariants` (11/11 passed).</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 95: Elimination of Windows 10 Frameless Window Defects &amp; DialogKit Measure Inflation Guard</h3><p>*Time: November 22, 2026, 01:15 (~35 minutes)*</p><p>In accordance with `win10_csd_and_dialog_fix_plan.md`, eliminated system frameless rendering defects on Windows 10 and prevented modal dialog inflation by long variable labels:<br>1. **Windows 10 26 px Black Bar &amp; Mouse Offset Fix (BUG-017):**<br>   * Integrated safe Win32 API wrapper `winsafe = &quot;0.0.29&quot;` in `crates/statcraft_app/Cargo.toml` (100% Safe Rust without `unsafe`);<br>   * Implemented window frame guard `crates/statcraft_app/src/window_frame.rs` following the PhotoCraft canon:<br>     - `strip(hwnd)`: dynamically strips `WS_CAPTION | WS_BORDER` imposed by `winit` and triggers frame recalculation (`SWP_FRAMECHANGED`);<br>     - `keep_clear_of_the_taskbar(hwnd)`: prevents maximized frameless windows from sliding beneath standard or auto-hidden taskbars;<br>     - Initialized in `StatCraftApp::new` via safe HWND enumeration (`EnumWindows`) and updated each frame in `eframe::App::update`;<br>     - Preserved 100% Client-Side Decoration (CSD) appearance with exact 1:1 mouse hit-testing;<br>     - Added 7 unit tests for window frame guards.<br>2. **DialogKit Modal Protection Against Long Labels:**<br>   * Added `.max_size(size)` and `.constrain_to(ctx.screen_rect())` to `dialog_shell.rs`, enforcing canonical bounds;<br>   * In `variable_picker.rs`, added `.max_width(inner_size.x)` to `ScrollArea::vertical()`, enabled `.truncate()` on items, and displayed full label in `.on_hover_text(...)`.<br>3. **Verification &amp; Quality Gate:**<br>   * 100% Quality Gate pass via `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- ci`: fmt, clippy (0 warnings), layers, file-guard (473 files), design-guard, full test suite (38 dialog invariants, 11 output viewer invariants), undo/redo reversibility matrix.</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 96: FREQUENCIES Core Decomposition, 14 SPSS Univariate Statistics &amp; Golden Oracle</h3><p>*Time: November 22, 2026, 03:50 (~25 minutes)*</p><p>In strict accordance with IBM SPSS Statistics canon and Rule 12 (File Size Guard), successfully completed Phase 1 of the Frequencies computational engine modernization:<br>1. **Architectural Decomposition of FREQUENCIES Core (`crates/statcraft_algo`):**<br>   * Decomposed monolithic `frequencies.rs` (405 lines) into modular subpackage `crates/statcraft_algo/src/frequencies/` with all files $\le 500$ lines:<br>     - `options.rs` (83 lines): configuration structs `FrequenciesStatisticsOptions` (14 statistics, percentiles, grouped midpoints) and `PercentilesOptions` (quartiles, N-tiles, custom cutpoints);<br>     - `percentiles.rs` (237 lines): percentile calculation using standard **SPSS HAVERAGE** (Weibull / Type 6, rank $r = p \cdot (n + 1)$ with linear interpolation), N-tiles `compute_ntiles`, custom percentiles `compute_custom_percentiles`, and grouped midpoints `compute_grouped_percentile`;<br>     - `stats.rs` (308 lines): calculation of central tendency, dispersion, and distribution shape metrics:<br>       * Mean $\bar{x}$, variance $s^2$, standard deviation $s$, standard error of mean $SE_{\bar{x}}$;<br>       * Range, minimum, maximum, sum;<br>       * Canonical SPSS Mode Tie-Breaker: smallest numeric value selected when maximum frequencies are tied, setting `has_multiple_modes = true`;<br>       * Skewness ($g_1$) and excess kurtosis ($g_2$) with standard errors $SE_{\text{skew}}$ and $SE_{\text{kurt}}$ using Fisher&#39;s unbiased formulas;<br>     - `table.rs` (310 lines): frequency counts, percents, valid percents, and cumulative percents with support for weights and user missing values;<br>     - `mod.rs` (18 lines): public facade preserving 100% backward compatibility for dependent crates (`statcraft_syntax`, `statcraft_app`).<br>2. **Precision Golden Oracle Verification (`tests/frequencies_oracle_test.rs`):**<br>   * Implemented comprehensive test suite verified against analytical solutions and SciPy/SPSS standards with tolerance $\le 10^{-6}$:<br>     - `test_golden_oracle_symmetric_uniform_sample`: verified 11 descriptive metrics on uniform sample $1 \dots 10$ (including exact kurtosis $-1.2$ and standard error of skewness);<br>     - `test_golden_oracle_asymmetric_sample_with_unique_mode`: validated right-skewed distribution and unique mode;<br>     - `test_golden_oracle_weighted_equivalence`: confirmed equality of weighted items and replicated observations;<br>     - `test_golden_oracle_percentiles_ntiles_and_custom`: verified deciles and custom cutpoints;<br>     - `test_compute_frequencies_full_integration`: end-to-end frequency table and descriptive statistics calculation in a single pass.<br>3. **Quality Gate &amp; UI Invariants:**<br>   * All 218 unit and integration tests of `statcraft_algo` passed with exit code 0;<br>   * All 11 tests of `output_viewer_invariants` and `output_viewer_navigation` passed without errors;<br>   * Linter `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- file-guard` verified file size compliance for all 478 Rust files;<br>   * Architectural linter `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- layers` confirmed strict layer boundary compliance;<br>   * Compiler checks