UM`, `SKEWNESS`, `KURTOSIS`;<br>   * Implemented parsing for `/PERCENTILES` (cutpoint list), `/NTILES=n`, `/FORMAT=NOTABLE / DFREQ`, and `/ORDER=ANALYSIS / VARIABLE`.<br>3. **Quality Gate &amp; Invariant Testing:**<br>   * All 133 unit tests of `statcraft_syntax` and 58 integration syntax tests passed with 100% success (`cargo test -p statcraft_syntax -j 1`);<br>   * All 11 tests of Output Viewer invariants (`output_viewer_invariants`) passed without error;<br>   * Linter `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- file-guard` verified file limits for all 482 Rust files across the workspace;<br>   * Architectural linters `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- layers` and `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- design-guard` confirmed full compliance with ecosystem canon.</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 98: &quot;Frequencies: Statistics&quot; Modal Subdialog and DialogKit Modernization (Phase 3)</h3><p>*Time: November 22, 2026, 08:35 (~35 minutes)*</p><p>In strict accordance with the **DialogKit** design guide (`docs/DESIGN_GUIDE.md`), Spec-Kit requirements, and Rule 12 (`File Size Guard`), Phase 3 of the Frequencies procedure modernization has been implemented вЂ” a modal &quot;Frequencies: Statistics&quot; subdialog and updated main dialog layout:<br>1. **Frequencies Dialog Decomposition (`statcraft_app::dialogs::frequencies_dialog`):**<br>   * Decomposed the monolithic file `frequencies_dialog.rs` into a clean subpackage `crates/statcraft_app/src/dialogs/frequencies_dialog/`:<br>     - `state.rs` (152 lines): structures `FrequenciesStatisticsState`, `FrequenciesDialogState`, and action `FrequenciesDialogAction` with JSON serialization methods for engine parameters (`statistics`, `percentiles`, `group_midpoints`);<br>     - `statistics_subdialog.rs` (215 lines): modal subdialog for configuring statistics and percentiles using `DialogShell::new` ($380 \times 460$ px);<br>     - `mod.rs` (230 lines): main dialog coordinating subdialogs, variable list pickers, and user actions.<br>   * Every file in the package is strictly bounded below the $\le 500$ line threshold (Rule 12).<br>2. **&quot;Frequencies: Statistics&quot; Modal Subdialog (`statistics_subdialog.rs`):**<br>   * Canonical two-column SPSS layout built on `DialogKit` components:<br>     - **GroupBox &quot;Percentile Values&quot;:** checkboxes `Quartiles`, `Cut points for: [ 10 ] equal groups` (with custom $N$ intervals), numerical percentile text edit ($0.1 \dots 99.9$) with buttons `[ Add ] [ Change ] [ Remove ]` and a compact ascending-sorted list;<br>     - **GroupBox &quot;Central Tendency&quot;:** Mean, Median, Mode, Sum;<br>     - **Checkbox &quot;Values are group midpoints&quot;** (`group_midpoints`);<br>     - **GroupBox &quot;Dispersion&quot;:** Std. deviation, Variance, Range, Minimum, Maximum, S.E. mean;<br>     - **GroupBox &quot;Distribution&quot;:** Skewness, Kurtosis;<br>   * Bottom action bar using canonical Type 2 widget `SubdialogActionBar::new(true)` (`[ Continue ] [ Cancel ] [ Help ]`):<br>     - Pressing `[ Continue ]` applies the options;<br>     - Pressing `[ Cancel ]` or window close (&#39;X&#39;) immediately reverts changes to the pre-opening snapshot (`stats_backup`).<br>3. **Main Frequencies Dialog Modernization:**<br>   * Right `SubdialogSidebar`: active `[ Statistics... ]` button opening the subdialog, reserved buttons `[ Charts... ]`, `[ Format... ]`, `[ Style... ]`, `[ Bootstrap... ]`;<br>   * Added checkboxes `Display frequency tables` and `Create APA style tables`;<br>   * The `[ Reset ]` button (`ActionBarAction::Reset`) clears selected variables and resets all statistics to SPSS defaults;<br>   * Full parameter package forwarded upon execution to `CommandBus` and syntax generation via `FrequenciesCommand::to_sps_from_params`.<br>4. **Test Suite Decomposition (`tests/dialog_invariants.rs`):**<br>   * To prevent exceeding the 1000-line limit, `dialog_invariants.rs` was architecturally decomposed into `tests/dialog_invariants/` (`fixtures.rs` and `extended_dialogs.rs`);<br>   * Added new precision headless test `test_headless_render_frequencies_statistics_subdialog`;<br>   * All 39 dialog invariant tests (38 preexisting + 1 new) passed with 100% test integrity.<br>5. **Bilingual Localization &amp; Quality Gate:**<br>   * Added 19 new semantic translation keys in `locales/en.ftl` and `locales/ru.ftl` (Zero-Hardcode i18n);<br>   * 100% success on `i18n_lint_test`, `xtask design-guard`, `xtask file-guard` (486 files), `xtask layers`, and `output_viewer_invariants`.</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 99: &quot;Statistics&quot; Summary Table and Frequency Tables in Output Viewer (Phase 4)</h3><p>*Time: November 22, 2026, 09:10 (~35 minutes)*</p><p>In strict accordance with IBM SPSS Statistics reporting standards, Spec-Kit requirements, and Rule 12 (`File Size Guard`), Phase 4 of the Frequencies procedure modernization has been implemented — the authentic &quot;Statistics&quot; summary pivot table and the architectural decomposition of the frequencies rendering module in the Output Viewer:<br>1. **Architectural Decomposition of Frequency Tables (`output_view::tables_frequencies`):**<br>   * The previously monolithic file `tables_frequencies.rs` (375 lines) has been converted into a structured subpackage `crates/statcraft_app/src/views/output_view/tables_frequencies/`:<br>     - `stats_summary_table.rs` (305 lines): authentic SPSS &quot;Statistics&quot; summary table with variable column headers and dynamic row composition;<br>     - `freq_table.rs` (255 lines): detailed category distribution tables for each variable with support for value labels, frequencies, raw, valid, and cumulative percentages;<br>     - `mod.rs` (50 lines): procedure output coordination and TSV clipboard/file export.<br>   * All package files strictly adhere to the $\le 500$ line per file threshold (Rule 12).<br>2. **Authentic SPSS &quot;Statistics&quot; Summary Table (`stats_summary_table.rs`):**<br>   * Column headers contain the names of all analyzed variables (`salary`, `educ`, `gender`);<br>   * Row headers follow the canonical SPSS metric order:<br>     - Mandatory block: $N$ Valid, $N$ Missing;<br>     - 14 univariate statistics (only rows computed for at least one variable are rendered): Mean, Std. Error of Mean, Median, Mode, Std. Deviation, Variance, Skewness, Std. Error of Skewness, Kurtosis, Std. Error of Kurtosis, Range, Minimum, Maximum, Sum;<br>     - Percentiles: header row &quot;Percentiles&quot; followed by indented rows for all unique percentiles in the analysis (quartiles 25, 50, 75, $N$-tiles, and custom cutpoints);<br>   * Multiple modes footnote support: when ties occur, the mode value is marked with flag `a` (`format!(&quot;{:.4} a&quot;, mode)`), and a footnote `t!(&quot;output-freq-mode-footnote&quot;)` (&quot;a. Multiple modes exist. The smallest value is shown.&quot;) is rendered below the table;<br>   * Variables without requested statistics (such as nominal scales) are filled with `.` without layout distortion.<br>3. **Canonical `/FORMAT=NOTABLE` Mode Support:**<br>   * In `statcraft_syntax::commands::frequencies_cmd`, parameter `display_tables: false` (`/FORMAT=NOTABLE`) is now observed;<br>   * When frequency tables are suppressed, detailed category tables are omitted, while the &quot;Statistics&quot; summary table is preserved in both the Output Viewer and TSV export.<br>4. **Invariant Integration Testing (`tests/output_viewer_frequencies_invariants.rs`):**<br>   * Added an integration test suite validating panic-free headless rendering in the `egui` context and TSV export integrity for both summary and category tables;<br>   * Verified table suppression behavior under `NOTABLE` mode.<br>5. **Bilingual Localization and Quality Gate (DoD):**<br>   * Added 19 semantic translation keys to `locales/en.ftl` and `locales/ru.ftl` (Zero-Hardcode i18n);<br>   * 100% pass across all stages of `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- ci` (`file-guard` over 489 files, `design-guard`, `layers`, `cargo fmt --check`, `cargo clippy --workspace -j 1 -- -D warnings`, full workspace test suite, and Undo/Redo reversibility matrix).</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 100: Nominal Scale Numeric Statistics Restoration &amp; Variable Labels Display</h3><p>*Time: November 22, 2026, 10:55 (~30 minutes)*</p><p>Successfully implemented enhancements to the Frequencies procedure for production workflows with real-world research datasets (including sociological and healthcare survey microdata) in strict compliance with the IBM SPSS Statistics canon:<br>1. **Restoration of Descriptive Statistics &amp; Percentiles for Numeric Variables:**<br>   * Removed the artificial suppression of `res.quartiles = None` and `res.statistics = None` when `Measure::Nominal` in `statcraft_syntax::commands::frequencies_cmd`.<br>   * In full alignment with SPSS behavior, univariate statistics (Mean, Median, Mode, Quartiles, Percentiles, Range, Variance, etc.) are computed for all numeric data regardless of the nominal/ordinal scale assignment. Statistics are suppressed exclusively for non-numeric text variables within `compute_frequencies_full`.<br>2. **Variable Labels Display in Output Viewer and TSV Export:**<br>   * Added `variable_label: Option&lt;String&gt;` to `statcraft_algo::FrequencyResult` along with helper methods `display_title()` (returning `Label [Name]` or raw `Name` if label is absent) and `display_label_or_name()`.<br>   * Frequency table headers in `freq_table.rs` now render as `Frequency Table: Label [Name]`, providing researchers with immediate substantive context.<br>   * In the &quot;Statistics&quot; summary table (`stats_summary_table.rs`), column headers now display variable labels with interactive hover tooltips indicating full label and technical variable identifier.<br>   * TSV export preserves human-readable variable labels in both summary and frequency table sections.<br>3. **Authentic Syntax Journaling in Output Log:**<br>   * Method `add_frequencies_with_log` in `OutputViewerState` and invocation pipelines in `app_dialogs.rs` and `syntax_runner.rs` now journal the actual executed SPSS syntax generated by `FrequenciesCommand::to_sps_from_params` (including `/STATISTICS=...`, `/PERCENTILES=...`, `/FORMAT=...`).<br>4. **Testing and Quality Gate (DoD):**<br>   * Added unit tests in `statcraft_algo` (`table.rs`), `statcraft_syntax` (`tests.rs`), and headless integration invariant tests in `statcraft_app` (`output_viewer_frequencies_invariants.rs`).<br>   * 100% pass across all stages of `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- ci` (formatting, clippy, design-guard, file-guard across 489 files, and 41-command Undo/Redo reversibility matrix).</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 101: Frequencies Charts — Stage 1: DialogKit Subdialog, State &amp; SPSS Syntax (.sps)</h3><p>*Time: November 22, 2026, 20:15 (~20 minutes)*</p><p>Successfully implemented Stage 1 of the Frequencies Charts feature (Feature 017) in strict compliance with the IBM SPSS Statistics canon and the `DialogKit` design system:<br>1. **Canonical &quot;Frequencies: Charts&quot; Modal Subdialog (`charts_subdialog.rs`):**<br>   * Created a Type 2 modal subdialog ($360 \times 300$ px) utilizing `DialogShell::subdialog`;<br>   * &quot;Chart Type&quot; group: radio options `None`, `Bar charts`, `Pie charts`, `Histograms:`;<br>   * Indented checkbox `Show normal curve on histogram`, conditionally enabled only when &quot;Histograms:&quot; is selected;<br>   * &quot;Chart Values&quot; group: `Frequencies` and `Percentages` options, enabled exclusively for Bar and Pie charts (disabled for Histograms and None);<br>   * Standard `SubdialogActionBar` (`[ Continue ] [ Cancel ] [ Help ]`) with robust state backup and cancellation rollback.<br>2. **Sidebar Integration and Dialog State (`statcraft_app`):**<br>   * Activated the `Charts...` button in `SubdialogSidebar` of the main Frequencies dialog;<br>   * Extended `FrequenciesDialogState` with `charts: FrequenciesChartOptions` and `charts_backup`;<br>   * Actions `FrequenciesDialogAction::Run` and `Paste` propagate the chart JSON payload into `app_dialogs.rs`.<br>3. **Command Bus and SPSS Bidirectional Syntax (`statcraft_syntax`):**<br>   * Extended `stat.frequencies` command `specs()` with the `charts` schema (`chart_type`, `values`, `normal_curve`);<br>   * In `sps.rs`, implemented canonical emission of `/BARCHART [FREQ|PERCENT]`, `/PIECHART [FREQ|PERCENT]`, `/HISTOGRAM [NORMAL]` subcommands for the Paste action;<br>   * In `syntax_parser/mappers/stats/frequencies.rs`, added parsing for `/BARCHART`, `/PIECHART`, `/HISTOGRAM [NORMAL]`, and `/CHARTS` subcommands.<br>4. **Testing, i18n &amp; Quality Gate (DoD):**<br>   * Added unit tests for syntax generation and parsing in `statcraft_syntax`;<br>   * Added headless rendering invariant test `test_headless_render_frequencies_charts_subdialog` in `dialog_invariants.rs`;<br>   * 100% coverage with bilingual Fluent localization in `locales/en.ftl` and `locales/ru.ftl` (Zero-Hardcode i18n);<br>   * 100% clean passes for `xtask file-guard` (all 490 files within strict limits), `xtask design-guard`, and `xtask layers`.</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 102: Frequencies Charts — Stage 2: Mathematical Models and Chart Computation (L2 statcraft_algo)</h3><p>*Time: November 22, 2026, 20:35 (~20 minutes)*</p><p>Implemented Stage 2 of the Frequencies Charts feature (Feature 017 — Frequencies: Charts) — pure mathematical data structures, categorical aggregation, and adaptive histogram binning in `statcraft_algo`:<br>1. **Chart Options Specifications (`options.rs`):**<br>   * Introduced `ChartType` (`None`, `Bar`, `Pie`, `Histogram`), `ChartValueMode` (`Frequencies`, `Percentages`), and `FrequencyChartSpec` with serde serialization and default implementations.<br>2. **Chart Algorithms and Data Structures (`charts.rs`):**<br>   * Data structures `BarCategoryData` (labels, value representations, counts, and percentages) and `HistogramBinData` (interval boundaries `left`/`right`, `midpoint`, counts, and percentages);<br>   * `HistogramSummary` (sample mean $\mu$, sample standard deviation $\sigma$, sample size $N$, `bin_width`, bins vector, and normal curve coordinates);<br>   * Output payload `FrequencyChartResult` (`Bar`, `Pie`, `Histogram`) with title and variable name formatters;<br>   * Adaptive histogram binning algorithm `compute_histogram` using Scott&#39;s rule ($h = 3.49 \cdot s \cdot n^{-1/3}$) paired with human-readable grid step rounding via `calculate_nice_step` (steps in $1, 2, 5, 10 \times 10^k$);<br>   * Generation of 101 theoretical points for the Gaussian normal distribution curve $\mathcal{N}(\mu, \sigma^2)$, correctly scaled to match the histogram area ($scale = N \cdot bin\_width$);<br>   * Resilience to degenerate distributions: zero variance ($s = 0$), small sample sizes ($N &lt; 2$), and string variables safely yield `None` or a single bin without runtime panics;<br>   * `compute_bar_chart` and `compute_pie_chart` aggregation functions with strict missing values exclusion;<br>   * Unified dispatcher `compute_frequency_chart`.<br>3. **Integration with Result Payloads and Command Bus:**<br>   * Extended `FrequencyResult` with an optional `pub chart: Option&lt;FrequencyChartResult&gt;` field with `skip_serializing_if = &quot;Option::is_none&quot;` ensuring 100% backward compatibility;<br>   * Wired automated chart computation into `commands/frequencies_cmd/mod.rs` when `charts` options are provided;<br>   * Added unit tests `test_frequencies_with_charts_execution` covering Bar charts and Histograms with normal curve overlay.<br>4. **Mathematical Verification via Golden Oracle (`frequencies_charts_oracle_test.rs`):**<br>   * 6 dedicated unit tests verifying normal distribution probability density points and bin properties against `scipy.stats.norm.pdf` and `numpy.histogram` with precision $\le 10^{-6}$;<br>   * Verified category percentage sums ($100.0 \pm 10^{-6}$), category ordering retention, and absence of panics;<br>   * 100% clean passes for all output viewer invariants (`output_viewer_invariants`, `output_viewer_frequencies_invariants`, `output_viewer_navigation`), `xtask file-guard` (492 files), and `cargo clippy -- -D warnings`.</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 103: Frequencies Charts — Stage 3: Vector Rendering in Output Viewer, Outline Tree &amp; Export (L6)</h3><p>*Time: November 22, 2026, 21:05 (~30 minutes)*</p><p>Completed the final third stage of the frequency distribution charts feature (Feature 017 — Frequencies: Charts) — native graphical interface in Output Viewer, Outline tree navigation, and report export:<br>1. **Vector-First Chart Rendering without external heavyweight dependencies (L6):**<br>   * Module `freq_chart_bar_pie.rs` ($\le 500$ lines):<br>     - Bar Charts (`render_bar_chart`): continuous axis scaling with human-readable tick rounding (`calculate_nice_axis_max`), gridlines, category bars with hover highlighting, value labels, and category ticks;<br>     - Pie Charts (`render_pie_chart`): sector triangulation via `Shape::convex_polygon` starting at 12 o&#39;clock, authentic SPSS 10-color contrasting palette (`PIE_PALETTE`), side legend with swatches and proportions;<br>   * Module `freq_chart_histogram.rs` ($\le 500$ lines):<br>     - Histograms (`render_histogram`): contiguous bin columns without gaps, continuous numeric $X$-axis;<br>     - Smooth Gaussian normal distribution curve overlay $\mathcal{N}(\mu, \sigma^2)$ in authentic SPSS orange (`Color32::from_rgb(0xED, 0x7D, 0x31)`);<br>     - Authentic SPSS summary statistics badge in the upper-right corner (`Mean`, `Std. Dev.`, `N`).<br>2. **Output Viewer &amp; Command Coordinator Integration:**<br>   * Added `OutputItemKind::FrequencyCharts(Vec&lt;FrequencyChartResult&gt;)` to output model;<br>   * In `builder.rs`, `add_frequencies_with_log` automatically appends a dedicated chart item to the procedure tree when charts are present;<br>   * Refactored repetitive procedures in `builder.rs` through `push_standard_procedure`, reducing file size to 467 lines (well below the 500-line ceiling).<br>3. **Outline Tree &amp; Export:**<br>   * Vector chart icon `paint_output_chart_icon` (3 vertical columns on a baseline) in `widgets/output_icons.rs`;<br>   * Navigation and context menu support in Outline tree (`outline.rs`);<br>   * Tabular chart export to TSV, TXT, and HTML via `frequency_charts_to_tsv` and `extract_item_tsv`.<br>4. **Definition of Done (DoD):**<br>   * 100% tests passing in workspace (including 6/6 tests in `output_viewer_frequencies_invariants.rs`);<br>   * Full compliance with `xtask file-guard` (all 494 files $\le 500$ lines), `xtask design-guard` (zero emojis, canonical DialogKit), `xtask layers`, and `cargo clippy -- -D warnings`.</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 104: Frequencies Format — Stage 1: Engine, Algorithms &amp; SPSS Syntax (L2 statcraft_algo &amp; L5 statcraft_syntax)</h3><p>*Time: November 23, 2026, 09:20 (~25 minutes)*</p><p>Completed the first stage of the frequency distribution format options feature (Feature 018 — Frequencies: Format / SPSS `FREQUENCIES /FORMAT`) — mathematical types, unified category ordering, table suppression threshold `LIMIT(n)`, and syntax processing:<br>1. **Mathematical Types &amp; Format Options in L2 (`options.rs`):**<br>   * Added `CategoryOrder` enum (`AValue`, `DValue`, `AFreq`, `DFreq`) with resilient `from_str_loose` and `as_str` conversions;<br>   * Added `MultipleVarsMode` enum (`Compare`, `Variable`) for multi-variable output organization;<br>   * Added `FrequenciesFormatOptions` struct encapsulating `order`, `multiple_vars_mode`, and optional `suppress_tables_limit`.<br>2. **Category Ordering &amp; Table Suppression in L2 (`table.rs`):**<br>   * Extended `FrequencyResult` with `pub table_suppressed: bool` annotated with `#[serde(default)]` for 100% backward compatibility;<br>   * Added `sort_categories` and `recalculate_cumulative_percents` for canonical re-ordering with precise recalculation of cumulative percentages based on `valid_percent`;<br>   * Added `apply_format_options` to sort categories and suppress table when category count exceeds threshold $N &gt; \text{limit}$.<br>3. **Command Bus &amp; SPSS Syntax in L5 (`frequencies_cmd`, `sps.rs`, `syntax_parser`):**<br>   * Extended `specs()` in `stat.frequencies` with `order` (`&quot;avalue&quot;`, `&quot;dvalue&quot;`, `&quot;afreq&quot;`, `&quot;dfreq&quot;`), `multiple_vars_mode` (`&quot;compare&quot;`, `&quot;variable&quot;`), and `suppress_tables_limit` (`integer &gt;= 1`);<br>   * Integrated format options in `execute()`, ensuring statistics and charts are preserved when category tables are suppressed;<br>   * SPSS syntax generator in `sps.rs`: serialization of the canonical `/FORMAT` subcommand (e.g., `/FORMAT=DFREQ VARIABLE LIMIT(10)`);<br>   * Syntax mapper in `mappers/stats/frequencies.rs`: token parser for `LIMIT(n)` and `LIMIT n` as well as `COMPARE` and `VARIABLE` modes in `/FORMAT`.<br>4. **Definition of Done (DoD):**<br>   * New test suite `frequencies_order_and_limit_test.rs` in `statcraft_algo` covering all 4 ordering modes, cumulative percent recalculation, and `LIMIT(n)` thresholds;<br>   * Unit tests for round-trip syntax generation and execution with `suppress_tables_limit` in `frequencies_cmd/tests.rs`;<br>   * 100% passes for all invariant test suites (`output_viewer_invariants`, `output_viewer_frequencies_invariants`, `output_viewer_navigation`);<br>   * Strict compliance with `xtask file-guard` (495 files, all $\le 500$ lines), `xtask layers`, `xtask design-guard`, and `cargo clippy --workspace -j 1 -- -D warnings` with zero warnings.</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 105: Website Audit Synchronization &amp; CI Gate Automation (xtask sync-site &amp; CI Gate 10)</h3><p>*Time: November 23, 2026, 09:35 (~20 minutes)*</p><p>Implemented and embedded automated validation into the quality pipeline to guarantee 100% synchronization between the SPSS algorithms audit matrix (`docs/SPSS_ALGORITHMS_AUDIT.md`) and the project website (`website/src/lib/audit-data.ts`, `docs-data.ts`):<br>1. **Synchroniz