br>1. **Frequency Table Suppression Indication (`freq_table.rs`):**<br>   * When `LIMIT(n)` category threshold is exceeded, `res.table_suppressed == true` triggers an SPSS-authentic italic note in `Tokens::text_muted()`: *&quot;The frequency table for variable [NAME] is not displayed because the number of categories exceeds the specified limit.&quot;* via semantic key `output-freq-table-suppressed-note`;<br>   * Computed univariate statistics in the Statistics table and generated distribution charts (histograms with normal curve, bar charts) remain fully visible;<br>   * Updated `frequency_table_to_tsv` to export the suppression notice to TSV streams.<br>2. **Multiple Variables Output Organization (`MultipleVarsMode` in `mod.rs` &amp; `builder.rs`):**<br>   * Extended `FrequencyResult` with `pub multiple_vars_mode: MultipleVarsMode` (`#[serde(default)]`), populated by the `stat.frequencies` command handler;<br>   * **`Compare` mode (default):** displays a single unified summary statistics table (one column per variable), sequential category tables, and an outline Charts node;<br>   * **`Variable` mode:** organizes output into autonomous consecutive blocks for each variable (personal statistics $\to$ frequency table $\to$ chart), with charts rendered inline without duplication;<br>   * TSV export `frequencies_to_tsv` produces structured columns and variable blocks matching the selected mode.<br>3. **End-to-End Invariant Testing (DoD):**<br>   * Added tests in `output_viewer_frequencies_invariants.rs`:<br>     - `test_frequencies_limit_suppression_renders_note_and_preserves_statistics`: verifies report generation under `LIMIT(10)`, suppression note display, and statistics retention;<br>     - `test_frequencies_multivars_compare_and_variable_modes`: verifies output organization and sequencing under `Compare` and `Variable` modes;<br>   * Added tests in `dialog_invariants.rs`:<br>     - `test_frequencies_format_subdialog_transactionality_on_cancel`: verifies transaction