egration tests in `crates/statcraft_app/tests/dialog_invariants/table_style_invariants.rs` (6/6 tests: basic headless render, rollback transactionality, rule mutations, and Frequencies dialog integration);<br>   * 49/49 tests passing in `dialog_invariants.rs`, 11/11 in `output_viewer_invariants.rs`, 8/8 in `output_viewer_frequencies_invariants.rs`;<br>   * 100% pass on `xtask file-guard` (506 files within limits), `xtask design-guard` (0 violations), `xtask layers`, and `cargo clippy --workspace -j 1 -- -D warnings`.</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 111: Table Style &amp; Conditional Formatting — Phase 3: Output Viewer Rendering, Audit Report Table, and End-to-End Integration (L6 statcraft_app + L5 statcraft_syntax)</h3><p>*Time: November 24, 2026, 17:35 (~40 minutes)*</p><p>Successfully completed Phase 3 of the table styling and conditional formatting architecture (**Feature 019: Table Style / Conditional Formatting**), unifying the L4 analytics engine, L5 syntax generators, and L6 presentation layer:<br>1. **L4 Report Model Serialization (`statcraft_reporting`):**<br>   * Implemented `Serialize` and `Deserialize` derivations for `ReportTable` and `CellAlignment`;<br>   * Added `cell_styles_serde` module ensuring `HashMap&lt;(usize, usize), CellStyleFormat&gt;` serializes into a clean JSON sequence of `[[row, col], style]` pairs.<br>2. **Output Viewer Styled Cell Rendering L6 (`statcraft_app`):**<br>   * Added `ReportTable(statcraft_reporting::model::ReportTable)` variant to `OutputItemKind`;<br>   * In `tables_common.rs`, implemented `render_report_table` and `render_data_row_styled`:<br>     - Custom background fill (`bg_color`) rendered via `ui.painter().rect_filled`;<br>     - Custom typography colors (`text_color`) and font weighting (`bold`);<br>     - Dynamic column width layout with responsive horizontal scrolling (`ScrollArea::horizontal`);<br>   * End-to-end preservation in TSV export (`extract_item_tsv`) and HTML export (`procedures_to_report_document`), preserving inline CSS formatting for web export.<br>3. **Frequencies Styling Module &amp; Audit Report Table (`tables_frequencies::style_report`):**<br>   * Created modular leaf file `style_report.rs` (241 lines, $\le 500$ lines pursuant to `file-guard`), converting `FrequencyResult` to `ReportTable` and applying rules through `ConditionalFormattingEngine`;<br>   * When &quot;Create styles report&quot; (`create_style_report`) is enabled, the system automatically appends an auxiliary *«Conditional Styles Report»* audit table to Output Viewer:<br>     - Columns: *Table*, *Target*, *Condition*, *Format*, *Modified Cells Count*;<br>     - Accurately tallies all modified data cells across categories and summary totals.<br>4. **Canonical SPSS `OUTPUT MODIFY` Syntax Generation L5 (`statcraft_syntax`):**<br>   * Extended `to_sps_from_params` in `FREQUENCIES` command to generate authentic SPSS `OUTPUT MODIFY` syntax:<br>     - Selection targeting `/SELECT TABLES /IF SUBTYPES=[&#39;Frequencies&#39;]`;<br>     - Dimension and cell styling block `/TABLECELLS SELECT=[DIMENSION=...] CONDITION=... STYLE=[...]`;<br>     - Translation of logical operators (`EQ`, `NE`, `LT`, `LE`, `GT`, `GE`, `BETWEEN`, `SYSMIS`) and RGB color specifications `BACKGROUND=RGB(...) COLOR=RGB(...) FONTSTYLE=BOLD`.<br>5. **Zero-Hardcode i18n (`locales/ru.ftl`, `locales/en.ftl`):**<br>   * Registered 6 bilingual semantic localization keys (`dialog-style-report-title`, `dialog-style-report-col-table`, `dialog-style-report-col-target`, `dialog-style-report-col-condition`, `dialog-style-report-col-format`, `dialog-style-report-col-modified`).<br>6. **Testing &amp; End-to-End Verification (DoD):**<br>   * Developed end-to-end test suite `crates/statcraft_app/tests/table_style_e2e_test.rs` (5 tests):<br>     - `test_frequencies_with_table_style_rule`: verifies cell background styling and bold typography;<br>     - `test_create_style_report_generates_audit_table`: verifies audit table generation and modified cell counts;<br>     - `test_output_modify_syntax_paste_generation`: verifies SPSS `OUTPUT MODIFY` syntax generation;<br>     - `test_html_export_preserves_table_styles`: verifies inline CSS generation in exported HTML;<br>     - `test_headless_egui_render_with_styled_table`: headless egui context rendering without panics;<br>   * Added unit test `test_frequencies_sps_generation_with_table_styles` in `frequencies_cmd/tests.rs`;<br>   * 100% clean Quality Gate execution via `cargo run -p xtask -j 1 -- ci` (10/10 gates passed).</p><p>---</p><h3>Phase 112: 100% Visual and Structural SPSS Parity Alignment for Table Style</h3><p>*Time: November 24, 2026, 18:40 (~45 minutes)*</p><p>Following visual testing and audit of live IBM SPSS Statistics screenshots, conducted a comprehensive UI and structural remediation of the **Table Style (Feature 019: Table Style / Conditional Formatting)** dialog complex:<br>1. **Critical egui Layout Remediation:**<br>   * Resolved the horizontal layout bug that broke table row positioning: isolated the rules table inside a dedicated `ui.vertical(|ui| { ... })` container, ensuring the horizontal separator sits strictly below header columns and row contents stack vertically in natural order.<br>2. **Restoration of 5 Canonical Rule Columns:**<br>   * Removed artificial `№` sequence column;<br>   * Restored 5 authentic columns with native inline dropdowns (`ComboBox`) directly in table cells:<br>     1. `Table`: `ComboBox` (*All eligible tables, Frequencies, Statistics*);<br>     2. `Value`: `ComboBox` (*All data cells, Count (N), Mean, Median, Percent*);<br>     3. `Dimension`: `ComboBox` (*Columns, Rows, Columns and rows*);<br>     4. `Condition`: clickable cell opening the Condition subdialog;<br>     5. `Format`: clickable cell opening the Format subdialog;<br>   * Segmented the right actions column: `[ Add ]`, `[ Duplicate ]`, `[ Move Up ]`, `[ Move Down ]`, spacer, and `[ Delete ]` positioned at the lower boundary.<br>3. **Canonical &quot;Table Style :